1
00:00:04,240 --> 00:00:06,670
(The last round of Fact Land Grab)

2
00:00:07,040 --> 00:00:09,080
(Only two questions are left.)

3
00:00:09,780 --> 00:00:10,950
O.

4
00:00:12,250 --> 00:00:13,310
Correct.

5
00:00:13,310 --> 00:00:14,980
- Yes!
- Yes!

6
00:00:16,580 --> 00:00:18,620
- It's Busan.
- Skip the turn now.

7
00:00:18,620 --> 00:00:19,720
She can just skip the turn.

8
00:00:19,720 --> 00:00:20,820
- It's a tie.
- It's a tie.

9
00:00:20,820 --> 00:00:22,490
- Do we win if she answers it?
- Yes.

10
00:00:22,660 --> 00:00:24,630
(Only one question remains.)

11
00:00:31,430 --> 00:00:33,170
I choose C3.

12
00:00:33,170 --> 00:00:35,470
(According to
UN's Food and Agriculture Organization,)

13
00:00:35,470 --> 00:00:38,310
(coffee is the second most consumed
beverage in the world after water.)

14
00:00:38,310 --> 00:00:39,540
I don't think that's true.

15
00:00:39,540 --> 00:00:40,940
- I think it'd be tea.
- Coke.

16
00:00:40,940 --> 00:00:42,580
It might be coffee.

17
00:00:42,580 --> 00:00:43,610
You never know.

18
00:00:43,640 --> 00:00:45,050
- I have no idea.
- I think it's Coke.

19
00:00:45,050 --> 00:00:46,110
- It could be coffee.
- It's not Coke.

20
00:00:46,110 --> 00:00:47,780
- No?
- It's either tea or coffee,

21
00:00:47,780 --> 00:00:49,180
and I think it's coffee.

22
00:00:49,180 --> 00:00:52,290
(According to
UN's Food and Agriculture Organization,)

23
00:00:52,290 --> 00:00:56,720
(coffee is the second most consumed
beverage in the world after water.)

24
00:01:00,660 --> 00:01:01,730
O.

25
00:01:02,830 --> 00:01:04,500
- Let's go, the heart of a beast.
- Let's go!

26
00:01:04,500 --> 00:01:05,900
- The heart of a beast!
- Let's go!

27
00:01:05,900 --> 00:01:06,970
I think it's tea.

28
00:01:07,100 --> 00:01:08,400
My heart hurts.

29
00:01:11,640 --> 00:01:12,670
Incorrect.

30
00:01:22,820 --> 00:01:24,290
- Yes!
- We won!

31
00:01:24,290 --> 00:01:25,590
- What?
- Who won?

32
00:01:25,590 --> 00:01:26,620
Did he win?

33
00:01:26,620 --> 00:01:28,160
- This is unreal.
- A one-point difference.

34
00:01:28,160 --> 00:01:29,160
For real?

35
00:01:34,060 --> 00:01:35,500
(Groaning)

36
00:01:35,500 --> 00:01:36,500
That was tough.

37
00:01:36,560 --> 00:01:39,970
Round Three of Fact Land Grab is over.

38
00:01:39,970 --> 00:01:41,800
Here are the results.

39
00:01:42,340 --> 00:01:44,240
Team Gold, 24 points.

40
00:01:44,410 --> 00:01:46,270
Team White, 25 points.

41
00:01:46,270 --> 00:01:48,340
Team White won.

42
00:01:48,340 --> 00:01:49,380
Seriously.

43
00:02:02,460 --> 00:02:03,760
It was a real bummer.

44
00:02:03,760 --> 00:02:05,230
To lose by just one question.

45
00:02:05,530 --> 00:02:07,660
I had caught up so much.

46
00:02:07,830 --> 00:02:11,200
Had the alliance team not had the items,

47
00:02:11,330 --> 00:02:14,200
we would've definitely won.

48
00:02:14,400 --> 00:02:15,400
"Please get it wrong."

49
00:02:15,400 --> 00:02:17,870
"Please believe that it's coffee."

50
00:02:17,870 --> 00:02:20,910
I was shaking all over.

51
00:02:20,910 --> 00:02:23,580
I kept silently hoping
she'd get it wrong...

52
00:02:23,580 --> 00:02:25,510
and counting only the numbers
she got right.

53
00:02:25,680 --> 00:02:27,180
Solving the question was
the least of my concerns.

54
00:02:27,420 --> 00:02:28,880
"Win with your skills."

55
00:02:29,050 --> 00:02:32,350
"Just win,"
was what we talked about a lot.

56
00:02:32,450 --> 00:02:34,360
Skills weren't what helped me win today.

57
00:02:34,360 --> 00:02:36,360
I used two pricey weapons.

58
00:02:36,720 --> 00:02:38,060
I barely won by doing so.

59
00:02:38,390 --> 00:02:39,830
I couldn't be over the moon about it.

60
00:02:39,830 --> 00:02:41,660
Of course, winning the war was...

61
00:02:41,800 --> 00:02:43,930
great news for the team.

62
00:02:44,030 --> 00:02:45,570
But I'm still ashamed.

63
00:02:46,570 --> 00:02:50,300
(Episode 10: The Perfect Victory)

64
00:02:50,840 --> 00:02:53,410
The final result of Fact Land Grab.

65
00:02:53,510 --> 00:02:56,880
Having won 2 rounds out of the 3,

66
00:02:56,880 --> 00:02:59,650
- Team White has won the war.
- Thank you.

67
00:02:59,650 --> 00:03:00,950
- Thank you.
- Well done.

68
00:03:01,220 --> 00:03:03,120
It would've been sadder
had it been 2 to 0.

69
00:03:03,420 --> 00:03:05,290
The winning team...

70
00:03:05,450 --> 00:03:08,560
claims half
of the losing team's total assets...

71
00:03:08,560 --> 00:03:10,320
as spoils of war.

72
00:03:11,060 --> 00:03:13,830
The total spoils that
Team Gold must give to...

73
00:03:13,830 --> 00:03:17,030
Team White are as follows.

74
00:03:17,830 --> 00:03:21,200
Ninety-nine diamonds, eight lives,

75
00:03:21,200 --> 00:03:24,770
five credits, and seventy-five gold.

76
00:03:26,470 --> 00:03:28,080
They really didn't do anything.

77
00:03:28,940 --> 00:03:30,710
Teams White and Red,

78
00:03:30,710 --> 00:03:33,880
please discuss
how you would like to divide the spoils.

79
00:03:34,050 --> 00:03:36,550
The transfer of the spoils
will take place...

80
00:03:36,550 --> 00:03:39,090
at the Community Center shortly.

81
00:03:39,090 --> 00:03:43,090
Team Gold wasn't bluffing about
how many resources they had at all.

82
00:03:43,220 --> 00:03:46,860
From what I saw, Team Gold had
enough lives to survive until the end.

83
00:03:46,890 --> 00:03:50,060
That was what could've put them at ease.

84
00:03:50,200 --> 00:03:52,700
I felt a sense of disconnect there.

85
00:03:52,970 --> 00:03:55,140
After checking the amount of spoils,

86
00:03:55,440 --> 00:03:56,800
it became much clearer.

87
00:03:58,640 --> 00:04:02,210
The transfer of the spoils will now begin.

88
00:04:02,210 --> 00:04:03,950
(Transfer of the Spoils)

89
00:04:03,950 --> 00:04:06,880
The losing team is to check
the amount of spoils...

90
00:04:06,880 --> 00:04:09,580
and submit them in the central box.

91
00:04:23,970 --> 00:04:26,130
The winning team is
to collect the spoils...

92
00:04:26,130 --> 00:04:27,900
from the slot.

93
00:04:31,470 --> 00:04:34,080
(Team Red collects
all the credits and lives.)

94
00:04:38,510 --> 00:04:41,180
(Team White collects
all the diamonds and gold.)

95
00:04:45,250 --> 00:04:48,620
The spoils transfer has been completed.

96
00:04:52,490 --> 00:04:55,800
As of this moment,
the state of war has been lifted.

97
00:04:56,430 --> 00:04:59,470
The leader negotiation will now begin.

98
00:05:00,100 --> 00:05:03,140
First off,
here's the pollution index for...

99
00:05:03,140 --> 00:05:04,810
the entire Community Town.

100
00:05:05,240 --> 00:05:07,840
The total pollution index
accumulated over the past seven days...

101
00:05:07,840 --> 00:05:09,540
is 70.

102
00:05:10,340 --> 00:05:13,410
Please note that
once the pollution index reaches 100,

103
00:05:13,650 --> 00:05:15,280
the town will be considered saturated.

104
00:05:16,750 --> 00:05:19,320
Personally, I did want to experience...

105
00:05:19,320 --> 00:05:21,920
the pollution event.

106
00:05:21,920 --> 00:05:25,360
It's said to be deadly, so I wonder
how much danger it could cause.

107
00:05:25,930 --> 00:05:29,600
But I can't put the community at risk
just because of my curiosity.

108
00:05:29,700 --> 00:05:33,000
Even if we use up all the credits
currently available in the market,

109
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:35,000
we won't exceed the pollution limit.

110
00:05:36,140 --> 00:05:40,110
Here is the agenda for
the leader negotiation.

111
00:05:41,380 --> 00:05:42,840
The first agenda item is...

112
00:05:43,480 --> 00:05:45,380
the no-war treaty.

113
00:05:46,250 --> 00:05:48,450
(First agenda item: No-war treaty)

114
00:05:48,980 --> 00:05:50,450
As of today, Day Seven,

115
00:05:50,450 --> 00:05:54,560
two wars have broken out
within the Community Town,

116
00:05:54,820 --> 00:05:58,130
causing damage to several town members.

117
00:06:00,030 --> 00:06:02,660
If 3 of the 5 leaders agree,

118
00:06:03,060 --> 00:06:06,170
no further wars may be declared for
the remainder of the period.

119
00:06:10,500 --> 00:06:13,640
It'd be too selfish of me,
so I'm staying still.

120
00:06:14,980 --> 00:06:18,550
If there were no wars,
I'd be at a loss as the weapon dealer.

121
00:06:19,580 --> 00:06:24,950
This isn't something I could say
as someone who started a war.

122
00:06:24,950 --> 00:06:27,390
It will sound very hypocritical.

123
00:06:27,720 --> 00:06:29,390
The first war broke out...

124
00:06:29,390 --> 00:06:32,160
due to survival.

125
00:06:35,130 --> 00:06:36,760
The second war was also...

126
00:06:37,130 --> 00:06:39,400
(Team White declares war on...)

127
00:06:39,400 --> 00:06:40,940
(Team Gold.)

128
00:06:41,140 --> 00:06:43,740
Part of the reason was for survival.

129
00:06:44,810 --> 00:06:46,640
Our safety...

130
00:06:47,210 --> 00:06:49,780
wasn't guaranteed until the end.

131
00:06:50,040 --> 00:06:52,280
Who knows what kind of variables...

132
00:06:52,280 --> 00:06:55,820
there may be until the final goal,

133
00:06:56,450 --> 00:06:59,290
but I no longer want a war to survive.

134
00:06:59,290 --> 00:07:01,160
In Team Gold's shoes,

135
00:07:01,360 --> 00:07:03,190
you may think,

136
00:07:03,360 --> 00:07:06,230
"Didn't you declare war against us?"

137
00:07:06,230 --> 00:07:08,800
"Taking away the chance
to take your spoils is absurd."

138
00:07:10,230 --> 00:07:12,670
This is simply my opinion.
I can't tell what's right at the moment.

139
00:07:12,670 --> 00:07:15,700
I simply stated my opinion
after reading that agenda item.

140
00:07:16,270 --> 00:07:18,410
(Leia agrees with the no-war treaty.)

141
00:07:23,280 --> 00:07:24,780
What do you think, Reboot?

142
00:07:25,550 --> 00:07:27,820
I do see the need...

143
00:07:28,350 --> 00:07:30,680
for the no-war treaty,

144
00:07:31,320 --> 00:07:33,320
but is there really a need to...

145
00:07:33,320 --> 00:07:36,360
forcibly ban it by making it a treaty?

146
00:07:43,530 --> 00:07:45,830
(Reboot disagrees with the no-war treaty.)

147
00:07:46,570 --> 00:07:49,170
I understand the purpose of it.

148
00:07:49,270 --> 00:07:52,870
From where we stand, the other teams
can declare war and are justified.

149
00:07:53,170 --> 00:07:55,080
But since we joined later,

150
00:07:55,240 --> 00:07:57,240
we can't declare war even if we want to.

151
00:07:57,240 --> 00:07:58,880
In a way, it's like...

152
00:07:59,080 --> 00:08:02,720
the environmental regulations
by the big powers.

153
00:08:02,880 --> 00:08:03,920
But...

154
00:08:04,520 --> 00:08:05,990
you don't have enough for tomorrow.

155
00:08:07,120 --> 00:08:08,120
And I mean lives.

156
00:08:09,120 --> 00:08:10,420
We're not short of it.

157
00:08:10,890 --> 00:08:13,060
- What?
- You're not short of it?

158
00:08:13,260 --> 00:08:16,060
Don't you have 3 left
after submitting 5 today?

159
00:08:17,830 --> 00:08:18,870
Yes.

160
00:08:18,870 --> 00:08:19,870
(3 lives remain after submitting 5)

161
00:08:19,870 --> 00:08:21,670
Feel free to tell us your thoughts.

162
00:08:22,900 --> 00:08:26,810
Is Team Gold's opinion that
concluding the treaty isn't necessary?

163
00:08:27,480 --> 00:08:29,040
I see it as unnecessary.

164
00:08:32,050 --> 00:08:33,110
I'm...

165
00:08:34,380 --> 00:08:35,380
against it.

166
00:08:36,250 --> 00:08:37,250
What?

167
00:08:40,450 --> 00:08:43,460
I don't think there's a need
for the no-war treaty.

168
00:08:43,490 --> 00:08:45,990
It's totally fine
even if war breaks out tomorrow.

169
00:08:47,060 --> 00:08:48,930
As this is a survival show,

170
00:08:49,430 --> 00:08:51,970
our team will win
with an absolute winning method.

171
00:08:52,230 --> 00:08:54,070
I don't want to create any variables.

172
00:08:54,770 --> 00:08:57,970
I'm even thinking of
starting a war tomorrow.

173
00:08:58,270 --> 00:09:00,110
Hence, I'm against the no-war treaty.

174
00:09:01,180 --> 00:09:03,840
Those who are against the no-war treaty,

175
00:09:03,980 --> 00:09:05,650
please raise your hand.

176
00:09:05,980 --> 00:09:08,380
(3 teams are against the no-war treaty.)

177
00:09:08,880 --> 00:09:11,150
- We're done here.
- Okay, got it.

178
00:09:14,960 --> 00:09:17,760
Speaking on behalf of my team,

179
00:09:18,260 --> 00:09:22,400
although we haven't been here
for very long,

180
00:09:22,730 --> 00:09:25,630
before we can even think about
whether we can do well,

181
00:09:25,770 --> 00:09:27,330
we're faced with
a more fundamental question.

182
00:09:27,330 --> 00:09:29,340
Can we actually play the game?

183
00:09:29,640 --> 00:09:32,540
There was no Gold Rush
when we had just joined.

184
00:09:33,310 --> 00:09:36,710
You all even voted that gold
wasn't acceptable at the supermarket.

185
00:09:37,710 --> 00:09:41,680
What's more, you decided
not to sell any food to us.

186
00:09:43,180 --> 00:09:46,250
With that, the rest were reluctant
to trade with us.

187
00:09:46,490 --> 00:09:50,320
Distribution was almost nonexistent,
which made the game impossible to play.

188
00:09:50,890 --> 00:09:52,630
We joined...

189
00:09:52,630 --> 00:09:55,300
within relationships shaped by...

190
00:09:55,300 --> 00:09:57,830
vested interests among the others.

191
00:09:57,830 --> 00:10:01,240
The basic conditions for competition
should have been in place.

192
00:10:01,240 --> 00:10:05,810
Honestly, it was hard to see
how we could play the game...

193
00:10:05,810 --> 00:10:09,010
in a situation
where competition wasn't taking place.

194
00:10:09,110 --> 00:10:12,450
There obviously needs to be
a more forward-looking attitude.

195
00:10:12,880 --> 00:10:17,080
I dearly hoped you would eat today.

196
00:10:17,550 --> 00:10:19,220
It was a choice we made,

197
00:10:19,220 --> 00:10:22,260
so you're not entirely to blame.

198
00:10:22,460 --> 00:10:26,160
I've rarely gone without food
for this long.

199
00:10:26,530 --> 00:10:28,760
Honestly speaking, it is tough.

200
00:10:28,760 --> 00:10:30,700
But that's not what got me enraged.

201
00:10:30,830 --> 00:10:34,200
The part that made me think
things weren't right was...

202
00:10:34,270 --> 00:10:35,800
him telling the other teammates,

203
00:10:36,040 --> 00:10:38,510
"Buy gold, and I'm cutting off food."

204
00:10:38,710 --> 00:10:40,870
I feel that was very unjust.

205
00:10:40,870 --> 00:10:44,980
I didn't eat as a way of protesting.

206
00:10:45,410 --> 00:10:48,080
Are you planning to starve
tomorrow as well?

207
00:10:48,080 --> 00:10:49,550
That's something my team...

208
00:10:49,550 --> 00:10:50,850
- will decide.
- Of course.

209
00:10:50,850 --> 00:10:53,650
The supermarket is open,
and the food is free.

210
00:10:53,650 --> 00:10:55,520
Feel free to come and eat.

211
00:10:55,520 --> 00:10:56,990
Why the sudden change of heart?

212
00:10:56,990 --> 00:10:59,130
Since we brought it up yesterday,

213
00:10:59,130 --> 00:11:01,200
you could've come
with a light heart today.

214
00:11:01,400 --> 00:11:03,560
Here's what frustrated me the most.

215
00:11:03,960 --> 00:11:06,570
Team Gold begs the question...

216
00:11:06,570 --> 00:11:09,000
and isn't willing to communicate.

217
00:11:09,200 --> 00:11:11,610
That boosted the distrust I had.

218
00:11:11,870 --> 00:11:15,210
We concluded that
you weren't willing to talk to us.

219
00:11:15,210 --> 00:11:19,910
But asking us to make it
so that you can take part in the game?

220
00:11:20,010 --> 00:11:23,880
Personally, it's hard to understand.

221
00:11:23,880 --> 00:11:29,060
There was plenty of
space and time for us to talk,

222
00:11:29,290 --> 00:11:31,930
but the one who refused to communicate...

223
00:11:32,360 --> 00:11:34,060
wasn't us. It was Team Gold.

224
00:11:35,100 --> 00:11:38,970
Honestly, I wanted to agree to
the no-war treaty.

225
00:11:39,500 --> 00:11:43,840
That would help us feel at ease
for tomorrow...

226
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:48,910
and secure our victory more.

227
00:11:49,310 --> 00:11:52,550
But Team Gold said they didn't feel...

228
00:11:52,850 --> 00:11:56,320
they had a fair chance to play,

229
00:11:56,420 --> 00:11:59,790
that none of the teams
were being cooperative,

230
00:11:59,790 --> 00:12:01,960
and that the game had been structured
to prevent them...

231
00:12:01,960 --> 00:12:04,690
from participating
from the moment they joined.

232
00:12:05,060 --> 00:12:07,760
Team Gold had plenty of opportunities.

233
00:12:08,000 --> 00:12:10,760
It's a real shame
they couldn't seize them.

234
00:12:10,930 --> 00:12:15,040
The moment I heard that,
I wanted another war.

235
00:12:15,470 --> 00:12:17,740
There is definitely a difference in
perspective there as well.

236
00:12:17,740 --> 00:12:22,910
I believe we didn't give it our all
and didn't have the capability to do so.

237
00:12:22,910 --> 00:12:27,610
If we had circulated gold
and traded with each other,

238
00:12:27,610 --> 00:12:28,680
then asking,

239
00:12:28,820 --> 00:12:32,720
"Why are you being so passive?"
"Why are you so isolated?"

240
00:12:32,720 --> 00:12:36,090
would have been a fair
and understandable criticism.

241
00:12:36,090 --> 00:12:38,860
But they blocked that circulation
for two days.

242
00:12:38,860 --> 00:12:40,630
You can still find...

243
00:12:40,630 --> 00:12:43,960
plenty of examples today of people
using arguments...

244
00:12:43,960 --> 00:12:47,430
to defend their own interests
and preserve the vested interests...

245
00:12:47,570 --> 00:12:49,500
of the old system.

246
00:12:49,670 --> 00:12:52,440
Either way,
can we move on from this treaty?

247
00:12:52,440 --> 00:12:54,740
- No no-war treaty.
- Sure.

248
00:12:54,940 --> 00:12:56,940
We have disagreed on...

249
00:12:57,080 --> 00:12:59,150
the no-war treaty.

250
00:12:59,510 --> 00:13:01,580
Negotiation failed.

251
00:13:01,780 --> 00:13:03,780
War is not prohibited.

252
00:13:03,780 --> 00:13:05,050
(No-war treaty negotiation failed)

253
00:13:06,450 --> 00:13:10,490
Next is whether to provide aid
or impose sanctions.

254
00:13:11,130 --> 00:13:12,290
I have a question.

255
00:13:12,960 --> 00:13:15,200
Is food trading included in the sanctions?

256
00:13:17,160 --> 00:13:20,400
Food trading is not included in
the sanctions.

257
00:13:22,370 --> 00:13:24,470
Team Red wants to...

258
00:13:27,070 --> 00:13:30,580
sanction Team Gold
for resource trading tomorrow.

259
00:13:35,550 --> 00:13:38,190
Team Gold wanted to maintain war,

260
00:13:38,190 --> 00:13:41,020
meaning they wanted to keep
playing the game.

261
00:13:41,020 --> 00:13:42,790
Fine then. I'll do my best.

262
00:13:42,790 --> 00:13:44,760
To make Team Diamond win,

263
00:13:44,760 --> 00:13:48,130
I will use every means possible.

264
00:13:48,230 --> 00:13:50,830
As wars are allowed,
I want to impose a sanction.

265
00:13:50,830 --> 00:13:53,430
There was no reason to hold back
on the other things either.

266
00:13:53,430 --> 00:13:56,200
They could think,
"Aren't you making us play with..."

267
00:13:56,200 --> 00:13:58,140
"both hands and feet tied?"

268
00:13:58,140 --> 00:13:59,540
But we have two more days left.

269
00:13:59,710 --> 00:14:02,510
Nobody can imagine
what kind of variables could pop up.

270
00:14:02,510 --> 00:14:05,510
We should widen the gap
at this very moment.

271
00:14:07,010 --> 00:14:08,980
- I agree.
- I agree.

272
00:14:09,680 --> 00:14:11,050
I disagree.

273
00:14:11,950 --> 00:14:13,590
Shut everything down completely,

274
00:14:13,720 --> 00:14:16,720
and they might just be going through
a few days of trial and error...

275
00:14:16,720 --> 00:14:19,660
before they're actually ready
to make a move.

276
00:14:19,760 --> 00:14:21,930
"Don't close the final door."

277
00:14:22,060 --> 00:14:23,160
"Let's give them a chance."

278
00:14:23,360 --> 00:14:25,600
"We shouldn't ban them outright."

279
00:14:25,600 --> 00:14:26,830
I opposed it on those grounds.

280
00:14:26,830 --> 00:14:29,470
Just as court rulings include
a minority opinion,

281
00:14:29,540 --> 00:14:32,010
I wanted to make sure my position was
also on the record.

282
00:14:32,310 --> 00:14:34,310
The sanction has been imposed.

283
00:14:34,710 --> 00:14:39,280
Team Gold can't trade for a day tomorrow.

284
00:14:41,150 --> 00:14:43,720
It's true that I was taken aback.

285
00:14:43,850 --> 00:14:45,590
What I can't grasp even now is that...

286
00:14:45,850 --> 00:14:47,350
sanctions are imposed...

287
00:14:47,350 --> 00:14:49,490
when someone does something wrong
and a reason is given.

288
00:14:49,490 --> 00:14:51,660
But I did not hear any reasons.

289
00:14:51,660 --> 00:14:53,260
The vote still passed.

290
00:14:53,490 --> 00:14:55,160
Even with the way...

291
00:14:55,160 --> 00:14:56,860
this community's voting system
is structured,

292
00:14:56,960 --> 00:14:59,900
it still reveals how much power...

293
00:14:59,900 --> 00:15:03,000
the stronger players have
to push down those...

294
00:15:03,000 --> 00:15:06,440
who are newer or in a weaker position.

295
00:15:06,470 --> 00:15:09,010
I couldn't help but have
that somewhat bitter thought.

296
00:15:10,240 --> 00:15:12,110
All discussions have ended.

297
00:15:12,480 --> 00:15:15,720
We'll move on to today's life submission.

298
00:15:17,580 --> 00:15:19,820
(The one-person groups,
Blue and White, are eliminated.)

299
00:15:19,820 --> 00:15:22,590
(Day 7 Life Submission)

300
00:15:26,190 --> 00:15:29,460
(Everyone in Team Red survives Day 7.)

301
00:15:30,960 --> 00:15:32,530
Let's toughen up.

302
00:15:36,470 --> 00:15:38,440
Let's toughen up.

303
00:15:40,540 --> 00:15:42,740
Please check the contents
of the central box...

304
00:15:42,910 --> 00:15:45,280
and allocate the lives.

305
00:15:45,910 --> 00:15:47,350
(Day 7 Life Submission)

306
00:15:53,650 --> 00:15:57,120
(Reboot's life hasn't been submitted.)

307
00:15:57,120 --> 00:16:00,230
(Day 7 Life Submission:
Mokgye, Luna, Maetel, Ugong)

308
00:16:04,800 --> 00:16:08,740
The life was not submitted for
Reboot today.

309
00:16:09,270 --> 00:16:10,270
What?

310
00:16:10,270 --> 00:16:13,140
The resident whose life
was not submitted...

311
00:16:13,140 --> 00:16:15,480
must leave now.

312
00:16:15,910 --> 00:16:17,080
Why is he leaving?

313
00:16:17,410 --> 00:16:19,280
Why did he do that?

314
00:16:19,280 --> 00:16:21,650
Why is he making it hard for us?

315
00:16:22,250 --> 00:16:24,180
- Did you hear that?
- Did you just hear that?

316
00:16:25,350 --> 00:16:27,490
Why would he make a move like this?

317
00:16:28,690 --> 00:16:30,690
Does he want the four of us to survive
until tomorrow?

318
00:16:31,730 --> 00:16:33,690
Is there any meaning behind it?

319
00:16:34,800 --> 00:16:36,700
He should've fought until the last moment.

320
00:16:36,700 --> 00:16:38,700
Of course, it's for each of us to decide.

321
00:16:38,770 --> 00:16:41,170
No wonder he asked me
whether the leader would leave...

322
00:16:41,170 --> 00:16:43,440
if he didn't allocate one to the leader.

323
00:16:44,000 --> 00:16:46,510
(Reboot returns to the dormitory
after submitting the lives for Day 7.)

324
00:16:49,780 --> 00:16:52,110
I should still pass on the information.

325
00:16:52,680 --> 00:16:57,420
Honestly, I don't understand why...

326
00:16:57,820 --> 00:16:59,490
you made such a decision.

327
00:16:59,920 --> 00:17:01,660
I should pass on the information.

328
00:17:03,120 --> 00:17:05,760
I'll share the information and my opinion.

329
00:17:06,330 --> 00:17:08,160
I'll go call Ugong.

330
00:17:09,830 --> 00:17:13,530
I disagreed with the agenda item
to conclude a no-war treaty.

331
00:17:13,730 --> 00:17:15,300
Team Red disagreed.

332
00:17:15,300 --> 00:17:17,200
The leader disagreed with
the no-war treaty.

333
00:17:17,200 --> 00:17:18,610
So did Team Blue.

334
00:17:18,610 --> 00:17:20,240
In the end,
there will be no no-war treaty.

335
00:17:20,240 --> 00:17:22,680
In short, it was voted down.

336
00:17:22,680 --> 00:17:23,980
Did Team White agree to it?

337
00:17:23,980 --> 00:17:26,850
Team White did say that
it was necessary in a way.

338
00:17:26,850 --> 00:17:28,750
Of course, she felt bad about it.

339
00:17:28,750 --> 00:17:30,520
- Ultimately,
- Ultimately...

340
00:17:30,520 --> 00:17:31,690
let's not make a treaty banning it.

341
00:17:31,690 --> 00:17:33,150
It was voted down 2 to 3.

342
00:17:33,320 --> 00:17:34,790
After that,

343
00:17:35,020 --> 00:17:36,960
Team Red wanted to impose a sanction...

344
00:17:37,120 --> 00:17:40,030
when it came to providing aid
or imposing sanctions.

345
00:17:40,030 --> 00:17:41,560
He suggested imposing...

346
00:17:41,560 --> 00:17:44,060
a sanction
on Team Gold's trading tomorrow.

347
00:17:44,400 --> 00:17:46,230
That was agreed upon.

348
00:17:46,870 --> 00:17:49,270
But that's not just limited to
the supermarket.

349
00:17:49,270 --> 00:17:52,210
It includes everything tomorrow,
including the Platform trading.

350
00:17:52,210 --> 00:17:54,610
In short, the number of resources
won't change.

351
00:17:54,710 --> 00:17:58,880
From what I see, I think Team Red
did that to get back at me...

352
00:17:59,680 --> 00:18:00,950
out of some...

353
00:18:00,950 --> 00:18:03,080
- ill feelings.
- That's why he imposed a sanction?

354
00:18:03,080 --> 00:18:05,490
And so it was approved.

355
00:18:05,490 --> 00:18:06,620
By approved, you mean...

356
00:18:06,620 --> 00:18:08,190
- it passed, right?
- Yes, it passed.

357
00:18:08,190 --> 00:18:10,090
- Now...
- Can we not use our gold?

358
00:18:10,090 --> 00:18:13,590
We can't make any trades all day tomorrow.
It's a sanction.

359
00:18:13,590 --> 00:18:15,300
- Tomorrow's the last day.
- Yes, a sanction for tomorrow.

360
00:18:15,660 --> 00:18:18,030
It could be that Team Red...

361
00:18:18,170 --> 00:18:21,100
already had that in mind
and imposed it at a bad time.

362
00:18:21,300 --> 00:18:24,170
- It's just my opinion.
- Whatever the trigger was,

363
00:18:24,170 --> 00:18:27,270
- it doesn't matter.
- What matters is that it was approved.

364
00:18:27,270 --> 00:18:29,080
Yes, that's what matters.

365
00:18:29,080 --> 00:18:32,680
But the fact that it was brought about
right now is...

366
00:18:32,850 --> 00:18:34,580
- It's absurd.
- Yes, it's absurd.

367
00:18:34,580 --> 00:18:35,880
Tomorrow's game will be meaningless.

368
00:18:35,880 --> 00:18:38,450
If Team Red did it spontaneously,

369
00:18:38,750 --> 00:18:42,220
why did Teams Black and Blue agree
to impose a sanction on us?

370
00:18:42,220 --> 00:18:43,460
It leaves me with that question.

371
00:18:43,460 --> 00:18:45,560
They knew they'd win
and wanted to secure it.

372
00:18:45,560 --> 00:18:46,560
I'm not sure about that.

373
00:18:46,560 --> 00:18:48,800
I don't think this is right.

374
00:18:49,430 --> 00:18:50,500
What now?

375
00:18:54,840 --> 00:18:56,700
This is so wrong.

376
00:18:59,870 --> 00:19:02,080
This is so unfair
that I'm actually in tears.

377
00:19:05,110 --> 00:19:07,410
The way I see it,

378
00:19:07,410 --> 00:19:11,420
there's a possibility that
Team Red brought it up spontaneously.

379
00:19:11,420 --> 00:19:13,350
But I'm not too sure.

380
00:19:13,350 --> 00:19:16,220
I'm not sure what intentions he had
in bringing it up.

381
00:19:16,460 --> 00:19:18,430
I was quite shocked myself...

382
00:19:19,060 --> 00:19:20,460
after hearing the result.

383
00:19:20,890 --> 00:19:23,500
I couldn't stop it.
The decision was made by voting.

384
00:19:46,750 --> 00:19:48,120
I'm going to go cheer her up.

385
00:19:57,900 --> 00:19:59,030
Luna.

386
00:20:00,100 --> 00:20:02,770
It's okay. It's just a game.

387
00:20:02,970 --> 00:20:05,640
They're making the game so dirty.

388
00:20:05,640 --> 00:20:08,070
- Doing so...
- It's okay. It's just a game.

389
00:20:08,380 --> 00:20:10,540
A game should be played like one.

390
00:20:10,540 --> 00:20:13,280
What is this
if we're going to do things like this?

391
00:20:13,450 --> 00:20:15,720
Maybe we have to see this through
for something to come of it.

392
00:20:15,980 --> 00:20:18,950
- We have to hit rock bottom...
- They're nasty.

393
00:20:19,290 --> 00:20:22,920
I'm so angry that I'm in tears.

394
00:20:22,920 --> 00:20:24,460
It's okay.

395
00:20:25,560 --> 00:20:27,560
I'm so frustrated I'm in tears.

396
00:20:27,560 --> 00:20:30,160
More things in life will make you angry.
This is nothing.

397
00:20:30,500 --> 00:20:31,730
Cry if you want to.

398
00:20:32,100 --> 00:20:33,800
Crying might make you feel better.

399
00:20:35,870 --> 00:20:39,470
Our team couldn't even trade,
to begin with.

400
00:20:39,910 --> 00:20:42,840
The other teams weren't trading with us
on purpose.

401
00:20:43,040 --> 00:20:45,250
But was it necessary
to impose this sanction on us?

402
00:20:45,250 --> 00:20:47,210
I don't know what they were trying to do.

403
00:20:47,210 --> 00:20:48,650
Do they just want to fight?

404
00:20:48,650 --> 00:20:50,580
At this point, they just hate us.
It's personal.

405
00:20:54,590 --> 00:20:57,020
I'd like to say two things here.

406
00:20:57,020 --> 00:20:58,120
First,

407
00:20:58,830 --> 00:21:03,660
my actions here led
to certain situations unfolding.

408
00:21:04,560 --> 00:21:06,600
And you must have been hurt by them.

409
00:21:06,930 --> 00:21:09,040
I failed to see the consequences...

410
00:21:09,900 --> 00:21:11,170
of my actions,

411
00:21:11,640 --> 00:21:14,270
and I didn't do enough
to apologize for my actions.

412
00:21:15,180 --> 00:21:16,580
For that, I'm deeply sorry.

413
00:21:18,040 --> 00:21:20,110
I'm very sad to hear that you're leaving.

414
00:21:20,110 --> 00:21:22,750
A big part of me feels guilty too.

415
00:21:23,850 --> 00:21:25,020
First of all,

416
00:21:25,850 --> 00:21:28,890
I'm telling you this person-to-person.

417
00:21:30,020 --> 00:21:31,990
As for the second thing I want to say,

418
00:21:32,960 --> 00:21:34,490
if I'm being honest,

419
00:21:35,800 --> 00:21:38,770
your decision makes me think...

420
00:21:39,600 --> 00:21:41,870
that you're being irresponsible.

421
00:21:44,140 --> 00:21:45,710
We're a team.

422
00:21:45,940 --> 00:21:51,110
We were all trying our best
to survive here.

423
00:21:51,980 --> 00:21:54,180
But your departure only crushed our hopes.

424
00:21:55,880 --> 00:21:57,480
With your decision,

425
00:21:59,690 --> 00:22:02,190
you're robbing us even of our hopes now.

426
00:22:02,820 --> 00:22:05,130
On top of that, you're the leader.

427
00:22:05,990 --> 00:22:08,700
You're passing the buck,
which is an irresponsible act.

428
00:22:09,460 --> 00:22:12,800
There are winners and losers in games.
That's the nature.

429
00:22:13,030 --> 00:22:17,500
We might still end up as losers,
but we'd be losers who did their best.

430
00:22:18,440 --> 00:22:20,210
Of course, things look hopeless now.

431
00:22:20,810 --> 00:22:23,710
But we could have kept trying to the end.

432
00:22:23,740 --> 00:22:25,910
And some of us hadn't given up.

433
00:22:26,150 --> 00:22:28,980
Why are you making
the rest of us give up too?

434
00:22:30,750 --> 00:22:32,490
Anyway, I'm sorry.

435
00:22:33,090 --> 00:22:36,020
I'll give what you said
some serious thought.

436
00:22:37,060 --> 00:22:40,260
Before making this decision,
I thought long and hard about it.

437
00:22:40,630 --> 00:22:44,330
But from my point of view,

438
00:22:44,330 --> 00:22:47,470
there are basic principles
people should stick to.

439
00:22:47,700 --> 00:22:50,370
Anyway, there were some things...

440
00:22:51,140 --> 00:22:52,840
I wanted to address.

441
00:22:52,840 --> 00:22:56,210
And my sole focus was to bring them up,
to be honest.

442
00:22:56,440 --> 00:23:00,910
At the Leader Negotiation,
I felt like I hit a massive wall.

443
00:23:01,480 --> 00:23:05,490
According to the basic standards I have,
it was irrational.

444
00:23:05,690 --> 00:23:08,960
He was using food, which was
a basic necessity, for his own gain.

445
00:23:08,960 --> 00:23:11,390
Involving the basic element
of human survival...

446
00:23:11,730 --> 00:23:13,960
was something I personally
couldn't tolerate.

447
00:23:13,960 --> 00:23:16,630
I couldn't accept myself staying here...

448
00:23:16,630 --> 00:23:18,230
and playing the game.

449
00:23:18,470 --> 00:23:20,000
I want to apologize to you the most...

450
00:23:20,200 --> 00:23:22,170
for not staying here with you...

451
00:23:22,170 --> 00:23:25,070
and not giving you a heads-up.

452
00:23:25,070 --> 00:23:27,140
For that, I'm truly sorry.

453
00:23:27,140 --> 00:23:31,610
I'd like to ask you once again
to try to understand my decision.

454
00:23:32,580 --> 00:23:35,120
We lost, and we were running low on lives.

455
00:23:35,120 --> 00:23:37,250
If I had stayed, we would've had
only three left by tomorrow.

456
00:23:37,250 --> 00:23:38,690
We would've been okay
if we got more lives.

457
00:23:38,690 --> 00:23:41,250
But without new lives,
two of us would have to leave.

458
00:23:41,620 --> 00:23:44,490
So I decided to leave the game today.

459
00:23:44,690 --> 00:23:46,590
That way, the four of them...

460
00:23:46,590 --> 00:23:49,200
could survive to the end.
That was my wish.

461
00:23:49,460 --> 00:23:50,930
If someone had to leave,

462
00:23:50,930 --> 00:23:54,600
it made more sense for me
to take responsibility and leave the game.

463
00:23:55,340 --> 00:23:59,640
Reboot kept mentioning
problems with the system...

464
00:23:59,640 --> 00:24:04,180
and pointed out the flawed attitudes
of the other teams.

465
00:24:04,310 --> 00:24:06,650
As an act of protest,

466
00:24:07,480 --> 00:24:09,450
he decided to leave.

467
00:24:09,920 --> 00:24:13,850
I still wonder if that was
the only decision he could have made.

468
00:24:14,320 --> 00:24:15,860
I understand his decision.

469
00:24:15,860 --> 00:24:18,430
When it comes to this game,

470
00:24:18,430 --> 00:24:21,830
if it starts to diverge
from your core beliefs and principles...

471
00:24:22,000 --> 00:24:24,230
or crosses the line you can tolerate,

472
00:24:24,230 --> 00:24:27,370
although everyone might have
a different threshold...

473
00:24:27,370 --> 00:24:29,040
for where the line is,

474
00:24:29,040 --> 00:24:31,000
as long as
you no longer see this as right,

475
00:24:31,000 --> 00:24:33,170
it becomes a matter of freedom.

476
00:24:33,640 --> 00:24:36,140
When I heard what happened
during the Leader Negotiation...

477
00:24:36,140 --> 00:24:39,680
and what he tried to get across
to the other leaders,

478
00:24:39,680 --> 00:24:40,910
I could understand his decision even more.

479
00:24:41,050 --> 00:24:42,820
He didn't have to apologize to us.

480
00:24:43,620 --> 00:24:46,450
It looked like
he was trying to convey the message...

481
00:24:46,450 --> 00:24:48,920
that something was terribly wrong
about the system...

482
00:24:48,920 --> 00:24:52,430
by voluntarily dropping out of the game.

483
00:24:52,530 --> 00:24:54,430
I just wanted to respect his decision.

484
00:24:55,200 --> 00:24:59,370
I should get going now.
The announcement was made.

485
00:24:59,700 --> 00:25:01,730
The principles of market economy...

486
00:25:01,730 --> 00:25:05,070
are interlinked with the principles
of capitalism from our Constitution.

487
00:25:05,070 --> 00:25:07,540
It gives us freedom
and a system to thrive in.

488
00:25:07,540 --> 00:25:10,010
Our profits are maximized through trade.

489
00:25:10,010 --> 00:25:13,580
In the utilitarian sense,
everyone in the community can be happy.

490
00:25:13,580 --> 00:25:16,080
With that purpose,
this system was implemented in society.

491
00:25:16,080 --> 00:25:17,750
Over the years,
it's been modified and improved.

492
00:25:18,120 --> 00:25:20,950
Just as expected,
when information isn't transparent...

493
00:25:20,950 --> 00:25:23,760
and when people aren't
on an equal footing to compete,

494
00:25:23,760 --> 00:25:25,860
while allowing people's greed
to take over,

495
00:25:25,860 --> 00:25:26,960
our society would turn into chaos,

496
00:25:26,960 --> 00:25:29,130
resembling the concept,
"The war of all against all."

497
00:25:29,130 --> 00:25:31,700
We'd end up in a chaotic situation,
reverting back to a primitive society.

498
00:25:31,700 --> 00:25:34,370
In the end, power is the law...

499
00:25:34,370 --> 00:25:37,240
where brute force becomes justice
in this world.

500
00:25:37,240 --> 00:25:40,810
So I spent a lot of time
thinking about my decision.

501
00:25:47,150 --> 00:25:50,150
(Reboot)

502
00:25:52,250 --> 00:25:54,520
(Morning of Day 8)

503
00:25:54,650 --> 00:25:57,260
(Dormitory for Gold)

504
00:25:58,790 --> 00:26:02,560
(Dormitory for White)

505
00:26:07,270 --> 00:26:09,040
As soon as I woke up,

506
00:26:09,440 --> 00:26:12,340
I could only think of one solution.

507
00:26:12,570 --> 00:26:15,010
I wanted to talk to Team White...

508
00:26:15,010 --> 00:26:16,840
and risk my place in the game.

509
00:26:17,380 --> 00:26:22,180
I wanted to try to come up with a way
by giving more gold to Team White.

510
00:26:24,650 --> 00:26:25,690
They're not here.

511
00:26:28,660 --> 00:26:29,690
(Dormitory for Red)

512
00:26:29,690 --> 00:26:30,890
- Yes?
- Yes?

513
00:26:31,190 --> 00:26:33,360
- Hello. I see.
- Hello.

514
00:26:33,360 --> 00:26:35,660
- Is Leia here?
- Yes?

515
00:26:35,660 --> 00:26:36,660
Leia isn't here.

516
00:26:36,660 --> 00:26:37,800
- Really?
- Yes.

517
00:26:38,730 --> 00:26:39,730
Okay.

518
00:26:43,970 --> 00:26:46,170
(Leia is getting ready in the dorm.)

519
00:26:46,340 --> 00:26:47,440
I couldn't find her.

520
00:26:47,510 --> 00:26:48,940
- You couldn't find her?
- No.

521
00:26:48,940 --> 00:26:50,210
She wasn't in the center?

522
00:26:50,380 --> 00:26:52,510
- No. No one was in there.
- Okay.

523
00:26:53,380 --> 00:26:55,210
- Maybe she's just getting ready...
- Just during that time?

524
00:26:55,210 --> 00:26:56,950
- in the dorm?
- What?

525
00:26:57,320 --> 00:26:59,650
Anyway, Reboot...

526
00:26:59,720 --> 00:27:03,890
- was our leader up until yesterday.
- Okay.

527
00:27:03,890 --> 00:27:09,100
Now that our leader is gone,
we have to pick another leader.

528
00:27:09,100 --> 00:27:11,160
Halfway through yesterday,
the player who led the most...

529
00:27:11,160 --> 00:27:12,770
It was like a coup.

530
00:27:12,770 --> 00:27:14,970
Mokgye was leading our team.

531
00:27:14,970 --> 00:27:18,440
If you agree to appoint her as the leader,
raise your hands.

532
00:27:18,840 --> 00:27:19,970
I agree.

533
00:27:19,970 --> 00:27:22,110
Thank you. I'll do my best.

534
00:27:22,110 --> 00:27:23,210
(Mokgye becomes the leader on Day 8.)

535
00:27:23,210 --> 00:27:27,450
I tried to find Leia this morning.

536
00:27:27,550 --> 00:27:31,650
Leia didn't seem happy yesterday.

537
00:27:31,780 --> 00:27:35,620
Of course, we're competing here
for our personal gain.

538
00:27:35,620 --> 00:27:38,860
But we also need to consider
what's right for this community.

539
00:27:38,860 --> 00:27:40,590
That should be another agenda.

540
00:27:41,260 --> 00:27:46,630
And I'm sure this matter is
on Leia's mind.

541
00:27:47,070 --> 00:27:50,540
"Is this the right direction
of our community?"

542
00:27:50,640 --> 00:27:52,340
That's what I'm going to ask her first.

543
00:27:52,570 --> 00:27:55,780
Donkey will have to share his prize
with Vector.

544
00:27:56,080 --> 00:27:58,340
That way, Donkey can be...

545
00:27:58,340 --> 00:28:00,650
the last surviving member of White.

546
00:28:01,280 --> 00:28:04,420
We can accept Leia, Paul, and Siseon.
This is the best we can do.

547
00:28:04,420 --> 00:28:07,890
We can form a new team with them
and share the gains.

548
00:28:08,220 --> 00:28:10,020
Then just like yesterday,
they'll say that...

549
00:28:10,020 --> 00:28:12,890
we're not making any sacrifices
while they are.

550
00:28:12,890 --> 00:28:15,930
They'll say something like that.

551
00:28:15,930 --> 00:28:17,960
Then I'll say...

552
00:28:18,530 --> 00:28:21,770
I'm going to take responsibility.

553
00:28:22,000 --> 00:28:24,840
I'm going to tell her
that I won't submit a life for myself.

554
00:28:25,270 --> 00:28:26,370
My plan was...

555
00:28:26,770 --> 00:28:30,510
to have gold as the final resource
by ensuring...

556
00:28:30,810 --> 00:28:34,610
the alliance between White and Gold...

557
00:28:34,610 --> 00:28:35,880
through relocation.

558
00:28:35,980 --> 00:28:37,750
I thought we'd be able to...

559
00:28:37,750 --> 00:28:40,050
come to an agreement
by sacrificing my gains.

560
00:28:40,290 --> 00:28:43,390
- That's the only solution I have for now.
- That's...

561
00:28:43,920 --> 00:28:45,790
(They haven't returned to their team
after yesterday's war.)

562
00:28:45,790 --> 00:28:47,490
There's not an easy day here.

563
00:28:48,290 --> 00:28:50,500
They should've imposed a sanction
to prevent wars.

564
00:28:51,230 --> 00:28:53,800
But the players of Team Gold said...

565
00:28:53,800 --> 00:28:56,400
it wasn't fair to prevent any future wars.

566
00:28:56,400 --> 00:28:57,800
So the sanction to prevent wars...

567
00:28:59,070 --> 00:29:00,240
I really don't understand them.

568
00:29:00,240 --> 00:29:02,110
They should've imposed the sanction
to prevent any future wars.

569
00:29:02,610 --> 00:29:05,780
They should try to trade
through the Platform...

570
00:29:06,050 --> 00:29:09,280
No. Their leader told me
he wanted the option to start a war.

571
00:29:09,280 --> 00:29:10,380
That's why I stopped them
from doing any trades today.

572
00:29:11,520 --> 00:29:13,690
Then I really don't understand
their decision.

573
00:29:14,850 --> 00:29:17,990
- As long as war is still on the table,
- Okay.

574
00:29:17,990 --> 00:29:19,030
the risk can't be contained.

575
00:29:19,830 --> 00:29:22,900
Well, they'll probably want to start a war
after running the scenarios in their head.

576
00:29:27,900 --> 00:29:29,270
Shockingly enough,

577
00:29:30,340 --> 00:29:32,940
there will be another war today.

578
00:29:33,010 --> 00:29:35,610
Yesterday's war was about...

579
00:29:35,610 --> 00:29:38,880
checking their resources
and acquiring their lives.

580
00:29:38,880 --> 00:29:40,610
That's why we started the war.

581
00:29:40,680 --> 00:29:44,550
As for today,
we already divided up the diamonds.

582
00:29:44,550 --> 00:29:46,990
But if they start the war,

583
00:29:46,990 --> 00:29:48,790
we'll end up losing a lot of the diamonds.

584
00:29:48,790 --> 00:29:51,590
They might not start it.

585
00:29:51,590 --> 00:29:53,960
But if we rely on that possibility,

586
00:29:54,630 --> 00:29:56,700
there's a risk of an uneven distribution.

587
00:29:56,830 --> 00:30:00,200
The only reason behind our alliance is...

588
00:30:00,600 --> 00:30:02,940
that the eight of us will end up...

589
00:30:02,940 --> 00:30:04,940
with the same amount of money
as our prize.

590
00:30:05,170 --> 00:30:06,910
If Team Gold...

591
00:30:07,270 --> 00:30:11,310
were to come after one of our teams,

592
00:30:11,780 --> 00:30:14,280
one of us would end up with less money.

593
00:30:14,280 --> 00:30:16,780
To prevent that,
we have to start the war first.

594
00:30:16,850 --> 00:30:20,650
By now, they know that
they don't stand a chance. Right?

595
00:30:20,650 --> 00:30:22,020
- That's why they brought up...
- It's really over now.

596
00:30:22,020 --> 00:30:23,990
- Right. I...
- It's really over.

597
00:30:23,990 --> 00:30:25,660
I'll be honest.

598
00:30:25,760 --> 00:30:27,730
Starting another war with them...

599
00:30:27,730 --> 00:30:29,830
would be crossing the line.

600
00:30:30,400 --> 00:30:33,630
After listening to
the leader of Team Gold earlier,

601
00:30:33,630 --> 00:30:34,800
I've changed my mind.

602
00:30:35,170 --> 00:30:37,440
I do see the need for the no-war treaty,

603
00:30:37,440 --> 00:30:39,240
but is there really a need to...

604
00:30:39,240 --> 00:30:41,010
forcibly ban it by making it a treaty?

605
00:30:41,070 --> 00:30:44,510
Just like we did today, we'll hit them
first by starting another war.

606
00:30:44,980 --> 00:30:46,250
We'll kill them all,

607
00:30:46,510 --> 00:30:48,410
so Team Gold has zero chance of winning.

608
00:30:48,410 --> 00:30:51,450
I'll go with the plan
that will guarantee our team's victory.

609
00:30:51,780 --> 00:30:52,890
I'll hit them with the bomb...

610
00:30:53,120 --> 00:30:54,520
before the war.

611
00:30:54,590 --> 00:30:57,220
I won't leave anything to chance.

612
00:30:57,220 --> 00:30:58,520
It will be a total victory.

613
00:31:03,260 --> 00:31:06,300
To make sure
we don't lose anything from the war,

614
00:31:06,700 --> 00:31:11,470
we have to move all the diamonds
from Blue to Red.

615
00:31:11,470 --> 00:31:12,970
Then Blue has to start the war.

616
00:31:12,970 --> 00:31:16,080
As for the share of the diamonds,

617
00:31:16,080 --> 00:31:19,150
we can return them to her through aid
after the war.

618
00:31:19,150 --> 00:31:21,310
Everyone will end up
with the same number of diamonds.

619
00:31:21,310 --> 00:31:23,380
Starting this war is
absolutely necessary to us.

620
00:31:23,580 --> 00:31:25,350
They said
they wanted the option to start wars.

621
00:31:25,350 --> 00:31:26,350
Yes.

622
00:31:26,350 --> 00:31:28,890
I thought, "Really? They want to have
another war on the last day too?"

623
00:31:28,890 --> 00:31:31,290
"All right.
I'll cripple one of your hands."

624
00:31:31,290 --> 00:31:33,260
That's why I imposed the sanction on them.

625
00:31:34,030 --> 00:31:35,190
Okay.

626
00:31:35,960 --> 00:31:37,730
Why is Luna with Team White?

627
00:31:38,360 --> 00:31:40,730
- That's what we need to talk about.
- Really?

628
00:31:40,830 --> 00:31:42,740
- Leia...
- Yes.

629
00:31:42,870 --> 00:31:44,470
and I...

630
00:31:44,470 --> 00:31:45,940
That's what you guys want?

631
00:31:45,940 --> 00:31:49,480
I think she's really sorry
about how things panned out.

632
00:31:49,480 --> 00:31:51,580
Considering everything,

633
00:31:51,680 --> 00:31:53,810
we want to persuade Luna to join us.

634
00:31:53,810 --> 00:31:58,180
We want to end on a good note together
as players of Team White.

635
00:31:59,320 --> 00:32:01,850
Actually, the game is over.

636
00:32:01,920 --> 00:32:03,860
There's nothing Team Gold can do now.

637
00:32:03,920 --> 00:32:05,930
A lot of things already happened...

638
00:32:06,090 --> 00:32:07,660
at yesterday's Leader Negotiation.

639
00:32:07,660 --> 00:32:09,400
We practically cut off their limbs.

640
00:32:09,630 --> 00:32:12,900
We thought if that was the case,
we should bring back Luna.

641
00:32:12,900 --> 00:32:15,530
Team Gold won't have any lives left
after tonight.

642
00:32:15,530 --> 00:32:17,240
So I spent a lot of time...

643
00:32:17,240 --> 00:32:19,670
trying to convince Red
so they'd agree to our plan to bring Luna.

644
00:32:19,910 --> 00:32:21,570
If everything goes well...

645
00:32:21,570 --> 00:32:24,110
and she were to split the gains with us,

646
00:32:24,280 --> 00:32:27,210
we wouldn't have to change
the number of diamonds you guys take.

647
00:32:27,210 --> 00:32:28,780
- You guys would split your gains?
- We're going to split...

648
00:32:28,780 --> 00:32:30,520
- our gains with her.
- You'll do that?

649
00:32:30,720 --> 00:32:32,820
That's how deeply you care about Luna.

650
00:32:32,820 --> 00:32:34,620
- Right.
- That's how we felt.

651
00:32:35,960 --> 00:32:39,030
Then, regarding this matter,
let me talk to her first...

652
00:32:39,030 --> 00:32:40,760
- before today's productive activities.
- Okay.

653
00:32:40,790 --> 00:32:42,630
- And we'll update you right away.
- Okay.

654
00:32:42,760 --> 00:32:44,700
- Her opinion is also important.
- Yes.

655
00:32:44,760 --> 00:32:46,570
- You won't do the quizzes today?
- No.

656
00:32:46,770 --> 00:32:48,470
- Okay.
- All right.

657
00:32:48,570 --> 00:32:50,870
I'll request for relocation now.

658
00:32:50,870 --> 00:32:53,140
- We have to relocate to Blue.
- To Blue.

659
00:32:53,140 --> 00:32:54,270
- Blue.
- For that.

660
00:32:54,270 --> 00:32:55,540
- Just for that.
- Let's do our best.

661
00:32:55,610 --> 00:32:57,680
You guys have to follow the plan, though.

662
00:32:57,910 --> 00:32:59,750
Use six credits for the bidding.

663
00:32:59,750 --> 00:33:00,810
- Pitou has to do it, right?
- Yes.

664
00:33:00,810 --> 00:33:02,720
Use one to start the quizzes.

665
00:33:02,720 --> 00:33:04,150
- Two hints. Okay.
- Two credits for the hints.

666
00:33:04,150 --> 00:33:06,120
- We must have 11 credits at the end.
- Okay.

667
00:33:06,120 --> 00:33:07,150
- We just need to use two.
- Without them,

668
00:33:07,150 --> 00:33:08,420
we can't hit them with the bomb.

669
00:33:08,420 --> 00:33:10,520
(Hints: 2, Bidding: 6,
Ticket: 1, Bomb: 10)

670
00:33:14,990 --> 00:33:18,260
Today's production activity
will begin shortly.

671
00:33:18,360 --> 00:33:21,630
There's ongoing resource depletion
within the Community Town.

672
00:33:22,230 --> 00:33:25,570
Only one production site is open
for production.

673
00:33:25,710 --> 00:33:30,080
The bidding for this one production site
will begin now.

674
00:33:30,410 --> 00:33:32,380
- We'll bid six.
- Okay.

675
00:33:32,380 --> 00:33:33,410
Relocate quickly.

676
00:33:33,410 --> 00:33:35,480
- Let's relocate quickly.
- Okay.

677
00:33:35,480 --> 00:33:38,280
Blue has to go down to make a bid.

678
00:33:44,120 --> 00:33:46,130
I'd like to relocate to Team White.

679
00:33:46,130 --> 00:33:48,130
Okay. I'll accept the request.

680
00:33:48,190 --> 00:33:50,060
I'd like to relocate to Team Blue.

681
00:33:50,060 --> 00:33:51,300
I'd like to relocate to Team Blue.

682
00:33:51,300 --> 00:33:53,900
I'd like to relocate to Team Blue
and produce a lot of lives.

683
00:33:54,670 --> 00:33:56,000
Okay.

684
00:33:56,000 --> 00:33:57,570
(Donkey, Izaha, and Siseon
relocate to Team Blue.)

685
00:33:58,540 --> 00:34:01,510
I need to bring some credits with me.

686
00:34:02,170 --> 00:34:04,640
What about us?
Should we bid for the production site?

687
00:34:04,810 --> 00:34:07,110
- Let's talk to them about that.
- Okay.

688
00:34:07,110 --> 00:34:09,720
- Let's ask them why they need more lives.
- Let's ask them.

689
00:34:09,720 --> 00:34:12,320
We can only decide
if we should participate in...

690
00:34:12,320 --> 00:34:15,550
the production activity today or not...

691
00:34:15,550 --> 00:34:16,560
- after talking to them first.
- But...

692
00:34:16,560 --> 00:34:19,930
so many people have already relocated
to Blue for the production activity.

693
00:34:19,930 --> 00:34:22,700
- It means they're highly motivated.
- It means they will do it.

694
00:34:22,700 --> 00:34:25,730
Anyway, we should let them know
that we need lives too.

695
00:34:25,730 --> 00:34:29,240
No, they think that we don't need lives
when it's just us.

696
00:34:29,340 --> 00:34:30,540
We have four lives.

697
00:34:30,540 --> 00:34:31,970
- Right. We don't need any lives.
- Right.

698
00:34:31,970 --> 00:34:33,110
- I'm sorry.
- Okay.

699
00:34:33,110 --> 00:34:34,640
"Why do you want to get more lives?"

700
00:34:34,640 --> 00:34:36,440
- They might feel that way.
- That's possible.

701
00:34:36,440 --> 00:34:38,410
"We'll go in, so you shouldn't."
If we say that,

702
00:34:38,410 --> 00:34:40,980
- they might not understand us.
- We don't need to get more lives.

703
00:34:40,980 --> 00:34:43,750
We don't have any leverage to use
when it comes to bidding.

704
00:34:43,820 --> 00:34:46,420
Should I relocate to Blue
and solve the quizzes with them?

705
00:34:46,450 --> 00:34:48,520
- Why?
- To get more lives.

706
00:34:48,520 --> 00:34:50,020
What if it becomes
an integrated community?

707
00:34:50,220 --> 00:34:51,390
- Is that pointless?
- No.

708
00:34:51,390 --> 00:34:55,830
Their alliance hasn't changed yet.

709
00:34:55,830 --> 00:34:57,930
- But...
- It's an interesting offer.

710
00:34:58,330 --> 00:35:00,170
- Should we try that?
- There's a possibility...

711
00:35:00,170 --> 00:35:02,540
that she might not come back
after relocating.

712
00:35:02,570 --> 00:35:03,840
- So...
- Why wouldn't I come back?

713
00:35:04,170 --> 00:35:05,600
- I see.
- To get the prize?

714
00:35:05,600 --> 00:35:06,810
But that's...

715
00:35:06,810 --> 00:35:09,510
Here's the thing. It's over for us.

716
00:35:09,640 --> 00:35:12,310
There's no way of staying here.

717
00:35:12,340 --> 00:35:13,580
- So...
- They won't let us in...

718
00:35:13,580 --> 00:35:14,910
- They won't.
- given the current situation.

719
00:35:14,910 --> 00:35:16,520
That's the point.

720
00:35:16,580 --> 00:35:17,850
We already lost,

721
00:35:17,850 --> 00:35:19,650
- and asking them to take us now...
- Exactly.

722
00:35:19,650 --> 00:35:21,920
- That's why we don't need to do that.
- Yes.

723
00:35:21,920 --> 00:35:23,760
- We don't need to get more lives.
- But...

724
00:35:23,760 --> 00:35:26,290
When she said it,
she wasn't trying to make a point.

725
00:35:26,290 --> 00:35:28,660
She just meant to say
she wanted to play games before leaving.

726
00:35:28,660 --> 00:35:30,260
- That was her point.
- I have no airtime now.

727
00:35:30,260 --> 00:35:32,100
Why don't you go and ask them?

728
00:35:32,230 --> 00:35:35,330
- We need to show them we changed too.
- But...

729
00:35:35,330 --> 00:35:37,140
we're too late to change.

730
00:35:37,140 --> 00:35:38,970
- That's what they're saying.
- But...

731
00:35:39,000 --> 00:35:40,240
- You know what?
- Yes.

732
00:35:40,240 --> 00:35:41,970
Let's not just stay here like before.

733
00:35:41,970 --> 00:35:43,640
- Let's go out.
- Let's please go out.

734
00:35:43,640 --> 00:35:45,210
- Let's go and face them.
- But...

735
00:35:45,210 --> 00:35:47,480
(Away)

736
00:35:47,480 --> 00:35:49,520
- Good morning.
- Hello.

737
00:35:51,820 --> 00:35:53,350
Are you going to use this?

738
00:35:54,190 --> 00:35:55,350
Today.

739
00:35:55,820 --> 00:35:59,090
- I'll give it to you as soon as I open.
- Okay.

740
00:35:59,990 --> 00:36:01,230
No? Right.

741
00:36:01,630 --> 00:36:03,000
- Hello.
- There's no mercy.

742
00:36:03,000 --> 00:36:05,200
- Hello.
- Good morning.

743
00:36:06,070 --> 00:36:07,670
Are you here to make a bid?

744
00:36:07,670 --> 00:36:09,670
Well, there's only one production site.

745
00:36:09,670 --> 00:36:11,900
You're going there. So there's no point.

746
00:36:11,900 --> 00:36:14,310
- We came down to talk.
- That's great.

747
00:36:14,310 --> 00:36:15,880
- Just to talk.
- The weather is great today.

748
00:36:15,910 --> 00:36:17,210
- A clear day after a rainy day.
- Right.

749
00:36:17,280 --> 00:36:19,040
How many of you are going? Four?

750
00:36:19,040 --> 00:36:21,250
- Is it just you guys?
- Yes, the four of us are going.

751
00:36:21,350 --> 00:36:22,480
- Should we get going?
- We...

752
00:36:22,480 --> 00:36:25,220
Right. We need to get going.
We have about five minutes left.

753
00:36:25,320 --> 00:36:26,420
How many...

754
00:36:26,620 --> 00:36:28,520
- I think we can just bid one.
- Let's play it safe.

755
00:36:28,720 --> 00:36:31,790
If they're not going to bid,
I think we can just bid one.

756
00:36:31,890 --> 00:36:33,060
But let's play it safe.

757
00:36:33,060 --> 00:36:34,890
We can't risk any damage
in case they bid at the last minute.

758
00:36:36,260 --> 00:36:38,430
Then let's wait in front of the door.

759
00:36:39,060 --> 00:36:40,130
- Should we?
- Yes.

760
00:36:40,130 --> 00:36:42,400
- I don't want to waste the credits.
- Sure.

761
00:36:43,170 --> 00:36:45,670
Can we join you
just to participate in the quizzes?

762
00:36:45,700 --> 00:36:47,470
You should've relocated.

763
00:36:47,470 --> 00:36:48,510
Is it not allowed now?

764
00:36:48,510 --> 00:36:50,210
- I thought we could do it anytime.
- We can do that now, can't we?

765
00:36:50,210 --> 00:36:51,540
- We don't have much time left.
- Right.

766
00:36:51,540 --> 00:36:53,310
- We're running out of time.
- That's...

767
00:36:53,450 --> 00:36:55,180
Well, I just want to join you...

768
00:36:55,180 --> 00:36:56,650
- and solve the quizzes with you.
- Right.

769
00:36:56,650 --> 00:36:58,180
- I won't even pack.
- I see.

770
00:36:59,990 --> 00:37:01,550
- How many minutes do we have left?
- I guess time's up.

771
00:37:01,590 --> 00:37:02,920
I guess it's about to end now.

772
00:37:03,490 --> 00:37:06,230
There are three minutes left
to bid on the production site.

773
00:37:06,260 --> 00:37:08,290
- She needs to bid first.
- Should I ask her?

774
00:37:08,290 --> 00:37:09,460
- Blue.
- Yes?

775
00:37:09,460 --> 00:37:12,970
Can I just join you for the quizzes
and leave right away?

776
00:37:12,970 --> 00:37:14,530
I won't even pack.

777
00:37:14,530 --> 00:37:15,940
I'm really going to leave...

778
00:37:15,940 --> 00:37:17,470
- after that.
- She just wants to solve the quizzes.

779
00:37:17,470 --> 00:37:19,140
I'm a bit worried, though.

780
00:37:19,140 --> 00:37:20,870
By the way, that's my thing.
I'm a worrywart.

781
00:37:21,940 --> 00:37:23,480
I'm worried that you might not leave.

782
00:37:25,410 --> 00:37:26,950
- Let me make a bid.
- Let's do that first.

783
00:37:26,950 --> 00:37:28,310
- Go ahead.
- Okay.

784
00:37:29,010 --> 00:37:31,020
- I'll just bid one.
- Okay. I'll stay here.

785
00:37:32,590 --> 00:37:34,550
If you want to bid on a production site,

786
00:37:34,550 --> 00:37:36,460
tell me the color of your team...

787
00:37:36,560 --> 00:37:39,760
and submit the credits in the central box.

788
00:37:43,160 --> 00:37:44,960
Please wait a bit.

789
00:37:45,800 --> 00:37:47,330
I haven't made up my mind yet...

790
00:37:47,700 --> 00:37:49,070
on how many I should bid.

791
00:37:59,280 --> 00:38:00,650
Blue.

792
00:38:00,650 --> 00:38:01,810
(Team Blue submits 1 credit.)

793
00:38:03,080 --> 00:38:04,180
(Blue didn't use 6 credits,
which was the plan.)

794
00:38:04,180 --> 00:38:06,990
Bidding for the production site
has closed.

795
00:38:07,090 --> 00:38:11,290
Team Blue has won the bidding
for the production site.

796
00:38:11,990 --> 00:38:13,390
- It's done.
- Good.

797
00:38:13,690 --> 00:38:15,030
- Time's up, right?
- Yes.

798
00:38:15,030 --> 00:38:16,060
- Yes.
- Great.

799
00:38:16,060 --> 00:38:18,560
- I was in there until time ran out.
- Right. I thought so.

800
00:38:18,560 --> 00:38:20,430
- I stalled for 20 seconds.
- Great job.

801
00:38:21,170 --> 00:38:24,200
The production activity for Day Eight
has begun.

802
00:38:24,700 --> 00:38:26,410
- Blue is going?
- Yes.

803
00:38:26,870 --> 00:38:28,070
How many did you bid?

804
00:38:28,070 --> 00:38:29,110
- One.
- One.

805
00:38:29,110 --> 00:38:30,840
- Get four hints.
- Okay.

806
00:38:30,840 --> 00:38:32,310
- You did the right thing by saving them.
- Yes.

807
00:38:32,310 --> 00:38:34,580
Whenever he tells us to do something,

808
00:38:34,650 --> 00:38:35,950
- I just say, "Yes, sir."
- "Yes, sir."

809
00:38:36,250 --> 00:38:38,720
- I just know he knows what he's doing.
- I'm sure he has a good reason for it.

810
00:38:38,780 --> 00:38:39,820
- Right.
- We'll be back.

811
00:38:39,820 --> 00:38:41,320
- We'll be back.
- Okay.

812
00:38:43,320 --> 00:38:44,490
Hello.

813
00:38:46,260 --> 00:38:47,260
- We'll be back.
- I...

814
00:38:47,260 --> 00:38:48,960
- Make a lot of money.
- Okay.

815
00:38:49,400 --> 00:38:51,000
Izaha!

816
00:38:51,560 --> 00:38:53,300
- He needs a minute.
- Wait.

817
00:38:53,370 --> 00:38:54,470
Yes?

818
00:38:54,600 --> 00:38:56,370
Use up to four.

819
00:38:56,370 --> 00:38:59,340
If you can solve it with one credit,
then use it.

820
00:38:59,340 --> 00:39:00,340
If we're completely sure,

821
00:39:00,340 --> 00:39:01,610
- we can use one more?
- Yes.

822
00:39:01,610 --> 00:39:02,810
- Okay.
- Okay.

823
00:39:03,940 --> 00:39:07,080
(Team Production is
strictly following Maillard's order.)

824
00:39:07,850 --> 00:39:08,850
Good.

825
00:39:09,780 --> 00:39:10,920
What should we do?

826
00:39:13,350 --> 00:39:15,120
I wonder what Gold is doing.

827
00:39:16,460 --> 00:39:19,090
Why did they not bid
on the production site?

828
00:39:19,120 --> 00:39:21,230
- The bidding?
- It'd be their loss.

829
00:39:21,230 --> 00:39:22,930
- Because they can't win the bidding?
- Right.

830
00:39:22,930 --> 00:39:25,660
They might have thought that
holding onto the credits would be better.

831
00:39:27,000 --> 00:39:28,100
My gosh.

832
00:39:34,070 --> 00:39:35,910
There will be a war today. Right?

833
00:39:36,110 --> 00:39:40,080
Starting a war today will guarantee
our win.

834
00:39:40,610 --> 00:39:43,280
Hitting them with the bomb
might trigger them...

835
00:39:43,280 --> 00:39:45,120
to start the war.

836
00:39:45,350 --> 00:39:47,420
- So we're striking first.
- Right.

837
00:39:47,420 --> 00:39:48,850
It's like a warning shot...

838
00:39:49,190 --> 00:39:50,290
before the war.

839
00:39:51,290 --> 00:39:52,690
We'll have to hit them with the bomb.

840
00:39:52,690 --> 00:39:53,890
We have no choice.

841
00:39:54,790 --> 00:39:57,900
It doesn't matter whether or not
Team Gold ends up with 1 or 0.

842
00:39:58,100 --> 00:40:00,200
The rest of them will have to leave
except for one.

843
00:40:00,200 --> 00:40:01,700
If they win the war,
they can take our lives.

844
00:40:01,970 --> 00:40:03,240
What if Blue loses?

845
00:40:03,240 --> 00:40:04,670
- If she were to start the war,
- Okay.

846
00:40:04,670 --> 00:40:06,570
she needs to have four with her.

847
00:40:06,610 --> 00:40:08,640
In case she loses, she needs to have two.

848
00:40:08,670 --> 00:40:11,180
That way, she uses one tonight
and uses the other one...

849
00:40:11,180 --> 00:40:12,510
during the vote tomorrow.

850
00:40:13,810 --> 00:40:15,050
Without wasting...

851
00:40:15,050 --> 00:40:16,220
(They can hear Team Production's cheering
from the hub.)

852
00:40:16,220 --> 00:40:17,280
They're going wild.

853
00:40:17,680 --> 00:40:18,750
I guess they got it right.

854
00:40:18,750 --> 00:40:19,820
They're so noisy.

855
00:40:21,020 --> 00:40:22,050
- They're clapping.
- They're clapping.

856
00:40:22,050 --> 00:40:23,290
I guess they're doing well today.

857
00:40:23,290 --> 00:40:24,420
They at least got two lives.

858
00:40:24,460 --> 00:40:25,590
That is correct.

859
00:40:25,590 --> 00:40:26,760
(Correct)

860
00:40:26,990 --> 00:40:28,030
- Wait.
- That's amazing.

861
00:40:28,030 --> 00:40:30,060
- Siseon, that's so sexy.
- I knew it, Siseon!

862
00:40:30,060 --> 00:40:31,160
- That's really sexy.
- We...

863
00:40:31,160 --> 00:40:32,800
could never have guessed that right.

864
00:40:32,800 --> 00:40:35,530
- Right. Only he could've gotten it right.
- It's my first time hearing it.

865
00:40:35,730 --> 00:40:37,340
- It's my first time hearing it.
- My field of study...

866
00:40:37,340 --> 00:40:39,170
- finally came up.
- No one could've gotten it but him.

867
00:40:39,170 --> 00:40:40,510
- Gosh, at last.
- This was...

868
00:40:40,510 --> 00:40:41,840
tailored for Siseon.

869
00:40:42,540 --> 00:40:44,680
I think having more resources...

870
00:40:44,810 --> 00:40:46,450
will definitely be an advantage.

871
00:40:46,450 --> 00:40:49,010
- Right.
- We fought over resources from the start.

872
00:40:49,010 --> 00:40:50,080
Exactly.

873
00:40:51,020 --> 00:40:52,250
What's Team Gold dong?

874
00:40:52,680 --> 00:40:54,420
- We barely got to talk.
- Right.

875
00:40:54,420 --> 00:40:56,790
- The game is nearing its end now.
- Right.

876
00:40:56,860 --> 00:40:59,960
There were some things
we wanted to tell you.

877
00:41:00,290 --> 00:41:02,930
We were informed about the agenda
from yesterday's negotiation...

878
00:41:02,930 --> 00:41:04,660
right before he left.

879
00:41:04,660 --> 00:41:05,700
He told you about them, right?

880
00:41:05,700 --> 00:41:08,170
He did tell us about the agenda
from yesterday...

881
00:41:08,170 --> 00:41:10,870
- and how the votes went.
- Okay.

882
00:41:11,700 --> 00:41:13,810
There was a bit of complacency.

883
00:41:13,810 --> 00:41:15,140
- It sounded like...
- It's like...

884
00:41:15,140 --> 00:41:17,640
wanting to go to war was our main opinion.

885
00:41:17,640 --> 00:41:19,310
- As talks progressed like that,
- That was the misunderstanding.

886
00:41:19,310 --> 00:41:20,450
that misunderstanding piled up...

887
00:41:20,450 --> 00:41:23,020
- to end up like this.
- We've never had those talks,

888
00:41:23,280 --> 00:41:24,580
but we ended up...

889
00:41:24,580 --> 00:41:28,250
- putting up walls against each other.
- Right.

890
00:41:28,490 --> 00:41:30,960
Was the reason for declaring war
a shortage of lives?

891
00:41:30,960 --> 00:41:33,660
No. We needed to know
if you guys were bluffing.

892
00:41:33,660 --> 00:41:34,730
Bluffing about what?

893
00:41:34,730 --> 00:41:35,730
Lives.

894
00:41:36,060 --> 00:41:37,860
We weren't able to talk it out.

895
00:41:39,770 --> 00:41:42,000
What was the first plan of Team Gold?

896
00:41:42,300 --> 00:41:46,070
As soon as you guys appeared,
you revealed Black's identity.

897
00:41:46,070 --> 00:41:48,940
You also thought about
blowing everything up.

898
00:41:48,940 --> 00:41:50,980
You considered making gold...

899
00:41:50,980 --> 00:41:52,740
- the main currency.
- Right.

900
00:41:52,740 --> 00:41:54,550
- Actually...
- To be honest,

901
00:41:54,550 --> 00:41:55,950
it's true that we were selfish.

902
00:41:55,950 --> 00:41:58,320
There was a reason why we missed out.

903
00:41:58,950 --> 00:42:01,190
We were starting a revolution.

904
00:42:01,420 --> 00:42:05,460
We were contributing to making
a better society.

905
00:42:05,460 --> 00:42:08,160
We had an idea that we deserved more.

906
00:42:08,160 --> 00:42:10,360
Was it simply just an issue of proportion?

907
00:42:10,360 --> 00:42:12,870
Well, that could be part of it.
It was because of stability.

908
00:42:12,870 --> 00:42:16,100
I think we were focused on our own profit.

909
00:42:17,170 --> 00:42:21,410
We even thought about this method.

910
00:42:21,640 --> 00:42:24,740
The first idea was to persuade everyone,
including Team Red.

911
00:42:25,180 --> 00:42:29,720
As Team Red has gained a lot of power
as the casting voter,

912
00:42:30,520 --> 00:42:32,850
considering that they have become
too greedy,

913
00:42:33,090 --> 00:42:36,360
the second idea was to join forces
only with Team White.

914
00:42:36,920 --> 00:42:38,120
- I see.
- Right.

915
00:42:39,160 --> 00:42:40,790
Are you going to declare war today?

916
00:42:40,790 --> 00:42:42,430
- No. There's no reason for that.
- No.

917
00:42:42,430 --> 00:42:44,260
- This is our last offer.
- Right.

918
00:42:44,260 --> 00:42:45,260
So let's make things clear.

919
00:42:45,260 --> 00:42:47,070
Team Red, Team Blue, and Team Black
will be excluded?

920
00:42:47,070 --> 00:42:48,970
- No.
- No. Red can be included.

921
00:42:48,970 --> 00:42:51,040
- They already have gold.
- Right.

922
00:42:51,040 --> 00:42:53,170
Based on the gold they have,

923
00:42:53,170 --> 00:42:55,470
it will be distributed equally.

924
00:42:55,470 --> 00:42:59,280
If you feel that our team
has too many members,

925
00:42:59,280 --> 00:43:01,210
I am willing to move.

926
00:43:01,550 --> 00:43:04,580
- So what I wish to do...
- Right.

927
00:43:04,580 --> 00:43:07,390
is to find the right balance.

928
00:43:07,590 --> 00:43:08,720
So...

929
00:43:09,320 --> 00:43:13,330
why is it better for us to live
in a world of gold in this process?

930
00:43:13,530 --> 00:43:17,230
The reason you're trying to persuade me...

931
00:43:17,230 --> 00:43:20,070
is that you're suggesting a move...

932
00:43:20,070 --> 00:43:22,730
- to a better and more developed world.
- Right.

933
00:43:22,730 --> 00:43:25,000
The reason why I feel torn...

934
00:43:25,000 --> 00:43:27,110
is that I don't know why
that is a better world.

935
00:43:27,110 --> 00:43:28,670
It's a transparent currency.

936
00:43:28,670 --> 00:43:31,580
- Right.
- If you consider this a real society...

937
00:43:31,580 --> 00:43:33,080
Think of it in that direction.

938
00:43:33,080 --> 00:43:35,710
I don't think it's an issue about it
being transparent or not.

939
00:43:35,710 --> 00:43:38,120
We don't have to be transparent
with our currency,

940
00:43:38,120 --> 00:43:40,050
but we're doing that on our own.

941
00:43:41,590 --> 00:43:44,860
I think it will be neater to say
that you guys wish to win as well.

942
00:43:45,960 --> 00:43:47,090
I couldn't understand them.

943
00:43:47,090 --> 00:43:49,660
I made this offer 2 or 3 days ago.

944
00:43:49,860 --> 00:43:54,870
They made another offer
with the project of choosing gold.

945
00:43:54,870 --> 00:43:56,070
And now,

946
00:43:56,440 --> 00:43:58,870
I believe it's their last resort...

947
00:43:58,870 --> 00:44:01,310
to go in that direction again.

948
00:44:01,640 --> 00:44:04,740
"We wish to live,"

949
00:44:04,940 --> 00:44:06,180
"but there's no other way."

950
00:44:06,650 --> 00:44:08,250
"If we do this,"

951
00:44:08,250 --> 00:44:12,120
"Team White or Team Red
can earn a better profit."

952
00:44:12,320 --> 00:44:15,720
Putting it like this
would've sounded much more honest...

953
00:44:16,020 --> 00:44:18,490
at this point.

954
00:44:20,160 --> 00:44:25,900
There's one last offer we wish to make.

955
00:44:26,030 --> 00:44:29,400
This was the conclusion we reached
after talking it through.

956
00:44:29,840 --> 00:44:33,140
She did her best
when she was in Team White.

957
00:44:33,470 --> 00:44:37,840
She had no choice but to act this way
because of the role she was given.

958
00:44:38,140 --> 00:44:39,280
As with Luna,

959
00:44:40,210 --> 00:44:41,580
we wish that...

960
00:44:42,150 --> 00:44:44,980
you guys would embrace her in the end.

961
00:44:45,680 --> 00:44:47,720
Luna doesn't know about this.

962
00:44:48,220 --> 00:44:50,990
- We didn't want to make her feel bad.
- Right.

963
00:44:50,990 --> 00:44:52,820
This was purely out of...

964
00:44:52,820 --> 00:44:54,260
- humanitarian consideration, right?
- Right.

965
00:44:54,260 --> 00:44:55,260
- Yes.
- Yes.

966
00:44:55,260 --> 00:44:56,430
Please put some thought into that.

967
00:44:56,430 --> 00:44:58,130
- That would be great.
- Right.

968
00:44:58,460 --> 00:45:00,970
- I'll be honest.
- Right.

969
00:45:00,970 --> 00:45:02,570
I'm willing to take you back.

970
00:45:02,570 --> 00:45:04,000
You tried to get me back, right?

971
00:45:04,000 --> 00:45:05,240
Yes. That's why I'm here.

972
00:45:05,640 --> 00:45:08,710
The only thing Team Gold can do
is declare war.

973
00:45:08,710 --> 00:45:09,710
Right.

974
00:45:09,910 --> 00:45:12,040
This is from my pure heart.

975
00:45:12,040 --> 00:45:14,950
I felt so bad seeing you wither away.

976
00:45:15,210 --> 00:45:18,820
"I'm a spy from Team Gold."

977
00:45:18,820 --> 00:45:20,190
"Is it right for me to speak
with Team White?"

978
00:45:20,190 --> 00:45:22,650
I believe you would've gone through
many different thoughts,

979
00:45:22,650 --> 00:45:25,720
but I wish to allow you
to end as a Team White member.

980
00:45:26,220 --> 00:45:28,990
You won't accept another member
from Team Gold, right?

981
00:45:29,160 --> 00:45:30,160
I won't.

982
00:45:33,670 --> 00:45:36,770
The other members of Team Gold
were already enemies.

983
00:45:36,870 --> 00:45:38,400
They were enemies,

984
00:45:38,570 --> 00:45:40,540
and they offered to save only me.

985
00:45:40,610 --> 00:45:45,710
They believed that I was suffering
in this whole situation.

986
00:45:46,040 --> 00:45:50,950
It was true that I was struggling,
but it wasn't because I was in Team Gold.

987
00:45:51,280 --> 00:45:52,780
But actually,

988
00:45:53,350 --> 00:45:54,890
- I was always a Team Gold member.
- Right.

989
00:45:55,220 --> 00:45:57,160
I wanted to do my best
as a Team Gold member.

990
00:45:57,160 --> 00:46:00,060
Excluding Team Gold...

991
00:46:00,630 --> 00:46:02,890
was never an option for me,

992
00:46:02,890 --> 00:46:04,430
- to be honest.
- Right.

993
00:46:04,430 --> 00:46:07,500
That was why I wanted to help Team Gold
and Team White...

994
00:46:07,500 --> 00:46:08,900
earn the greatest profit.

995
00:46:08,900 --> 00:46:12,670
The best scenario that I came up with
was the one I shared with Leia.

996
00:46:12,670 --> 00:46:14,340
Through the self-destruct project,

997
00:46:14,340 --> 00:46:15,640
we will move at least two
of our members...

998
00:46:15,640 --> 00:46:16,910
and live off gold.

999
00:46:16,910 --> 00:46:18,740
- That was my idea.
- I also thought that was the best method.

1000
00:46:19,210 --> 00:46:21,450
That day was the greatest opportunity
for Team Gold.

1001
00:46:21,450 --> 00:46:23,050
- Right. But...
- The day Black caused chaos.

1002
00:46:23,050 --> 00:46:24,180
there was no way
for me to make that happen.

1003
00:46:24,180 --> 00:46:25,950
- I didn't have the right reasoning.
- But...

1004
00:46:25,950 --> 00:46:27,390
- All that was wanted from me...
- But...

1005
00:46:27,390 --> 00:46:29,150
- was to save Team White.
- you shouldn't have talked to the team.

1006
00:46:29,150 --> 00:46:31,790
You should've shared that with me as well.

1007
00:46:32,260 --> 00:46:35,960
All of this happened
because of a block in communication.

1008
00:46:35,960 --> 00:46:38,360
After today's conversation,

1009
00:46:38,530 --> 00:46:42,430
I realized all of this happened
because of the refusal...

1010
00:46:42,430 --> 00:46:44,240
to move into our team.

1011
00:46:44,240 --> 00:46:46,200
Realizing that made everything make sense.

1012
00:46:46,200 --> 00:46:48,340
The winner and loser were already decided,

1013
00:46:48,340 --> 00:46:51,280
and it felt like I lost without even
being able to compete.

1014
00:46:51,640 --> 00:46:53,810
- I struggled because of that.
- Right.

1015
00:46:53,810 --> 00:46:55,280
- I now know why everything has happened.
- Right.

1016
00:46:55,280 --> 00:46:58,020
It doesn't matter if it happened
because of a misunderstanding...

1017
00:46:58,020 --> 00:46:59,050
or bad decision-making.

1018
00:46:59,050 --> 00:47:00,450
I just need to understand
why things happened this way.

1019
00:47:00,450 --> 00:47:02,520
After realizing that it was because
of a lack of my abilities,

1020
00:47:02,520 --> 00:47:04,490
I want to go back in time
to recover from this disappointment.

1021
00:47:04,490 --> 00:47:06,960
I love seeing you smile like this.

1022
00:47:06,960 --> 00:47:09,230
We did a great job with our roles.

1023
00:47:09,230 --> 00:47:11,430
- I did things to get information.
- Right.

1024
00:47:11,430 --> 00:47:14,400
Since you were a spy,
be a spy until the end.

1025
00:47:14,400 --> 00:47:16,700
Be a double spy.

1026
00:47:17,970 --> 00:47:19,470
Won't that be better?

1027
00:47:20,840 --> 00:47:22,370
To be honest,

1028
00:47:22,370 --> 00:47:25,980
everything has been decided
in my situation.

1029
00:47:26,340 --> 00:47:27,450
Well,

1030
00:47:28,280 --> 00:47:30,380
I don't wish to win like that.

1031
00:47:30,550 --> 00:47:32,850
That isn't my idea of how I wish to win.

1032
00:47:34,420 --> 00:47:36,920
I will have to make a decision,

1033
00:47:37,420 --> 00:47:39,590
but I don't wish to move.

1034
00:47:39,590 --> 00:47:40,830
- Right.
- I believe...

1035
00:47:40,830 --> 00:47:43,530
this is a punishment
that I have brought upon myself...

1036
00:47:43,530 --> 00:47:45,430
for my bad decision-making.

1037
00:47:45,660 --> 00:47:47,400
- Do as you wish.
- You get what I'm saying, right?

1038
00:47:47,400 --> 00:47:48,770
- It's up to you to decide.
- Right.

1039
00:47:49,000 --> 00:47:52,040
You saved me once.

1040
00:47:52,370 --> 00:47:55,340
It broke my heart to see you wither away.

1041
00:47:55,340 --> 00:47:56,680
That was why I wished to save you as well.

1042
00:47:56,680 --> 00:47:58,880
Things are clearer for me now.

1043
00:47:58,880 --> 00:48:01,180
I won't wither away now.

1044
00:48:01,510 --> 00:48:02,650
I feel better now.

1045
00:48:02,650 --> 00:48:03,850
- That's a relief.
- Right.

1046
00:48:04,380 --> 00:48:07,320
If you have a change of heart,

1047
00:48:08,020 --> 00:48:09,860
- make sure to let me know.
- Right.

1048
00:48:10,790 --> 00:48:14,530
Luna seemed to have
a greater affection toward Team Gold.

1049
00:48:14,530 --> 00:48:18,130
She wished to end the game
as a Team Gold member.

1050
00:48:18,130 --> 00:48:19,970
I still didn't give up on her.

1051
00:48:19,970 --> 00:48:22,200
I couldn't leave her out.

1052
00:48:23,130 --> 00:48:24,900
Do you still have more to talk about?

1053
00:48:24,900 --> 00:48:26,300
- Well,
- We're done.

1054
00:48:26,300 --> 00:48:27,770
- I've shared my thoughts.
- Right. I'll think about it.

1055
00:48:27,770 --> 00:48:29,510
- We'll end here.
- Right.

1056
00:48:29,510 --> 00:48:30,640
- Thank you for coming.
- Thank you.

1057
00:48:30,640 --> 00:48:31,840
We should've talked sooner like this.

1058
00:48:31,840 --> 00:48:33,610
- Right. This is such a great sight...
- What a bummer.

1059
00:48:33,610 --> 00:48:35,580
- even when we're against each other.
- We should've gone to see you guys.

1060
00:48:35,580 --> 00:48:38,280
- We lacked communication.
- Right.

1061
00:48:38,280 --> 00:48:41,390
Feel free to ring the bell at any time.

1062
00:48:41,390 --> 00:48:42,550
- Right.
- Knock at our door.

1063
00:48:42,550 --> 00:48:43,920
- Okay.
- We'll be waiting.

1064
00:48:43,920 --> 00:48:45,020
- Okay.
- Thank you.

1065
00:48:45,020 --> 00:48:46,460
Bye. Get some rest.

1066
00:48:50,060 --> 00:48:52,560
- I've shared my thoughts.
- What did you say?

1067
00:48:52,560 --> 00:48:53,930
- Did you ask if she wanted to return?
- Yes.

1068
00:48:53,930 --> 00:48:54,930
What did she say?

1069
00:48:54,930 --> 00:48:56,300
- She said she'll think about it.
- Right.

1070
00:48:56,300 --> 00:48:58,140
- She'll have to think carefully.
- They mentioned this as well.

1071
00:48:58,970 --> 00:49:03,170
No matter what happens,
they wanted us to save Luna...

1072
00:49:03,280 --> 00:49:04,780
- based on humanitarian considerations.
- Right.

1073
00:49:05,010 --> 00:49:07,050
- But they didn't tell Luna about this.
- Right.

1074
00:49:07,450 --> 00:49:09,880
- I think everyone feels pity toward Luna.
- Right.

1075
00:49:09,880 --> 00:49:12,220
They suggested that...

1076
00:49:12,220 --> 00:49:14,290
- we take Luna back.
- Right.

1077
00:49:16,050 --> 00:49:18,160
So what's their stance right now?

1078
00:49:18,760 --> 00:49:19,760
"Come to Team Gold?"

1079
00:49:20,330 --> 00:49:23,030
They will sacrifice
some of their members as well.

1080
00:49:24,200 --> 00:49:27,030
But in this situation,

1081
00:49:27,570 --> 00:49:30,200
Team White and Team Red can't break up.

1082
00:49:30,200 --> 00:49:31,940
- That isn't possible.
- Right.

1083
00:49:32,370 --> 00:49:33,770
Should we meet Maillard?

1084
00:49:33,770 --> 00:49:34,770
Sounds good.

1085
00:49:46,080 --> 00:49:47,620
- My gosh!
- Yes?

1086
00:49:47,620 --> 00:49:48,850
We weren't able to see you today.

1087
00:49:48,850 --> 00:49:50,490
- We've had our talks.
- Did you talk to them?

1088
00:49:50,490 --> 00:49:51,720
- We've talked to them.
- Right.

1089
00:49:51,720 --> 00:49:52,820
- We talked with Team Gold.
- Right.

1090
00:49:52,820 --> 00:49:54,460
- As you would have expected...
- What did you talk about with them?

1091
00:49:54,460 --> 00:49:55,560
- Well...
- They came to us first.

1092
00:49:55,560 --> 00:49:57,860
Team Gold came to see me in the morning.

1093
00:49:58,130 --> 00:49:59,830
- Simply put,
- Okay.

1094
00:49:59,860 --> 00:50:01,730
- they want us to move to their team.
- Okay.

1095
00:50:01,870 --> 00:50:04,600
So I asked, "What's good about that?"

1096
00:50:04,600 --> 00:50:06,810
And they said, "Team Black and Team Blue
will be punished,"

1097
00:50:06,810 --> 00:50:09,940
"and the rest will share the prize money
with gold."

1098
00:50:09,940 --> 00:50:12,080
That's because gold is spread out
right now.

1099
00:50:12,080 --> 00:50:14,080
So with the idea of serving justice,

1100
00:50:14,080 --> 00:50:16,780
- They wish to...
- they wish to make a way for themselves.

1101
00:50:16,780 --> 00:50:17,820
- Right.
- Right.

1102
00:50:17,820 --> 00:50:19,680
- I believe that's a good move.
- Right.

1103
00:50:20,090 --> 00:50:22,520
But I don't think I'll be accepting that.

1104
00:50:22,520 --> 00:50:23,520
Right.

1105
00:50:24,120 --> 00:50:25,560
It's our eighth day.

1106
00:50:25,890 --> 00:50:27,790
This isn't a time for harmony.

1107
00:50:28,090 --> 00:50:30,660
Team Gold was slow
with all of their decisions.

1108
00:50:30,660 --> 00:50:31,960
Tomorrow is the last day.

1109
00:50:32,330 --> 00:50:33,970
And as for Luna,

1110
00:50:34,500 --> 00:50:37,070
- We'll wait for Luna.
- we'll try to persuade her.

1111
00:50:37,070 --> 00:50:39,370
If war is declared today,
it will be by Team Blue.

1112
00:50:39,970 --> 00:50:41,840
If Team White does not wish
to join the fight,

1113
00:50:41,840 --> 00:50:43,140
- Team Red will.
- Right.

1114
00:50:43,540 --> 00:50:45,040
You don't have to spend anything...

1115
00:50:45,440 --> 00:50:46,540
or do anything.

1116
00:50:46,910 --> 00:50:49,180
This is a decision Leia should make.

1117
00:50:51,180 --> 00:50:52,720
This is why Team Blue must declare war.

1118
00:50:52,850 --> 00:50:54,290
Next morning,

1119
00:50:54,820 --> 00:50:57,760
we might be able to make a vote...

1120
00:50:58,020 --> 00:50:59,660
with the same number of lives
and credits...

1121
00:50:59,860 --> 00:51:02,760
as the number of members.

1122
00:51:03,090 --> 00:51:04,100
Right.

1123
00:51:04,100 --> 00:51:07,230
Out of the resources we are producing,

1124
00:51:07,230 --> 00:51:10,940
the hardest ones to produce are lives.

1125
00:51:10,940 --> 00:51:14,240
When the final vote happens,

1126
00:51:14,240 --> 00:51:18,380
we each might need one life
to make a vote.

1127
00:51:18,380 --> 00:51:20,550
In any way possible,

1128
00:51:20,750 --> 00:51:24,420
lives can become a variable
at the very last moment.

1129
00:51:24,420 --> 00:51:26,450
My final plan is to...

1130
00:51:26,580 --> 00:51:31,660
have more lives than gold.

1131
00:51:32,120 --> 00:51:34,390
This is why the resources...

1132
00:51:34,390 --> 00:51:35,860
- must be distributed like this.
- Right.

1133
00:51:35,860 --> 00:51:37,860
Team Red must have eight lives left.

1134
00:51:37,860 --> 00:51:40,630
Team Blue must have 4 lives left.
Team White must have 6 lives left.

1135
00:51:40,630 --> 00:51:42,570
- This is why.
- Why must Team Blue have four left?

1136
00:51:42,730 --> 00:51:44,840
We lose half of what we have
when we lose at war.

1137
00:51:45,270 --> 00:51:47,710
- One must be spent.
- Right.

1138
00:51:47,710 --> 00:51:49,170
(Four lives are required
while considering the spoils.)

1139
00:51:49,910 --> 00:51:54,110
We have issued 100 million diamonds
so far.

1140
00:51:54,250 --> 00:51:59,180
Around 25,000 dollars worth of diamonds...

1141
00:51:59,280 --> 00:52:00,950
were spent on weapons of war.

1142
00:52:01,090 --> 00:52:04,420
The weapon dealer
and the ally of the weapon dealer...

1143
00:52:04,560 --> 00:52:06,830
each have 12,500 dollars.

1144
00:52:06,830 --> 00:52:09,860
The remaining 75,000 dollars
must be shared.

1145
00:52:09,860 --> 00:52:11,800
When divided by six,

1146
00:52:11,800 --> 00:52:13,400
it's 12,500 dollars.

1147
00:52:14,100 --> 00:52:17,200
Excluding Donkey,
it's 37,500 dollars for the 3 in Team Red.

1148
00:52:17,570 --> 00:52:20,570
As for Team Blue,
it's 12,500 dollars for Pitou.

1149
00:52:20,870 --> 00:52:23,210
As for Team White,
it's 25,000 dollars for 2.

1150
00:52:23,210 --> 00:52:25,140
That's the overall plan.

1151
00:52:25,140 --> 00:52:27,480
So you'll work on this
when trading begins.

1152
00:52:27,710 --> 00:52:29,550
- I'll work on this when trading begins.
- Right.

1153
00:52:29,750 --> 00:52:31,280
The bomb will be used after that.

1154
00:52:31,650 --> 00:52:34,190
Let's not use the bomb.
We have to save our credits.

1155
00:52:34,650 --> 00:52:36,350
- That was included as well.
- That was included as well.

1156
00:52:36,860 --> 00:52:38,360
After using the bomb, we'll declare war.

1157
00:52:40,190 --> 00:52:41,790
But do we really have to go to war?

1158
00:52:42,130 --> 00:52:43,730
We must go to war.

1159
00:52:44,360 --> 00:52:45,500
- It's inevitable for us.
- Right.

1160
00:52:46,970 --> 00:52:48,900
Team Red shared that...

1161
00:52:49,300 --> 00:52:52,370
they were going to use the bomb,
which is their skill.

1162
00:52:52,500 --> 00:52:54,470
As a comparison to our history,

1163
00:52:54,470 --> 00:52:57,810
it's some sort of nuclear bomb.

1164
00:52:58,010 --> 00:53:02,450
It has the effect of blocking resistance.

1165
00:53:03,450 --> 00:53:05,420
I wondered if that was really necessary.

1166
00:53:05,880 --> 00:53:08,590
And if the bomb were to be used,

1167
00:53:08,790 --> 00:53:11,460
I wondered if going to war was necessary.

1168
00:53:12,360 --> 00:53:15,590
We were already in a very good position.

1169
00:53:15,790 --> 00:53:19,060
It made me think that going to war
was to fill the last one percent...

1170
00:53:19,060 --> 00:53:21,330
of the 99 percent we already had.

1171
00:53:25,400 --> 00:53:28,740
What play can Team Gold make?

1172
00:53:30,380 --> 00:53:31,940
- Hey!
- How did it go?

1173
00:53:32,180 --> 00:53:34,550
- We didn't do great.
- Right.

1174
00:53:34,850 --> 00:53:36,180
- To our disappointment...
- We missed a lot of them.

1175
00:53:36,310 --> 00:53:38,120
I heard the clapping three times.

1176
00:53:38,320 --> 00:53:39,320
You heard the clapping?

1177
00:53:39,520 --> 00:53:41,990
- It looks like they're acting.
- I heard clapping.

1178
00:53:41,990 --> 00:53:43,050
It seems like they produced a lot.

1179
00:53:43,050 --> 00:53:44,520
The production efficiency was really low.

1180
00:53:44,520 --> 00:53:46,460
- So how many did you produce?
- Should we tell you...

1181
00:53:46,460 --> 00:53:47,790
- how many questions we answered?
- Yes.

1182
00:53:47,990 --> 00:53:49,390
- Five?
- We...

1183
00:53:49,660 --> 00:53:50,830
We answered eight questions.

1184
00:53:50,960 --> 00:53:53,030
(Team Production did a great job.)

1185
00:53:53,030 --> 00:53:54,570
- Gosh!
- Gosh!

1186
00:53:54,570 --> 00:53:56,800
- Siseon carried us today.
- Really?

1187
00:53:56,900 --> 00:53:58,440
That's our man!

1188
00:53:58,440 --> 00:53:59,900
We got our job done.

1189
00:53:59,900 --> 00:54:01,440
- Maillard will get things sorted for us.
- You still have more to do.

1190
00:54:01,440 --> 00:54:02,840
- What?
- You still have more to do.

1191
00:54:02,840 --> 00:54:03,980
- There's a mission.
- Me?

1192
00:54:04,110 --> 00:54:05,740
You are today's warlord.

1193
00:54:05,940 --> 00:54:07,880
Gosh! You have to try going to war!

1194
00:54:07,980 --> 00:54:09,050
You have to declare war at this point.

1195
00:54:09,310 --> 00:54:11,250
That is why your diamonds
will be taken from you for now.

1196
00:54:11,720 --> 00:54:12,780
Understood.

1197
00:54:14,390 --> 00:54:15,850
But do you know what the problem is?

1198
00:54:15,850 --> 00:54:17,220
The Platform won't open tomorrow.

1199
00:54:17,220 --> 00:54:19,560
- The Community will close.
- Today will be the final count.

1200
00:54:19,660 --> 00:54:21,230
We should forget about tomorrow...

1201
00:54:21,230 --> 00:54:22,960
- and end things today.
- Right.

1202
00:54:23,160 --> 00:54:26,400
So we have to get
the calculations done today...

1203
00:54:26,400 --> 00:54:27,630
- Right.
- with the numbers.

1204
00:54:27,630 --> 00:54:28,700
- Except for those.
- Right.

1205
00:54:28,700 --> 00:54:30,270
How should we relocate ourselves?

1206
00:54:30,270 --> 00:54:31,900
- Team White should have a few members.
- We have to think about...

1207
00:54:31,900 --> 00:54:35,370
where we will relocate and become allies.

1208
00:54:35,370 --> 00:54:38,380
As of right now, the ones in Team White...

1209
00:54:38,880 --> 00:54:40,850
will be Paul and Leia.

1210
00:54:40,850 --> 00:54:42,450
If they are to have someone else,

1211
00:54:42,450 --> 00:54:44,120
- it will be Luna. That's it for them.
- Right.

1212
00:54:44,120 --> 00:54:45,780
The ones left in Team Red...

1213
00:54:45,880 --> 00:54:47,050
- will be like this.
- Right.

1214
00:54:47,050 --> 00:54:48,520
Team Blue will be like this.

1215
00:54:48,520 --> 00:54:50,290
- It will change...
- If she decides to move.

1216
00:54:50,290 --> 00:54:51,960
- based on Luna's decision.
- Right.

1217
00:54:51,960 --> 00:54:55,060
For your information,
Team Gold said this in the morning.

1218
00:54:55,330 --> 00:54:57,930
They made an offer to go with gold,

1219
00:54:57,930 --> 00:54:59,860
as they will make a few sacrifices.

1220
00:54:59,860 --> 00:55:01,630
- I will refuse their offer.
- Right.

1221
00:55:01,630 --> 00:55:02,630
That's it.

1222
00:55:02,730 --> 00:55:06,470
Changing the currency to gold...

1223
00:55:06,740 --> 00:55:08,110
- doesn't make sense.
- Right.

1224
00:55:08,570 --> 00:55:10,340
There's a trade ban,

1225
00:55:10,340 --> 00:55:11,540
so the gold cannot be distributed.

1226
00:55:11,540 --> 00:55:13,440
- Right. There's a trade ban.
- It's just the gold we have.

1227
00:55:13,440 --> 00:55:15,010
And to distribute gold,

1228
00:55:15,010 --> 00:55:16,410
credits must be spent...

1229
00:55:16,410 --> 00:55:17,920
- during each trade.
- Right.

1230
00:55:18,050 --> 00:55:19,980
- We're very short...
- It's hard to maintain the balance.

1231
00:55:19,980 --> 00:55:21,350
on credits to be able to do that.

1232
00:55:21,590 --> 00:55:24,160
- There's no way to distribute gold.
- Right.

1233
00:55:24,390 --> 00:55:26,460
All possibilities were closed down.

1234
00:55:26,460 --> 00:55:27,630
We stopped them from doing anything.

1235
00:55:27,630 --> 00:55:30,090
- It's suffocating for them.
- We stopped them from doing anything.

1236
00:55:30,460 --> 00:55:32,060
As they might find a way...

1237
00:55:32,060 --> 00:55:34,630
- to shake us up,
- Right.

1238
00:55:34,800 --> 00:55:37,970
I gave them a trade ban
to secure a complete victory.

1239
00:55:38,470 --> 00:55:40,670
I'm here to collect
the produced resources.

1240
00:55:41,470 --> 00:55:43,110
(Team Blue's produced resource)

1241
00:55:43,110 --> 00:55:46,640
(Team Blue's produced resource: 8 lives)

1242
00:55:46,640 --> 00:55:47,650
I'm rich.

1243
00:55:48,550 --> 00:55:50,210
Goodbye.

1244
00:55:50,950 --> 00:55:52,520
(Resources After Day 8's Production)

1245
00:55:52,520 --> 00:55:54,290
(Team Blue:
12,500,000 diamonds, 16 credits)

1246
00:55:54,290 --> 00:55:58,120
(Team Blue: 8 lives)

1247
00:55:58,190 --> 00:55:59,960
(Resources After Day 8's Production)

1248
00:56:00,260 --> 00:56:02,860
(Relocation request)

1249
00:56:04,760 --> 00:56:07,400
- I will return to Red.
- I request a relocation.

1250
00:56:08,400 --> 00:56:10,770
- Will you accept it?
- I accept it.

1251
00:56:12,340 --> 00:56:13,340
Let's go and eat.

1252
00:56:14,340 --> 00:56:15,340
Okay.

1253
00:56:15,870 --> 00:56:17,740
- Are you drawing again?
- Yes.

1254
00:56:18,340 --> 00:56:20,880
(Maillard plans for a resource move
ahead of a 3rd war.)

1255
00:56:21,810 --> 00:56:24,580
It's the trading session
in the afternoon after lunch, right?

1256
00:56:24,580 --> 00:56:25,620
Yes.

1257
00:56:25,680 --> 00:56:27,520
- We can't trade.
- Right.

1258
00:56:27,520 --> 00:56:29,750
- Should we go and watch?
- We'll go and watch.

1259
00:56:29,750 --> 00:56:31,690
- Right.
- Let's watch how they move...

1260
00:56:31,690 --> 00:56:33,930
and try to make them come to us.

1261
00:56:34,430 --> 00:56:37,130
There's a lot of lobbying
in the real world.

1262
00:56:37,130 --> 00:56:39,660
- Right.
- It's not just presidents talking.

1263
00:56:39,960 --> 00:56:41,870
- Right.
- It could be international organizations.

1264
00:56:41,870 --> 00:56:43,770
- It could be business people.
- Right.

1265
00:56:43,840 --> 00:56:48,510
We should make an appeal
with different points of view.

1266
00:56:49,870 --> 00:56:54,780
Many of the decisions haven't been made...

1267
00:56:55,010 --> 00:56:56,450
just on the expected value.

1268
00:56:56,450 --> 00:57:02,450
We should belatedly acknowledge
that we didn't get ourselves involved...

1269
00:57:02,450 --> 00:57:04,420
and try to make ourselves work with them.

1270
00:57:06,790 --> 00:57:07,860
The weather is great.

1271
00:57:08,260 --> 00:57:10,130
- Right.
- It's in use.

1272
00:57:10,400 --> 00:57:11,400
Where?

1273
00:57:11,660 --> 00:57:13,060
Isn't that where the resources
are collected?

1274
00:57:13,060 --> 00:57:15,270
- The produced resources?
- Right.

1275
00:57:15,270 --> 00:57:16,670
Does it take that long?

1276
00:57:17,100 --> 00:57:18,140
I'm not sure.

1277
00:57:18,770 --> 00:57:21,040
(Vector is setting
the war and weapon costs.)

1278
00:57:21,470 --> 00:57:24,980
The war cost will be set
to zero diamonds and zero gold.

1279
00:57:25,480 --> 00:57:28,210
The war cost has been set.

1280
00:57:30,380 --> 00:57:32,280
I will announce the weapon cost.

1281
00:57:32,620 --> 00:57:34,190
It will be set to zero diamonds...

1282
00:57:34,990 --> 00:57:36,450
and zero gold.

1283
00:57:38,090 --> 00:57:40,660
The weapon cost has been set.

1284
00:57:41,490 --> 00:57:44,230
The members
of the diamond alliance became one.

1285
00:57:44,560 --> 00:57:46,960
For them to share resources freely,

1286
00:57:47,430 --> 00:57:51,300
declare war to their advantage,
and avoid the most damage,

1287
00:57:51,300 --> 00:57:52,970
a weapon cost can't be set.

1288
00:57:52,970 --> 00:57:56,240
That was why I set everything to zero.

1289
00:57:57,140 --> 00:58:03,050
(Lunchtime)

1290
00:58:05,350 --> 00:58:08,150
I think it will be neat to tell you now.

1291
00:58:08,590 --> 00:58:09,720
I gave it some thought.

1292
00:58:11,090 --> 00:58:12,420
I think it will be hard
to accept your offer.

1293
00:58:12,420 --> 00:58:13,760
- Right.
- All right.

1294
00:58:13,760 --> 00:58:15,860
For me to make this decision,

1295
00:58:15,860 --> 00:58:17,660
my team members have to go.

1296
00:58:17,660 --> 00:58:20,830
I couldn't reach an agreement
with my team members.

1297
00:58:20,930 --> 00:58:22,670
I thought it would be fair...

1298
00:58:22,670 --> 00:58:24,540
- to tell you as soon as possible.
- Right.

1299
00:58:24,540 --> 00:58:25,840
That's the reason...

1300
00:58:25,840 --> 00:58:27,240
- I'm telling you now.
- Right.

1301
00:58:27,740 --> 00:58:30,310
We've done everything we could.

1302
00:58:30,410 --> 00:58:32,340
We have to think of the next step.

1303
00:58:32,840 --> 00:58:35,750
I asked if you had a different plan.

1304
00:58:36,380 --> 00:58:39,750
- We have to think of one.
- I hope you can find a good way.

1305
00:58:40,050 --> 00:58:41,190
I hoped they had a different plan.

1306
00:58:41,490 --> 00:58:45,690
If this was their one and only plan,

1307
00:58:45,990 --> 00:58:48,330
I just broke it apart.

1308
00:58:49,190 --> 00:58:50,700
That was when I thought...

1309
00:58:51,160 --> 00:58:55,830
war would be their last resort.

1310
00:58:56,970 --> 00:58:59,600
Your special meal has arrived.

1311
00:59:00,300 --> 00:59:04,080
It's our last lunch today.
Should we eat together?

1312
00:59:04,340 --> 00:59:06,940
- We can share.
- I'm fine with that as well.

1313
00:59:08,250 --> 00:59:09,710
- We can all share.
- Right.

1314
00:59:09,710 --> 00:59:11,120
(Team Gold joins in for lunch today.)

1315
00:59:11,780 --> 00:59:12,850
It's curry.

1316
00:59:13,350 --> 00:59:15,820
Being in an actual conversation
with the others...

1317
00:59:16,290 --> 00:59:19,590
is the best way to fit into a community.

1318
00:59:20,160 --> 00:59:22,160
- Enjoy your meal.
- Enjoy your meal.

1319
00:59:22,290 --> 00:59:23,390
Enjoy your meal.

1320
00:59:23,730 --> 00:59:25,660
Why are you called Pitou?

1321
00:59:26,030 --> 00:59:29,500
It's from an animated series
called "Hunter x Hunter."

1322
00:59:29,500 --> 00:59:31,640
I watched "Hunter x Hunter."
Which character is that?

1323
00:59:31,640 --> 00:59:35,210
It's 1 of the 3 strongest Chimera Ants
toward the end.

1324
00:59:35,470 --> 00:59:38,110
Does Vector have to do with direction?

1325
00:59:38,110 --> 00:59:40,480
- Yes. It has to do with decisions and...
- It's similar to Ugong.

1326
00:59:40,480 --> 00:59:43,350
Ugong resembles direction as well.

1327
00:59:43,350 --> 00:59:44,850
Consistently going in one direction.

1328
00:59:44,850 --> 00:59:47,450
Why are you Mokgye? I heard
a brief explanation of it yesterday.

1329
00:59:47,650 --> 00:59:50,050
There's a four-character idiom
called "Mokgyejideok."

1330
00:59:50,590 --> 00:59:53,290
It's the state of being calm
in any situation,

1331
00:59:53,290 --> 00:59:56,360
looking like a chicken made of wood.

1332
00:59:56,660 --> 00:59:58,660
It's about keeping calm, right?

1333
00:59:58,800 --> 01:00:01,130
- Right.
- But you were shaken a lot yesterday.

1334
01:00:01,230 --> 01:00:03,300
- It's a goal.
- It's a goal.

1335
01:00:03,300 --> 01:00:05,400
- It's a goal.
- Why would you say that?

1336
01:00:05,400 --> 01:00:07,610
I was just trying to break the ice.

1337
01:00:07,610 --> 01:00:09,470
- Breaking the ice on the last day?
- Right.

1338
01:00:09,710 --> 01:00:11,740
- On the last day.
- This is the only chance.

1339
01:00:13,040 --> 01:00:15,280
- Breaking the ice.
- Right.

1340
01:00:17,250 --> 01:00:20,020
The atmosphere was great during lunch.

1341
01:00:20,380 --> 01:00:22,420
Team Gold joined in for lunch as well.

1342
01:00:22,420 --> 01:00:25,820
It felt like we finally had a proper meal.

1343
01:00:25,820 --> 01:00:28,430
I realized that they wanted to
play the game with genuine hearts,

1344
01:00:28,490 --> 01:00:30,460
but it took them too long to adapt.

1345
01:00:30,460 --> 01:00:32,130
Seeing the way they behaved
in the Town Hall...

1346
01:00:32,130 --> 01:00:34,070
and the way they came to us...

1347
01:00:34,070 --> 01:00:35,770
to talk to us...

1348
01:00:35,900 --> 01:00:40,910
made me want to stop declaring war
from an emotional perspective.

1349
01:00:41,510 --> 01:00:42,910
This sort of gathering...

1350
01:00:43,470 --> 01:00:45,710
should have happened days ago.

1351
01:00:46,780 --> 01:00:48,510
Transfer students always struggle.

1352
01:00:48,880 --> 01:00:51,180
That's how it is.
Everyone else was good friends,

1353
01:00:51,180 --> 01:00:53,080
but new transfer students came.

1354
01:00:53,420 --> 01:00:56,920
"Hi. We're smart and rich."

1355
01:00:57,090 --> 01:00:59,220
"Would you like to be our friends?"
If they go like this,

1356
01:00:59,220 --> 01:01:00,830
anyone would go, "That's rude."

1357
01:01:00,830 --> 01:01:03,430
No one would say, "Sure!"

1358
01:01:03,890 --> 01:01:05,630
I know because
I've transferred schools a lot.

1359
01:01:05,630 --> 01:01:07,130
I went to five different
elementary schools.

1360
01:01:08,100 --> 01:01:09,870
That was why it became
a lot more complicated for me.

1361
01:01:10,900 --> 01:01:13,000
"Why behave this way now?"

1362
01:01:13,100 --> 01:01:16,840
"We're planning other things right now."

1363
01:01:17,510 --> 01:01:20,410
I knew that sitting and laughing
with each other...

1364
01:01:20,950 --> 01:01:23,310
was a temporary moment of peace.

1365
01:01:24,250 --> 01:01:27,590
I sat with them
and left out of frustration.

1366
01:01:32,220 --> 01:01:35,130
(Luna approaches Leia.)

1367
01:01:37,600 --> 01:01:39,730
- This is a personal thing.
- Right.

1368
01:01:41,770 --> 01:01:45,770
I'm so annoyed with Team Black
and Team Blue.

1369
01:01:48,370 --> 01:01:50,010
Unlike us, other teams...

1370
01:01:50,010 --> 01:01:53,510
seem indebted to those
who sacrificed themselves...

1371
01:01:53,640 --> 01:01:55,580
for the game.

1372
01:01:56,010 --> 01:01:58,450
Meanwhile, the enemy is the one...

1373
01:01:58,850 --> 01:02:01,890
who caused unnecessary sacrifices.

1374
01:02:01,890 --> 01:02:04,360
Team Blue is the one
that suddenly started a war,

1375
01:02:04,790 --> 01:02:09,260
and the ones who were sacrificed
were Hamlet, Boss, Genie, and Salt.

1376
01:02:09,530 --> 01:02:11,360
However, people don't seem
to think about...

1377
01:02:11,360 --> 01:02:13,360
who forced them out of the compound.

1378
01:02:13,700 --> 01:02:17,270
For instance,
Team Blue had a lot of lives to spare,

1379
01:02:17,500 --> 01:02:19,140
and Team Black was the weapon dealer.

1380
01:02:19,340 --> 01:02:23,740
After the revelation,
their anger should've been channeled...

1381
01:02:24,010 --> 01:02:26,580
in the same direction as mine.

1382
01:02:27,080 --> 01:02:32,050
I didn't get why everyone else wasn't
as furious with them as I was.

1383
01:02:32,550 --> 01:02:34,390
The ones I'm upset with...

1384
01:02:34,890 --> 01:02:38,290
aren't Team White or Team Red,
who are allied with them.

1385
01:02:38,290 --> 01:02:39,660
(Luna, Influencer)

1386
01:02:39,660 --> 01:02:42,160
It's Team Blue and Team Black
I'm mostly mad at.

1387
01:02:43,290 --> 01:02:46,000
I'm not asking everyone to be
on the same page,

1388
01:02:46,000 --> 01:02:47,060
but I still want confirmation.

1389
01:02:47,060 --> 01:02:48,730
You don't think that, right?

1390
01:02:51,240 --> 01:02:52,500
Am I annoyed with them?

1391
01:02:53,100 --> 01:02:54,110
Yes.

1392
01:02:54,540 --> 01:02:56,940
- But am I going to...
- Do something about it?

1393
01:02:57,740 --> 01:02:59,840
I must keep my team alive,

1394
01:03:00,510 --> 01:03:03,710
but achieving my goal
without excluding them...

1395
01:03:05,020 --> 01:03:07,280
won't be easy.
That's why I'm in this position.

1396
01:03:07,280 --> 01:03:09,350
That's why we started a war yesterday.

1397
01:03:10,620 --> 01:03:13,820
Let's say Siseon and Paul
joined Team Gold.

1398
01:03:14,190 --> 01:03:16,090
The team will have six people.

1399
01:03:16,090 --> 01:03:18,700
Including you, that will be seven votes.

1400
01:03:19,060 --> 01:03:22,000
If that happens, we'll get rid
of Red, Donkey, Black, and Blue.

1401
01:03:22,670 --> 01:03:24,470
But you don't hate them enough to do that.

1402
01:03:24,470 --> 01:03:26,570
We have too much history with Red.

1403
01:03:27,870 --> 01:03:29,740
- It's not that simple for you.
- Yes.

1404
01:03:30,740 --> 01:03:32,310
Why don't you join our team instead?

1405
01:03:33,440 --> 01:03:34,550
- Then...
- I...

1406
01:03:34,550 --> 01:03:36,280
don't want to share a prize with them.

1407
01:03:36,280 --> 01:03:38,780
I'd rather not win anything
than share a prize with Blue and Black.

1408
01:03:39,080 --> 01:03:40,890
That's how much I dislike them right now.

1409
01:03:40,890 --> 01:03:41,890
I see.

1410
01:03:42,590 --> 01:03:44,190
Let's take this back and talk some more.

1411
01:03:45,320 --> 01:03:46,890
Stay here. I'll be right back.

1412
01:03:47,990 --> 01:03:49,660
Who said they wanted hot dogs earlier?

1413
01:03:49,660 --> 01:03:51,030
- I want one.
- Me.

1414
01:03:51,730 --> 01:03:52,830
You're deciding...

1415
01:03:52,830 --> 01:03:55,030
- with your emotions right now.
- Yes.

1416
01:03:55,270 --> 01:03:58,640
We only joined forces with Team Red
because we have a common goal.

1417
01:03:58,870 --> 01:04:00,940
Maillard's only goal...

1418
01:04:00,940 --> 01:04:03,040
- is his team's survival.
- Right.

1419
01:04:03,740 --> 01:04:06,210
But Donkey's on that team too.

1420
01:04:06,580 --> 01:04:09,010
- That ties them to Black.
- Yes.

1421
01:04:09,250 --> 01:04:12,450
I've already accepted that
and given up on teaming up with them.

1422
01:04:12,450 --> 01:04:13,450
Right.

1423
01:04:13,450 --> 01:04:15,650
I don't want to share a prize with them.

1424
01:04:15,750 --> 01:04:17,450
I'd rather not switch teams.

1425
01:04:17,660 --> 01:04:20,290
That's my choice,
and I figured I should tell you that.

1426
01:04:26,630 --> 01:04:28,970
I believe we resemble each other a bit,

1427
01:04:29,600 --> 01:04:33,440
so if I were in your position right now,

1428
01:04:33,570 --> 01:04:35,710
I'd make the same choice.

1429
01:04:35,710 --> 01:04:37,640
- Right.
- Right.

1430
01:04:38,110 --> 01:04:40,580
That's why I want to respect your choice.

1431
01:04:41,350 --> 01:04:45,220
However,
although I'm with you emotionally,

1432
01:04:45,420 --> 01:04:47,690
I hope you know
I made a different choice...

1433
01:04:47,990 --> 01:04:50,090
because I'm choosing
as a member of a team,

1434
01:04:50,090 --> 01:04:52,260
not just for myself.

1435
01:04:52,260 --> 01:04:54,930
Had I been in your shoes,
I would've made the same decision.

1436
01:04:54,930 --> 01:04:56,360
- Right.
- I feel the same way.

1437
01:04:56,360 --> 01:04:57,430
Good.

1438
01:04:57,800 --> 01:04:59,660
We're in different positions now.

1439
01:04:59,660 --> 01:05:00,930
- We are.
- Right.

1440
01:05:02,900 --> 01:05:04,400
Still, you can always come to me to talk.

1441
01:05:04,800 --> 01:05:05,870
Got it.

1442
01:05:09,140 --> 01:05:10,510
- Okay.
- Off we go.

1443
01:05:10,840 --> 01:05:12,840
- What's in here?
- I put everything in here.

1444
01:05:13,340 --> 01:05:14,380
Lives too?

1445
01:05:14,380 --> 01:05:16,250
- Yes, 14 lives.
- Right.

1446
01:05:16,550 --> 01:05:18,880
There are some vouchers and the stamp.

1447
01:05:19,020 --> 01:05:20,580
Can't we carry them in our pockets?

1448
01:05:20,580 --> 01:05:22,790
- Are you afraid we'd lose these?
- To hide that we want to trade.

1449
01:05:23,520 --> 01:05:25,420
Oh, that. I see.

1450
01:05:25,420 --> 01:05:26,690
Can't we hide our intentions a bit?

1451
01:05:27,260 --> 01:05:29,830
(They carry the resources
in their pockets instead.)

1452
01:05:30,430 --> 01:05:32,700
- I can carry some more.
- No, I'm good.

1453
01:05:33,560 --> 01:05:35,070
- We're all set.
- Let's go.

1454
01:05:35,070 --> 01:05:36,170
Are we good?

1455
01:05:36,670 --> 01:05:37,970
- Do you have the stamp?
- Yes.

1456
01:05:37,970 --> 01:05:38,970
Off we go.

1457
01:05:39,740 --> 01:05:42,040
- I see you're already eating.
- Join us, guys.

1458
01:05:42,740 --> 01:05:44,410
- In the end, we...
- But...

1459
01:05:44,510 --> 01:05:45,780
(They see Leia talking to Luna.)

1460
01:05:45,780 --> 01:05:47,080
- I'm off.
- Okay.

1461
01:05:48,750 --> 01:05:50,680
- Isn't Luna going to join us?
- I think she's out.

1462
01:05:50,850 --> 01:05:52,780
- She'll choose not to join us?
- Yes.

1463
01:05:53,380 --> 01:05:56,120
I think she's just going to go out
with the rest of Team Gold.

1464
01:05:57,520 --> 01:05:59,120
We all have different opinions on things.

1465
01:06:01,490 --> 01:06:03,660
Not everyone thinks the same way.

1466
01:06:06,460 --> 01:06:08,070
That goes without saying, I suppose.

1467
01:06:09,500 --> 01:06:10,570
People...

1468
01:06:13,540 --> 01:06:15,310
I wonder what this is about.

1469
01:06:16,510 --> 01:06:18,880
This is an announcement
from the Community Center.

1470
01:06:19,240 --> 01:06:22,510
The trading for Day Eight will begin.

1471
01:06:22,910 --> 01:06:25,020
Please note that due to an agreement...

1472
01:06:25,220 --> 01:06:27,020
between the leaders,

1473
01:06:27,020 --> 01:06:29,490
Team Gold can't use the Trading Station.

1474
01:06:29,490 --> 01:06:30,820
Please keep this in mind.

1475
01:06:32,660 --> 01:06:34,290
Today's war cost...

1476
01:06:34,290 --> 01:06:36,790
(Today's war cost...)

1477
01:06:36,790 --> 01:06:40,760
is 0 diamonds and 0 gold.

1478
01:06:40,760 --> 01:06:42,930
(Today's war cost: 0 diamonds, 0 gold)

1479
01:06:44,170 --> 01:06:47,540
This concludes the announcement
from the Community Center.

1480
01:06:51,610 --> 01:06:53,040
They dropped bad news...

1481
01:06:53,880 --> 01:06:55,550
- when we were in a good mood.
- Well,

1482
01:06:56,910 --> 01:06:58,250
that certainly ruined the mood.

1483
01:07:10,060 --> 01:07:11,160
The next keyword,

1484
01:07:12,100 --> 01:07:13,400
"What's a rut or a slump?"

1485
01:07:13,400 --> 01:07:15,500
- You're hooked, aren't you?
- A rut or a slump.

1486
01:07:16,700 --> 01:07:21,040
I only thought of polyamory
because of that relationship rut.

1487
01:07:21,040 --> 01:07:22,740
But that's impossible, right?

1488
01:07:22,740 --> 01:07:24,480
- Exactly.
- It's the same with friends.

1489
01:07:24,480 --> 01:07:26,540
Some friends are great company
when out shopping,

1490
01:07:26,540 --> 01:07:28,550
- You're right.
- while others aren't.

1491
01:07:28,550 --> 01:07:29,580
Like that,

1492
01:07:29,580 --> 01:07:32,220
some spouses give emotional support,

1493
01:07:32,220 --> 01:07:34,280
while others are good for only one thing.

1494
01:07:34,280 --> 01:07:37,150
Some spouses help you grow as a person...

1495
01:07:37,150 --> 01:07:38,660
- True.
- and open up new doors for your career.

1496
01:07:40,060 --> 01:07:42,560
Let's say you're dating someone who's...

1497
01:07:48,670 --> 01:07:52,770
Lunchtime was
the most anxious part of my day today.

1498
01:07:53,000 --> 01:07:57,470
To adjust our resources ahead of the war,

1499
01:07:57,710 --> 01:08:00,940
at least 12 trades needed to take place
at the Platform.

1500
01:08:00,940 --> 01:08:02,110
(Maillard, Cooking YouTuber)

1501
01:08:02,110 --> 01:08:03,910
But that takes quite a long time.

1502
01:08:04,050 --> 01:08:08,090
But with Team Gold already having a spot
at the Platform,

1503
01:08:08,090 --> 01:08:10,590
they could see trades taking place.

1504
01:08:10,590 --> 01:08:14,120
Anyone could tell
that the trading itself looked suspicious.

1505
01:08:14,560 --> 01:08:16,860
Had Team Gold noticed
something suspicious...

1506
01:08:16,860 --> 01:08:21,500
and headed straight
to the Community Center...

1507
01:08:21,600 --> 01:08:23,770
to wage war on any team here,

1508
01:08:23,770 --> 01:08:28,740
it would've posed a massive threat
to our alliance.

1509
01:08:28,970 --> 01:08:32,140
That's why that moment was
the most nerve-wracking for me.

1510
01:08:36,880 --> 01:08:38,650
I value my personal relationships.

1511
01:08:38,650 --> 01:08:40,380
- You know why?
- That's what I said.

1512
01:08:40,380 --> 01:08:41,850
- Doing this...
- Different, right?

1513
01:08:42,620 --> 01:08:43,750
Seriously?

1514
01:08:43,750 --> 01:08:47,690
The situation here
is very similar to an actual war.

1515
01:08:50,430 --> 01:08:53,400
One hour into the trading session.

1516
01:09:02,270 --> 01:09:05,510
Today was practically
the last day we could trade...

1517
01:09:05,510 --> 01:09:07,040
since a war will stop all transactions.

1518
01:09:07,040 --> 01:09:09,480
That's why before the war, we needed...

1519
01:09:09,480 --> 01:09:12,650
to balance the diamonds, credits,
and lives everyone needed to survive,

1520
01:09:12,650 --> 01:09:15,450
but Team Gold wouldn't leave
the Town Hall.

1521
01:09:15,720 --> 01:09:18,020
We didn't know when to make the trade.

1522
01:09:18,390 --> 01:09:19,690
As a person...

1523
01:09:24,460 --> 01:09:27,260
("We need to talk to Blue outside.")

1524
01:09:37,810 --> 01:09:39,040
- So...
- Hold on.

1525
01:09:40,240 --> 01:09:42,550
- I get that, but...
- Right?

1526
01:09:42,550 --> 01:09:44,180
By doing that...

1527
01:09:47,380 --> 01:09:48,420
What do you think?

1528
01:09:48,420 --> 01:09:50,120
I think Luna will just be on the outside.

1529
01:09:50,320 --> 01:09:51,690
- From this plan?
- Yes.

1530
01:09:52,060 --> 01:09:55,990
Luna's made up her mind
to go out with the rest of Team Gold.

1531
01:09:56,160 --> 01:09:57,430
- So, as it is...
- I see.

1532
01:09:57,430 --> 01:09:59,000
I get that, but when do we trade?

1533
01:09:59,000 --> 01:10:00,830
What if Team Gold won't leave?

1534
01:10:01,730 --> 01:10:05,740
Maillard said we needed to talk
to Blue outside.

1535
01:10:06,340 --> 01:10:08,840
- They're not thinking about leaving.
- Exactly.

1536
01:10:08,840 --> 01:10:11,210
This morning, they said
they weren't going to start a war.

1537
01:10:11,440 --> 01:10:13,010
- Then...
- I'm not sure about that.

1538
01:10:13,210 --> 01:10:15,850
- Even after saying that...
- That's why I'm hovering like this.

1539
01:10:16,150 --> 01:10:17,350
I'm holding my ground.

1540
01:10:18,680 --> 01:10:20,280
If Team Gold makes a move,

1541
01:10:20,280 --> 01:10:22,050
- I'm going to block them first.
- How can we trade...

1542
01:10:22,050 --> 01:10:23,190
when they're here?

1543
01:10:23,190 --> 01:10:24,620
- That's what I'm saying.
- Just...

1544
01:10:24,620 --> 01:10:26,060
Can't we just go ahead with the trade?

1545
01:10:26,060 --> 01:10:29,930
We obviously just need to get it done,
but we'll have to talk to Maillard first.

1546
01:10:33,330 --> 01:10:34,930
You should step outside for a bit.

1547
01:10:46,380 --> 01:10:48,650
Did you bring your resources?

1548
01:10:48,650 --> 01:10:50,550
- The credits and stuff?
- Yes, I have mine.

1549
01:10:50,550 --> 01:10:53,050
We need to trade, but they're not leaving.

1550
01:10:53,580 --> 01:10:55,220
We should just do it with them here.

1551
01:10:56,090 --> 01:10:57,750
They don't intend to start a war.

1552
01:10:57,750 --> 01:10:59,390
- Really?
- You can...

1553
01:10:59,560 --> 01:11:01,390
distribute the resources
and set off the bomb...

1554
01:11:01,390 --> 01:11:03,090
- to destroy lives.
- Right.

1555
01:11:03,330 --> 01:11:06,030
If they see red and start a war,

1556
01:11:06,030 --> 01:11:07,160
we can absorb their attack...

1557
01:11:07,160 --> 01:11:08,570
- and strike back.
- Sure.

1558
01:11:09,400 --> 01:11:11,670
They could pretend to go back
after making us lower our guard,

1559
01:11:11,670 --> 01:11:13,470
and then head over there instead.

1560
01:11:13,800 --> 01:11:15,010
You never know.

1561
01:11:15,270 --> 01:11:16,810
Why on earth are they still here?

1562
01:11:17,710 --> 01:11:19,840
They really don't intend to start a war.

1563
01:11:20,040 --> 01:11:21,310
That isn't entirely far-fetched.

1564
01:11:22,180 --> 01:11:25,020
That's how Team Gold operates.

1565
01:11:30,620 --> 01:11:31,720
- Is he the leader?
- No.

1566
01:11:31,720 --> 01:11:32,820
He's not, right?

1567
01:11:32,820 --> 01:11:34,090
- Mokgye's the leader.
- Right.

1568
01:11:34,560 --> 01:11:36,630
Mokgye keeps looking this way.

1569
01:11:37,060 --> 01:11:38,760
Mokgye has been looking our way.

1570
01:11:41,470 --> 01:11:43,700
- I'm the only one who's anxious.
- I know.

1571
01:11:44,640 --> 01:11:46,270
I have over ten trades...

1572
01:11:46,270 --> 01:11:48,110
- to get done today.
- Exactly.

1573
01:11:48,110 --> 01:11:50,040
He needs to get through all of them,
and fast.

1574
01:11:58,350 --> 01:11:59,480
It could be like this.

1575
01:11:59,480 --> 01:12:02,320
They could be waiting for us to trade,

1576
01:12:02,320 --> 01:12:04,020
and the moment they see it happening,

1577
01:12:04,250 --> 01:12:06,290
they could make their move.

1578
01:12:06,290 --> 01:12:07,620
Are you slightly bored?

1579
01:12:08,090 --> 01:12:10,390
I wanted to hear what people had to say,

1580
01:12:10,390 --> 01:12:13,330
and maybe our activities...

1581
01:12:13,330 --> 01:12:15,570
To be honest,
I feel like we're finally meeting...

1582
01:12:15,570 --> 01:12:17,030
- face-to-face.
- I know.

1583
01:12:17,030 --> 01:12:18,800
It's like we've been behind
closed doors up until now,

1584
01:12:18,800 --> 01:12:20,370
- and finally...
- After four days, right?

1585
01:12:20,370 --> 01:12:22,510
We're finally meeting face-to-face
and actually talking.

1586
01:12:22,510 --> 01:12:24,740
- We're talking now.
- I've finally been able...

1587
01:12:24,740 --> 01:12:26,480
- I know.
- to talk to everyone.

1588
01:12:26,740 --> 01:12:29,080
"Are people finally
coming up to me to talk?"

1589
01:12:29,080 --> 01:12:30,410
That's what I'm thinking now.

1590
01:12:30,880 --> 01:12:34,480
I'm finally able to talk to people
outside my team.

1591
01:12:34,480 --> 01:12:35,850
- Finally,
- Together...

1592
01:12:35,850 --> 01:12:39,090
we feel like you've accepted us,
which is nice.

1593
01:12:39,090 --> 01:12:40,090
I know.

1594
01:12:40,090 --> 01:12:41,190
You said that your wish...

1595
01:12:41,190 --> 01:12:43,160
- was to talk to everyone here.
- Seriously.

1596
01:12:43,160 --> 01:12:44,430
- What a good feeling.
- Talk away.

1597
01:12:44,430 --> 01:12:46,230
- Darn.
- I mean it.

1598
01:12:46,230 --> 01:12:49,730
- Together, right?
- I haven't been able to even talk to you,

1599
01:12:50,170 --> 01:12:51,800
and it came down to this.

1600
01:12:51,800 --> 01:12:54,940
- True.
- When the timing isn't right,

1601
01:12:54,940 --> 01:12:57,210
- there's nothing you can do.
- Sure.

1602
01:12:57,210 --> 01:13:02,250
I guess we should've
taken action a day or two earlier.

1603
01:13:02,250 --> 01:13:03,280
- True.
- Right.

1604
01:13:03,280 --> 01:13:04,510
I totally agree.

1605
01:13:06,750 --> 01:13:07,820
Should we just do it?

1606
01:13:15,690 --> 01:13:17,860
Maillard, maybe the leaders...

1607
01:13:17,860 --> 01:13:19,060
- should gather.
- Yes.

1608
01:13:19,330 --> 01:13:21,370
Should the leaders talk at lunchtime too?

1609
01:13:21,370 --> 01:13:22,400
Yes.

1610
01:13:23,100 --> 01:13:24,470
Am I invited too?

1611
01:13:24,470 --> 01:13:27,500
Well, that's...

1612
01:13:31,880 --> 01:13:34,380
We should limit it to those
who can use the Platform for now.

1613
01:13:34,380 --> 01:13:35,880
We need to trade our resources, you see.

1614
01:13:37,310 --> 01:13:38,520
I need to purchase lives.

1615
01:13:38,650 --> 01:13:39,780
Yes.

1616
01:13:39,780 --> 01:13:41,650
- I figured you'd need lives.
- True.

1617
01:13:41,820 --> 01:13:43,690
We should talk for a bit.

1618
01:13:47,360 --> 01:13:49,230
We should transfer the lives we got.

1619
01:13:50,560 --> 01:13:51,760
Distribute them, I mean.

1620
01:13:52,260 --> 01:13:53,930
- I'll clear out.
- Sure.

1621
01:13:58,100 --> 01:14:00,240
- I feel bad for her.
- Leia should be here.

1622
01:14:00,240 --> 01:14:01,870
Leia? I'll bring her over.

1623
01:14:09,650 --> 01:14:11,380
- We need to tail her.
- Right.

1624
01:14:11,880 --> 01:14:14,420
I've written down what we should trade.

1625
01:14:14,750 --> 01:14:16,350
If I give you this and our resources,

1626
01:14:16,350 --> 01:14:18,820
can you take care of all the trades?

1627
01:14:18,820 --> 01:14:20,590
- You need to hand over the resources.
- Right.

1628
01:14:20,590 --> 01:14:21,830
- Okay.
- Right.

1629
01:14:29,930 --> 01:14:31,600
- We should trade.
- That's right.

1630
01:14:32,540 --> 01:14:34,840
- In total...
- Just follow it exactly.

1631
01:14:35,040 --> 01:14:39,780
To execute the plan
we put together to perfection,

1632
01:14:39,780 --> 01:14:42,610
the resources have to change hands
without Team Gold finding out.

1633
01:14:42,610 --> 01:14:45,650
But Team Gold was occupying the Platform.

1634
01:14:45,650 --> 01:14:47,720
That's why I brought
the leaders together...

1635
01:14:47,720 --> 01:14:49,450
to move forward with the trade...

1636
01:14:49,450 --> 01:14:51,050
and trigger the war.

1637
01:14:51,690 --> 01:14:54,190
White, Blue, Red, and Black.

1638
01:14:54,190 --> 01:14:56,060
- Diamonds, life, and credit.
- Life and credit.

1639
01:14:56,660 --> 01:14:59,000
How many credits should I trade
and how many should I keep?

1640
01:14:59,300 --> 01:15:02,000
For the Platform to operate,
a direct exchange won't do.

1641
01:15:02,000 --> 01:15:04,100
I need to sell what I have,
buy what I need,

1642
01:15:04,100 --> 01:15:07,340
sell it to someone else,

1643
01:15:07,340 --> 01:15:08,870
and buy from them.

1644
01:15:08,870 --> 01:15:10,440
To set it at 50 million,

1645
01:15:10,440 --> 01:15:12,580
you need to give me 12.5 million diamonds.

1646
01:15:12,580 --> 01:15:14,850
Since the process is pretty complicated,

1647
01:15:14,850 --> 01:15:18,110
I just asked Maillard
for the final numbers.

1648
01:15:18,350 --> 01:15:21,890
With the Platform officially open,
I passed along the skill I was holding...

1649
01:15:21,890 --> 01:15:23,420
to Team Red.

1650
01:15:23,420 --> 01:15:25,460
- Is it Day Eight today?
- Yes.

1651
01:15:25,860 --> 01:15:27,520
This expires after Day Eight.

1652
01:15:27,520 --> 01:15:28,530
(Black sells Bomb Manufacturing License
to Red for 1 diamond.)

1653
01:15:29,190 --> 01:15:31,290
- Here.
- Darn.

1654
01:15:31,930 --> 01:15:33,560
(Platform Trade Summary:
White, Blue, Red, Black)

1655
01:15:33,560 --> 01:15:37,430
(Diamonds, Lives, Credits, Gold)

1656
01:15:37,430 --> 01:15:38,700
(Declaring war)

1657
01:15:38,700 --> 01:15:39,800
Good job, guys.

1658
01:15:40,270 --> 01:15:43,910
What if they make us lower our guard...

1659
01:15:44,140 --> 01:15:46,110
and strike Red or White?

1660
01:15:46,480 --> 01:15:48,110
If they do that, we'll just have to win.

1661
01:15:48,350 --> 01:15:50,550
- You never know.
- You're right.

1662
01:15:50,780 --> 01:15:52,150
I want to be safe.

1663
01:15:52,150 --> 01:15:53,580
You are. There's no need to worry.

1664
01:15:53,820 --> 01:15:55,190
- You're not safe.
- Here.

1665
01:15:55,350 --> 01:15:58,360
I'll be safe if they strike me,
but that's unlikely.

1666
01:15:58,360 --> 01:15:59,490
Exactly. Yes, that.

1667
01:15:59,890 --> 01:16:01,790
- It'll be a disaster if they hit red.
- Right.

1668
01:16:02,130 --> 01:16:03,660
We'd lose 25,000 dollars.

1669
01:16:08,170 --> 01:16:10,930
There wasn't a single moment
where I could lower my guard.

1670
01:16:10,930 --> 01:16:12,740
We didn't have that kind of luxury.

1671
01:16:12,740 --> 01:16:17,170
If Mokgye ever left the Platform,

1672
01:16:17,170 --> 01:16:21,580
I had to sprint to ensure
I reached the Community Center first.

1673
01:16:21,580 --> 01:16:23,710
That was how critical my situation was.

1674
01:16:23,710 --> 01:16:26,480
That's why I kept my eyes
on everything and everyone.

1675
01:16:26,480 --> 01:16:29,790
I checked Mokgye's position
and was wary of her movements.

1676
01:16:31,320 --> 01:16:33,360
We had a plan for today too.

1677
01:16:33,360 --> 01:16:35,530
We couldn't risk Team Gold discovering...

1678
01:16:35,530 --> 01:16:37,660
the trade taking place at the Platform...

1679
01:16:37,660 --> 01:16:40,160
or letting them declare war...

1680
01:16:40,160 --> 01:16:43,170
before we had time to react,

1681
01:16:43,170 --> 01:16:45,940
so it was my job to keep them...

1682
01:16:45,940 --> 01:16:47,300
engaged and occupied.

1683
01:16:47,300 --> 01:16:50,540
That's why I brought up various topics
to keep their attention focused on me.

1684
01:16:50,540 --> 01:16:52,710
I'm not at all curious about the past.

1685
01:16:56,510 --> 01:17:01,180
- Two hours into the trading session.
- Time flies when we're talking like this.

1686
01:17:01,180 --> 01:17:03,420
- I know.
- Has no one traded?

1687
01:17:03,420 --> 01:17:05,260
- You're here, so you haven't.
- They're trading right now.

1688
01:17:05,260 --> 01:17:06,390
We can't be a part of it though.

1689
01:17:10,160 --> 01:17:11,700
This is when I feel the most anxious...

1690
01:17:13,060 --> 01:17:14,360
and on edge.

1691
01:17:17,000 --> 01:17:19,900
If we're being honest,
we're currently ahead.

1692
01:17:20,800 --> 01:17:21,870
Circumstantially, I mean.

1693
01:17:22,540 --> 01:17:23,610
However,

1694
01:17:24,170 --> 01:17:26,140
I'm the most on edge.

1695
01:17:26,140 --> 01:17:27,140
I think...

1696
01:17:27,610 --> 01:17:30,810
that's because you have it
in your heart to win for sure...

1697
01:17:31,250 --> 01:17:32,250
and not halfheartedly.

1698
01:17:32,250 --> 01:17:33,450
That's true. You see,

1699
01:17:33,450 --> 01:17:35,490
up until Day Five,

1700
01:17:35,490 --> 01:17:37,050
I just loved the quizzes,

1701
01:17:37,320 --> 01:17:39,220
and I was having a blast.

1702
01:17:39,820 --> 01:17:41,190
Ever since that day,

1703
01:17:41,630 --> 01:17:45,530
it's been a real struggle and so draining.

1704
01:17:46,230 --> 01:17:49,600
Don't you think you had to fight
an unseen threat?

1705
01:17:51,370 --> 01:17:54,370
There wasn't anyone
who was actually a threat to us.

1706
01:17:54,940 --> 01:17:58,170
Even if there's no clear justification,
a clear victory might be of value.

1707
01:17:58,170 --> 01:17:59,980
In my case,

1708
01:17:59,980 --> 01:18:03,110
the only objective in my mind
is the survival of my teammates.

1709
01:18:03,510 --> 01:18:05,680
Either way, the reality check is real.

1710
01:18:05,920 --> 01:18:07,080
I absolutely agree.

1711
01:18:07,380 --> 01:18:08,790
What are we even fighting for?

1712
01:18:08,890 --> 01:18:11,820
We'll have to go to war soon,

1713
01:18:12,320 --> 01:18:13,320
and honestly,

1714
01:18:14,020 --> 01:18:16,590
it takes a heavy mental toll on me.

1715
01:18:17,160 --> 01:18:19,730
We can't avoid it, though, right?

1716
01:18:19,730 --> 01:18:21,200
Can you walk away from it?

1717
01:18:21,630 --> 01:18:23,970
It's like this. I mean,

1718
01:18:25,100 --> 01:18:26,540
it sounds a bit funny...

1719
01:18:26,540 --> 01:18:28,810
comparing it to the arms race
between the US and the Soviets,

1720
01:18:29,440 --> 01:18:31,070
but I fear I might be the target if not.

1721
01:18:31,240 --> 01:18:33,740
It's just like
the US and Cuba wondering...

1722
01:18:33,740 --> 01:18:35,850
which side is going to press
the nuclear button first.

1723
01:18:38,210 --> 01:18:40,420
Wait. Can you two...

1724
01:18:40,950 --> 01:18:43,390
I'm just afraid
someone will target me first.

1725
01:18:43,390 --> 01:18:47,190
- No one's a threat, but...
- Team Gold doesn't have that in mind.

1726
01:18:47,360 --> 01:18:50,730
No one's actively targeting me, but...

1727
01:18:53,300 --> 01:18:57,400
Are you going to activate your skill first
or declare war first?

1728
01:18:57,700 --> 01:18:58,740
The skill.

1729
01:18:58,840 --> 01:19:00,270
Going nuclear in this situation?

1730
01:19:02,570 --> 01:19:05,780
If you're going to use the skill,
you have to get moving.

1731
01:19:05,780 --> 01:19:06,940
- We'll go together.
- Sure.

1732
01:19:07,310 --> 01:19:09,250
I'll close the Platform then.

1733
01:19:23,290 --> 01:19:24,760
- I'm going right now.
- I'm going.

1734
01:19:24,760 --> 01:19:26,000
- Right now?
- Yes.

1735
01:19:26,060 --> 01:19:27,160
Let's go together.

1736
01:19:31,370 --> 01:19:33,300
- Are you going over there?
- Yes.

1737
01:19:33,740 --> 01:19:34,840
Okay.

1738
01:19:46,720 --> 01:19:48,420
It was hard to watch.

1739
01:19:49,050 --> 01:19:51,420
We were talking friendly
with them one minute,

1740
01:19:51,420 --> 01:19:54,190
only to wage war the next.

1741
01:19:55,460 --> 01:19:57,490
I wouldn't have made it
if I were on the other end of that.

1742
01:19:57,490 --> 01:20:00,500
(Leia, Journalist)

1743
01:20:00,500 --> 01:20:02,670
That's why I asked Maillard...

1744
01:20:02,670 --> 01:20:04,870
if this war was absolutely necessary.

1745
01:20:05,240 --> 01:20:08,070
At that moment,
even Maillard was sick of it too.

1746
01:20:08,270 --> 01:20:11,410
"Was it necessary to finish them off?"

1747
01:20:11,540 --> 01:20:14,640
But in Maillard's case,
he had already done the math.

1748
01:20:14,640 --> 01:20:18,480
This was necessary
to guarantee everyone's safety.

1749
01:20:18,750 --> 01:20:24,390
I thought it wouldn't hurt
to give the others a chance,

1750
