01:32:26,710 --> 01:32:29,480
Let's go up and have a talk
among ourselves as well, Ugong.

2011
01:32:29,480 --> 01:32:31,380
- Okay.
- Let's talk first.

2012
01:32:31,380 --> 01:32:32,820
- Let's go up.
- All right.

2013
01:32:32,820 --> 01:32:34,380
- Luna went up.
- She did?

2014
01:32:40,520 --> 01:32:42,060
We've entered a state of war.

2015
01:32:42,220 --> 01:32:45,330
All residents, please remain
in your dormitories.

2016
01:32:45,390 --> 01:32:47,900
Since they're saying...

2017
01:32:48,000 --> 01:32:49,130
all that,

2018
01:32:50,300 --> 01:32:51,300
it doesn't feel good.

2019
01:32:53,940 --> 01:32:57,370
- I'm against fighting back.
- What?

2020
01:32:57,370 --> 01:32:58,740
- You're against entering the war?
- Yes.

2021
01:32:58,740 --> 01:32:59,780
- That's...
- Why?

2022
01:32:59,780 --> 01:33:01,080
- It's pointless.
- what I'm thinking as well.

2023
01:33:01,080 --> 01:33:02,180
Wouldn't it be fun?

2024
01:33:02,180 --> 01:33:03,980
- No, but...
- It's not about the fun.

2025
01:33:03,980 --> 01:33:06,180
I don't want us to be their toy.

2026
01:33:06,180 --> 01:33:08,650
- We'll consider it a loss.
- We'll consider it a loss.

2027
01:33:08,650 --> 01:33:10,590
- Let's just go home.
- That sounds good.

2028
01:33:11,550 --> 01:33:13,960
I really think it's an unnecessary war.

2029
01:33:13,960 --> 01:33:14,960
Me too.

2030
01:33:15,190 --> 01:33:16,190
It wasn't necessary.

2031
01:33:17,690 --> 01:33:19,630
They started a war
because they were anxious.

2032
01:33:20,300 --> 01:33:23,330
I understand Maillard's standards.

2033
01:33:24,400 --> 01:33:27,300
"It's not right to leave
even the slightest possibility open."

2034
01:33:28,070 --> 01:33:29,070
But...

2035
01:33:31,070 --> 01:33:34,540
But judging from their attitudes,
they never thought about going to war.

2036
01:33:34,540 --> 01:33:36,010
I totally agree with that.

2037
01:33:36,480 --> 01:33:37,780
The bomb? I agree.

2038
01:33:38,050 --> 01:33:40,050
They could have stopped there.

2039
01:33:40,380 --> 01:33:43,650
- That's what I think.
- They're saying that's more hypocritical.

2040
01:33:43,650 --> 01:33:45,550
- That it's crueler. But...
- Right.

2041
01:33:46,120 --> 01:33:49,290
But that's...

2042
01:33:49,730 --> 01:33:50,830
a bit of a stretch.

2043
01:33:50,830 --> 01:33:52,900
They had no intention
of going to war anyway.

2044
01:33:53,500 --> 01:33:55,400
We couldn't stop them...

2045
01:33:56,470 --> 01:33:58,400
In fact, we joined them.

2046
01:33:58,400 --> 01:33:59,400
Right.

2047
01:34:01,100 --> 01:34:03,070
We could have blocked them
with our bodies...

2048
01:34:03,070 --> 01:34:05,770
if they were going to enter
to start the war.

2049
01:34:06,480 --> 01:34:08,010
It wouldn't have been too late
to do it then.

2050
01:34:09,080 --> 01:34:11,050
It was too rash.

2051
01:34:14,720 --> 01:34:15,850
Well...

2052
01:34:25,590 --> 01:34:27,200
What should I say?

2053
01:34:35,740 --> 01:34:36,740
Let's not cry.

2054
01:34:36,740 --> 01:34:37,740
Yes.

2055
01:34:45,510 --> 01:34:48,580
This is what I'm mad about.

2056
01:34:49,250 --> 01:34:50,750
I wouldn't have minded...

2057
01:34:50,750 --> 01:34:52,250
if we could all survive when we win.

2058
01:34:52,250 --> 01:34:53,960
"One of you should leave."

2059
01:34:53,960 --> 01:34:56,030
That also doesn't make sense.

2060
01:34:56,360 --> 01:34:58,330
There's one thing I regret.

2061
01:34:58,630 --> 01:35:00,800
Things would have been neat...

2062
01:35:00,800 --> 01:35:02,200
if we had just accepted it...

2063
01:35:02,200 --> 01:35:04,130
when they asked.

2064
01:35:04,500 --> 01:35:07,340
It was our mistake for not doing that.

2065
01:35:07,340 --> 01:35:10,210
We were always one step behind too.

2066
01:35:10,470 --> 01:35:13,410
But there was a reason
we were always a step behind.

2067
01:35:13,410 --> 01:35:14,940
- Right.
- We came later.

2068
01:35:14,940 --> 01:35:17,350
- Right. Yes.
- We had to figure out the situation...

2069
01:35:17,350 --> 01:35:19,280
- with limited information.
- Of course.

2070
01:35:19,280 --> 01:35:20,980
The rules and the situation here...

2071
01:35:20,980 --> 01:35:22,480
We had to figure out
people's personalities.

2072
01:35:22,480 --> 01:35:23,490
- So...
- Everything was...

2073
01:35:23,490 --> 01:35:25,450
we could only follow along
with their decisions...

2074
01:35:25,450 --> 01:35:28,190
while guessing from the outside,

2075
01:35:28,190 --> 01:35:29,220
- honestly speaking.
- Right.

2076
01:35:29,220 --> 01:35:31,330
About issues like Donkey's.

2077
01:35:31,330 --> 01:35:32,960
They never told us.

2078
01:35:32,960 --> 01:35:34,860
- Right.
- We could have done something...

2079
01:35:34,860 --> 01:35:37,430
if they told us things
because they wanted something.

2080
01:35:38,570 --> 01:35:40,140
I'm glad we came as the catfish.

2081
01:35:40,140 --> 01:35:41,700
That says how good we are.

2082
01:35:43,110 --> 01:35:44,210
As expected.

2083
01:35:44,210 --> 01:35:45,270
That's a compliment.

2084
01:35:45,710 --> 01:35:48,410
They overprepared like that...

2085
01:35:48,410 --> 01:35:50,850
because we looked strong,
so they were trying to defend themselves.

2086
01:35:50,850 --> 01:35:53,680
They kept asking what skills we had.

2087
01:35:53,680 --> 01:35:56,190
- They think we're hiding something. Yes.
- They kept thinking that.

2088
01:35:56,190 --> 01:35:58,490
That's why they kept trying
to eliminate us...

2089
01:35:58,490 --> 01:36:00,660
and tried not to leave any chances.

2090
01:36:01,490 --> 01:36:02,760
I can understand them, though.

2091
01:36:03,490 --> 01:36:05,090
It's disappointing in many ways,

2092
01:36:05,090 --> 01:36:08,500
but we did really well.

2093
01:36:08,930 --> 01:36:10,930
Let's consider this a good experience.

2094
01:36:10,930 --> 01:36:13,070
- Let's keep it neat.
- Right.

2095
01:36:13,070 --> 01:36:15,900
Let's not leave while they mock us.

2096
01:36:15,900 --> 01:36:19,010
I want us to leave...

2097
01:36:19,710 --> 01:36:20,880
after declaring defeat.

2098
01:36:21,340 --> 01:36:23,210
I think that's the best we can do.

2099
01:36:23,210 --> 01:36:24,280
Declaring defeat.

2100
01:36:24,280 --> 01:36:26,520
That alone can say...

2101
01:36:26,520 --> 01:36:28,580
what a terrible thing they did...

2102
01:36:28,580 --> 01:36:31,690
and how they crushed our spirit.

2103
01:36:31,690 --> 01:36:34,390
They can think about that.

2104
01:36:34,690 --> 01:36:36,460
In the end...

2105
01:36:37,130 --> 01:36:38,190
Well...

2106
01:36:38,430 --> 01:36:39,900
We don't have lives,

2107
01:36:40,200 --> 01:36:42,100
and we have to go home today.

2108
01:36:42,530 --> 01:36:46,240
But one of us has no other choice...

2109
01:36:46,740 --> 01:36:47,970
than to stay here.

2110
01:36:48,640 --> 01:36:50,540
I want to take responsibility...

2111
01:36:51,070 --> 01:36:52,270
as the leader...

2112
01:36:52,410 --> 01:36:55,280
and stay behind to vote.

2113
01:36:56,980 --> 01:36:59,410
I think
if the original, new Gold member...

2114
01:36:59,720 --> 01:37:04,020
stays here until the end,

2115
01:37:05,350 --> 01:37:07,520
they'll think they won.

2116
01:37:09,290 --> 01:37:12,190
But if I stay behind...

2117
01:37:12,960 --> 01:37:15,160
I was an original member as well.

2118
01:37:16,100 --> 01:37:17,900
I would stay here until the end,

2119
01:37:17,900 --> 01:37:20,900
but I would be the only one leaving
with no prize.

2120
01:37:21,700 --> 01:37:23,670
I think we need to show them that...

2121
01:37:24,640 --> 01:37:27,080
so they could think...

2122
01:37:27,780 --> 01:37:29,380
- about what they did.
- But...

2123
01:37:29,380 --> 01:37:30,980
honestly speaking,

2124
01:37:30,980 --> 01:37:34,650
it breaks my heart
to leave behind our youngest member.

2125
01:37:35,120 --> 01:37:37,690
And from a humanitarian perspective,

2126
01:37:37,690 --> 01:37:41,190
that's an incredibly irresponsible thing
for adults to do.

2127
01:37:41,190 --> 01:37:42,460
- So...
- I'm saying,

2128
01:37:42,460 --> 01:37:44,330
if one person has to stay behind,

2129
01:37:44,330 --> 01:37:45,760
that has to be me.

2130
01:37:45,760 --> 01:37:48,160
- Right. That's a bit...
- Since I'm an original member.

2131
01:37:48,160 --> 01:37:49,900
"What did you do?"

2132
01:37:49,900 --> 01:37:53,300
"You teamed up with the original members,"

2133
01:37:53,300 --> 01:37:56,340
"but in the end, you singled out
one of the original members."

2134
01:37:56,340 --> 01:37:57,870
That's the message I want to send.

2135
01:38:02,010 --> 01:38:03,810
So will you stay behind?

2136
01:38:03,810 --> 01:38:04,980
- Can you do that?
- Okay.

2137
01:38:04,980 --> 01:38:06,950
- Yes.
- We'll exit.

2138
01:38:07,480 --> 01:38:08,480
So, this...

2139
01:38:09,020 --> 01:38:10,920
shakes your identity.

2140
01:38:10,920 --> 01:38:12,020
Right.

2141
01:38:12,020 --> 01:38:16,290
You'll get the thought,
"Am I really the villain?"

2142
01:38:16,290 --> 01:38:20,000
"Am I being rejected
because I'm the villain..."

2143
01:38:20,000 --> 01:38:22,700
"and I did bad things?"
Your identity gets shaken.

2144
01:38:22,700 --> 01:38:26,300
Your sense of identity.

2145
01:38:26,500 --> 01:38:30,570
There's nothing you can do to solve that,

2146
01:38:30,570 --> 01:38:31,910
but you keep...

2147
01:38:32,170 --> 01:38:34,780
having to clear up misunderstandings
and resolve things.

2148
01:38:34,780 --> 01:38:36,780
You keep getting discouraged,

2149
01:38:37,450 --> 01:38:39,410
so you end up giving up.

2150
01:38:40,950 --> 01:38:44,990
We didn't live our lives
based on other people's opinions so far.

2151
01:38:44,990 --> 01:38:48,820
The way I see myself. That...

2152
01:38:50,490 --> 01:38:51,790
was the standard.

2153
01:38:54,300 --> 01:38:55,660
But that's shaking.

2154
01:38:59,370 --> 01:39:00,940
That was hard.

2155
01:39:00,940 --> 01:39:04,210
But I really enjoyed being with you.

2156
01:39:05,470 --> 01:39:06,480
It was nice.

2157
01:39:08,840 --> 01:39:11,210
I didn't come here for this.

2158
01:39:11,210 --> 01:39:14,750
Ugong said he felt like
this wasn't the fight he had in mind.

2159
01:39:14,750 --> 01:39:18,590
He thought we were fighting
a different battle.

2160
01:39:18,590 --> 01:39:20,820
I agreed with him.

2161
01:39:20,820 --> 01:39:24,190
I think the reason I came
to that realization as late as I did...

2162
01:39:24,190 --> 01:39:26,530
was because
I was one of the original members.

2163
01:39:26,530 --> 01:39:30,600
So I could understand
why they made the decisions they did.

2164
01:39:30,600 --> 01:39:32,430
I could have done the same thing...

2165
01:39:32,430 --> 01:39:35,440
in their shoes.

2166
01:39:35,740 --> 01:39:37,810
While listening to Ugong,

2167
01:39:37,940 --> 01:39:40,880
I could really understand
how frustrating and hard...

2168
01:39:40,980 --> 01:39:44,410
it would have been
to be rejected as enemies...

2169
01:39:44,580 --> 01:39:46,480
just because we joined later...

2170
01:39:46,480 --> 01:39:50,950
when I put myself in their shoes.

2171
01:39:51,390 --> 01:39:54,020
I just felt sorry.

2172
01:39:54,720 --> 01:39:56,960
I felt bad.

2173
01:39:56,960 --> 01:39:58,960
(Luna, Influencer)

2174
01:39:58,960 --> 01:40:01,260
So we didn't want...

2175
01:40:01,460 --> 01:40:03,970
to let them have the satisfaction...

2176
01:40:04,370 --> 01:40:08,740
of winning a pointless war
until the very end.

2177
01:40:09,140 --> 01:40:13,680
We decided to declare defeat today.

2178
01:40:42,270 --> 01:40:44,210
Team Gold is heading down.

2179
01:40:44,940 --> 01:40:46,140
Why?

2180
01:40:46,140 --> 01:40:49,240
They're heading down with their resources.

2181
01:40:49,240 --> 01:40:50,250
What?

2182
01:40:50,510 --> 01:40:51,510
What's going on?

2183
01:40:51,580 --> 01:40:53,880
What are they doing as a group?

2184
01:41:00,260 --> 01:41:01,260
Where are they going?

2185
01:41:01,490 --> 01:41:03,360
What's going on?

2186
01:41:04,860 --> 01:41:05,860
What's going on?

2187
01:41:06,260 --> 01:41:07,330
Declaring defeat?

2188
01:41:08,660 --> 01:41:09,660
What?

2189
01:41:09,660 --> 01:41:10,930
Aren't they declaring defeat?

2190
01:41:17,240 --> 01:41:18,640
- That's Luna.
- Right.

2191
01:41:18,910 --> 01:41:19,910
Right.

2192
01:41:43,270 --> 01:41:44,630
Get in there and do your thing, Mokgye.

2193
01:42:00,920 --> 01:42:03,450
We declare defeat in this war.

2194
01:42:03,450 --> 01:42:06,820
(Team Blue has declared war on Team Gold.)

2195
01:42:06,820 --> 01:42:09,190
The declaration of defeat
has been confirmed.

2196
01:42:10,590 --> 01:42:13,460
Team Blue has won the war.

2197
01:42:14,060 --> 01:42:18,600
Please submit your spoils into the slot.

2198
01:42:25,870 --> 01:42:26,880
It's here.

2199
01:42:45,530 --> 01:42:47,700
(Transfer of spoils)

2200
01:42:47,700 --> 01:42:50,130
The spoils have been
successfully submitted.

2201
01:42:52,070 --> 01:42:55,570
Please select the final survivor.

2202
01:42:58,770 --> 01:43:00,110
The final survivor...

2203
01:43:01,110 --> 01:43:02,310
is Luna.

2204
01:43:06,580 --> 01:43:09,890
Team Gold's final survivor
has been chosen.

2205
01:43:10,220 --> 01:43:12,290
You may now exit.

2206
01:43:24,030 --> 01:43:25,330
- Are you done?
- I'm done.

2207
01:43:25,330 --> 01:43:26,330
- Good job.
- Good job.

2208
01:43:26,330 --> 01:43:28,970
- Good job.
- I made Luna the final survivor.

2209
01:43:28,970 --> 01:43:31,510
- Thank you.
- Please do well until the end.

2210
01:43:31,510 --> 01:43:32,510
- Okay.
- Okay.

2211
01:43:32,510 --> 01:43:34,240
- Our mom.
- It'll be painful for just one more day.

2212
01:43:34,240 --> 01:43:35,310
- Right.
- Right.

2213
01:43:35,540 --> 01:43:37,380
- I'll do my best.
- Good luck.

2214
01:43:37,510 --> 01:43:39,280
- Let's go. Good work, everyone.
- Let's go.

2215
01:43:39,280 --> 01:43:41,050
- Good work, everyone.
- Good work, everyone.

2216
01:43:46,490 --> 01:43:47,660
I'm so sad.

2217
01:43:50,360 --> 01:43:53,630
(Team Gold's Mokgye, Ugong, Maetel
leave the town.)

2218
01:44:06,240 --> 01:44:09,010
This is an announcement
from the Community Center.

2219
01:44:10,550 --> 01:44:12,710
Due to Team Gold's declaration of defeat,

2220
01:44:12,850 --> 01:44:15,650
Team Blue has won the war.

2221
01:44:16,790 --> 01:44:20,090
Effective immediately,
the state of war has been lifted.

2222
01:44:20,090 --> 01:44:21,490
Oh, I'm stressed.

2223
01:44:21,490 --> 01:44:25,160
All functions of the Community Town
are back to normal.

2224
01:44:32,570 --> 01:44:33,670
Effective immediately,

2225
01:44:33,670 --> 01:44:35,770
- the state of war has been lifted.
- Oh, my gosh.

2226
01:44:35,840 --> 01:44:38,110
All functions of the Community Town...

2227
01:44:38,110 --> 01:44:40,280
- are back to normal.
- Oh, my gosh.

2228
01:44:44,950 --> 01:44:46,510
This is the worst.

2229
01:44:50,590 --> 01:44:52,650
So they're all going home except one.

2230
01:44:52,850 --> 01:44:54,120
They're saying they can't handle a war.

2231
01:44:56,290 --> 01:44:57,330
Well...

2232
01:44:59,160 --> 01:45:01,100
- I can understand.
- Right.

2233
01:45:02,700 --> 01:45:03,770
We pushed them into a corner.

2234
01:45:04,630 --> 01:45:06,970
We did try to hit them again
when they were already...

2235
01:45:06,970 --> 01:45:08,370
pushed into a corner and down.

2236
01:45:10,170 --> 01:45:11,710
- But why?
- Team Blue...

2237
01:45:11,710 --> 01:45:13,580
has won the war.

2238
01:45:13,980 --> 01:45:15,480
Leader of Team Blue,

2239
01:45:15,480 --> 01:45:18,350
please collect the spoils from the Center.

2240
01:45:30,490 --> 01:45:34,330
Leader of Team Blue,
please collect the spoils from the Center.

2241
01:45:52,280 --> 01:45:54,780
The spoils have been collected.

2242
01:45:55,580 --> 01:45:56,650
This doesn't feel right.

2243
01:46:00,020 --> 01:46:03,430
(Team Blue collects the spoils.)

2244
01:46:09,630 --> 01:46:10,930
It feels a bit anticlimactic.

2245
01:46:11,370 --> 01:46:13,740
It feels like I'm leaving...

2246
01:46:14,440 --> 01:46:15,940
without getting to do anything.

2247
01:46:16,470 --> 01:46:18,170
There are many moments I regret.

2248
01:46:18,170 --> 01:46:19,810
Actually, we had some chances,

2249
01:46:19,810 --> 01:46:22,840
but I don't think
we were able to act on those chances.

2250
01:46:23,310 --> 01:46:26,280
It's not easy to persuade people.

2251
01:46:26,450 --> 01:46:29,580
It's not easy to change the world.

2252
01:46:30,150 --> 01:46:31,690
I felt so once again.

2253
01:46:32,390 --> 01:46:36,560
I think I'll live with more respect
for those who create change.

2254
01:46:38,230 --> 01:46:40,100
Our smart Luna.

2255
01:46:40,660 --> 01:46:42,560
Do your best until the end.

2256
01:46:43,800 --> 01:46:47,070
You did so well. You were so cool.

2257
01:46:47,200 --> 01:46:48,200
Thank you.

2258
01:46:49,000 --> 01:46:50,110
It feels...

2259
01:46:51,140 --> 01:46:54,410
like I was just in my room
and didn't get to do much.

2260
01:46:54,410 --> 01:46:56,110
I'm kind of sad about that.

2261
01:46:56,850 --> 01:46:59,510
I think we had...

2262
01:47:00,480 --> 01:47:02,580
many members who thought things through...

2263
01:47:02,580 --> 01:47:04,750
and were careful about making decisions.

2264
01:47:05,490 --> 01:47:08,690
In a way, it could be
because we're all too smart.

2265
01:47:08,690 --> 01:47:11,060
We pictured the chessboards in our minds,

2266
01:47:11,260 --> 01:47:14,200
trying to find the correct answer.

2267
01:47:14,330 --> 01:47:16,830
I guess that took a long time.

2268
01:47:17,300 --> 01:47:20,400
But looking at this community...

2269
01:47:20,400 --> 01:47:21,740
In the end,

2270
01:47:21,800 --> 01:47:24,570
even when great ideas...

2271
01:47:24,570 --> 01:47:26,710
or legislation are brought forth,

2272
01:47:26,980 --> 01:47:28,810
people in society move...

2273
01:47:28,940 --> 01:47:32,950
depending on how something is marketed...

2274
01:47:33,150 --> 01:47:36,220
and how you sway public opinion
to present an idea.

2275
01:47:36,420 --> 01:47:38,590
I think, in a way,

2276
01:47:38,590 --> 01:47:42,290
we're leaving like this
because we're hoping...

2277
01:47:42,290 --> 01:47:44,230
people understand how we were thinking.

2278
01:47:44,760 --> 01:47:47,030
I should've communicated...

2279
01:47:47,030 --> 01:47:49,960
a bit faster and more proactively.

2280
01:47:50,430 --> 01:47:54,170
But I was so late. I regretted that a lot.

2281
01:47:54,300 --> 01:47:57,210
Would it have been better...

2282
01:47:57,210 --> 01:47:59,270
if I communicated more proactively?

2283
01:47:59,470 --> 01:48:01,980
Or would it not have made
much of a difference?

2284
01:48:01,980 --> 01:48:05,410
Many thoughts came up in my head.

2285
01:48:05,510 --> 01:48:08,650
There are many worlds I didn't know about.

2286
01:48:08,650 --> 01:48:10,950
I mean, I'm just a nerd.

2287
01:48:10,950 --> 01:48:14,560
But I guess being here was nice.

2288
01:48:14,760 --> 01:48:16,990
Yes, it was nice to get to talk...

2289
01:48:17,590 --> 01:48:19,690
to a diverse group of people.

2290
01:48:21,930 --> 01:48:23,000
(Leia, Paul)

2291
01:48:23,000 --> 01:48:24,070
(Pitou, Siseon, Donkey,
Maillard, Izaha, Vector)

2292
01:48:24,070 --> 01:48:25,230
(Maetel, Ugong, Mokgye)

2293
01:48:26,170 --> 01:48:31,340
(Luna)

2294
01:48:38,280 --> 01:48:40,520
- Can we have a quick chat, Luna?
- Sure.

2295
01:48:40,820 --> 01:48:41,880
Just a quick chat.

2296
01:48:44,120 --> 01:48:48,260
Can you tell me a bit
about how you made your decision?

2297
01:48:48,460 --> 01:48:50,230
Well, first...

2298
01:48:50,560 --> 01:48:53,560
We don't know why everyone is...

2299
01:48:53,560 --> 01:48:55,200
taking things this far.

2300
01:48:55,960 --> 01:48:59,330
We already knew we were going to lose.

2301
01:48:59,330 --> 01:49:01,340
Because our final strategy...

2302
01:49:01,470 --> 01:49:04,210
was to persuade White somehow.

2303
01:49:05,110 --> 01:49:07,080
Our defeat has already been decided.

2304
01:49:07,280 --> 01:49:08,910
So why did everyone keep attacking...

2305
01:49:09,640 --> 01:49:10,680
Right.

2306
01:49:11,450 --> 01:49:14,750
There was no reason to,
so why did everyone keep attacking us?

2307
01:49:15,950 --> 01:49:18,420
This is just ridicule at this point.

2308
01:49:18,990 --> 01:49:21,460
"If you win,
we'll give you one more life."

2309
01:49:21,460 --> 01:49:23,260
What nonsense.

2310
01:49:23,420 --> 01:49:25,530
We had no reason to fight,
so that's why we left.

2311
01:49:26,590 --> 01:49:29,100
There's nothing for us to gain
through war.

2312
01:49:30,300 --> 01:49:32,800
We didn't want a war.

2313
01:49:33,300 --> 01:49:37,370
Every time, someone else
has declared war on me.

2314
01:49:37,770 --> 01:49:40,070
Of course, maybe I was too late.

2315
01:49:40,070 --> 01:49:42,810
I could've started the war.

2316
01:49:43,140 --> 01:49:45,310
Maybe I was letting it happen.

2317
01:49:46,850 --> 01:49:49,820
Anyway, I don't like
having people declare war against me.

2318
01:49:51,190 --> 01:49:55,660
If there was even a small chance
that we could win the war,

2319
01:49:55,920 --> 01:49:58,890
I'd fight passionately.
That's what a player should do.

2320
01:49:58,890 --> 01:50:00,900
But it was already decided.

2321
01:50:06,570 --> 01:50:07,870
But everyone...

2322
01:50:08,770 --> 01:50:10,970
keeps acting like Gold is the enemy.

2323
01:50:11,310 --> 01:50:14,280
But Gold didn't do anything wrong.

2324
01:50:16,640 --> 01:50:18,980
If we did anything wrong,

2325
01:50:20,050 --> 01:50:21,520
it was that we didn't move quickly.

2326
01:50:23,180 --> 01:50:26,250
We may seem strong,
but everyone was struggling a lot.

2327
01:50:27,190 --> 01:50:28,620
You didn't let us do anything.

2328
01:50:29,260 --> 01:50:31,390
We tried to trade, but we couldn't.

2329
01:50:32,030 --> 01:50:34,130
We tried to form alliances,
but we couldn't.

2330
01:50:35,800 --> 01:50:37,230
You could say...

2331
01:50:38,170 --> 01:50:40,300
they were all strategic failures...

2332
01:50:40,300 --> 01:50:42,140
or mistakes in judgment.

2333
01:50:42,500 --> 01:50:45,410
So that's why I acknowledged all of that.

2334
01:50:46,440 --> 01:50:48,110
I accepted defeat.

2335
01:50:51,250 --> 01:50:55,220
I know those actions stemmed from fear.

2336
01:50:56,280 --> 01:50:58,750
I also know
those actions stemmed from concern.

2337
01:50:58,750 --> 01:51:01,690
But we didn't have the capacity
to be understanding of all of that.

2338
01:51:01,690 --> 01:51:02,860
We just...

2339
01:51:03,660 --> 01:51:05,090
kept getting beat down.

2340
01:51:06,330 --> 01:51:08,730
So everyone decided to leave.

2341
01:51:09,430 --> 01:51:10,730
But in any case,

2342
01:51:11,900 --> 01:51:13,800
one person has to stay.

2343
01:51:14,570 --> 01:51:18,040
I told them I wanted to do that.

2344
01:51:20,540 --> 01:51:22,440
I wanted to stay...

2345
01:51:22,440 --> 01:51:25,210
to show the original members...

2346
01:51:27,650 --> 01:51:29,420
that they didn't have to take things
this far.

2347
01:51:33,820 --> 01:51:36,060
Everyone is getting prize money except me.

2348
01:51:36,160 --> 01:51:37,830
I wanted to tell everyone that.

2349
01:51:43,730 --> 01:51:44,830
I completely understand.

2350
01:51:51,170 --> 01:51:52,240
First of all,

2351
01:51:54,740 --> 01:51:55,940
I'm so sorry.

2352
01:51:58,350 --> 01:51:59,380
About this situation.

2353
01:52:02,480 --> 01:52:05,090
I couldn't stop them.

2354
01:52:05,590 --> 01:52:07,360
White did join in.

2355
01:52:07,360 --> 01:52:08,920
I did join in.

2356
01:52:10,630 --> 01:52:11,960
Up until yesterday, yes,

2357
01:52:11,960 --> 01:52:15,000
the war was partially about survival.

2358
01:52:16,200 --> 01:52:17,970
But today's war,

2359
01:52:22,300 --> 01:52:25,040
being completely honest,
had no justification.

2360
01:52:27,080 --> 01:52:28,710
If there was a justification,

2361
01:52:29,810 --> 01:52:32,950
it was Maillard's judgment
that we needed...

2362
01:52:33,250 --> 01:52:35,220
to remove the last unforeseen risk.

2363
01:52:36,750 --> 01:52:39,090
Those repeated thoughts...

2364
01:52:39,920 --> 01:52:42,490
of mistrust of the other side...

2365
01:52:43,420 --> 01:52:47,200
made us want to be sure.

2366
01:52:48,200 --> 01:52:50,930
I still did think it was too cruel.

2367
01:52:51,900 --> 01:52:55,440
But at the bottom of it, you're right.

2368
01:52:58,410 --> 01:52:59,570
It was a war...

2369
01:53:01,940 --> 01:53:04,150
that left us with absolutely nothing.

2370
01:53:11,920 --> 01:53:14,020
My heart feels so heavy.

2371
01:53:14,590 --> 01:53:16,020
But surrendering...

2372
01:53:16,020 --> 01:53:18,460
is something that happens
in an actual war.

2373
01:53:18,760 --> 01:53:22,130
Also, Ugong strongly wanted
to declare defeat.

2374
01:53:22,130 --> 01:53:23,300
- You're right.
- You're right.

2375
01:53:23,560 --> 01:53:25,270
- It must've been frustrating.
- Of course.

2376
01:53:25,270 --> 01:53:26,670
Because things didn't go
the way they wanted.

2377
01:53:27,030 --> 01:53:29,570
I was with them for the first time.

2378
01:53:29,740 --> 01:53:33,340
They had lost all motivation
to start a war...

2379
01:53:33,340 --> 01:53:35,540
- by lunchtime.
- They lost their motivation.

2380
01:53:36,280 --> 01:53:37,710
Oh, gosh. It's a bit...

2381
01:53:38,450 --> 01:53:39,880
I agreed with using the bomb.

2382
01:53:40,010 --> 01:53:43,750
I agreed with blocking them
from doing anything with the bomb.

2383
01:53:43,750 --> 01:53:44,750
But...

2384
01:53:45,190 --> 01:53:48,190
I am thinking it was a bit rash.

2385
01:53:48,760 --> 01:53:50,190
We think,

2386
01:53:50,190 --> 01:53:52,830
"You had a chance,
but you turned it down."

2387
01:53:52,830 --> 01:53:56,100
But for them, they could think,
"We haven't been here for long,"

2388
01:53:56,100 --> 01:53:57,970
"and we had no information,"

2389
01:53:57,970 --> 01:53:59,900
"so we can't make that judgment."

2390
01:53:59,900 --> 01:54:01,940
"If you see things that way,"

2391
01:54:01,940 --> 01:54:04,670
"we feel wronged."
They could protest like that.

2392
01:54:04,840 --> 01:54:07,480
For example, if you look
at declaring defeat or surrender...

2393
01:54:07,480 --> 01:54:09,910
as an action you take...

2394
01:54:09,910 --> 01:54:11,410
to lessen the damages of war,

2395
01:54:11,580 --> 01:54:13,010
this doesn't have that benefit.

2396
01:54:13,010 --> 01:54:14,350
Because you lose resources all the same.

2397
01:54:14,350 --> 01:54:16,250
Exactly, it's the same amount of damage.

2398
01:54:16,580 --> 01:54:20,420
The fact
that they didn't even try to win...

2399
01:54:20,890 --> 01:54:22,390
- is regrettable.
- Right.

2400
01:54:22,390 --> 01:54:23,720
There's nothing we can do.

2401
01:54:23,720 --> 01:54:25,360
We can't fix that feeling
we have about each other.

2402
01:54:25,360 --> 01:54:27,730
My heart keeps going back and forth.

2403
01:54:27,930 --> 01:54:28,930
"I get it."

2404
01:54:28,930 --> 01:54:30,900
"But that was still not it."

2405
01:54:30,900 --> 01:54:32,770
- I keep going back and forth like that.
- I feel...

2406
01:54:32,770 --> 01:54:35,740
a bit bad, but I'm also mad.

2407
01:54:35,900 --> 01:54:36,970
There's nothing we can do.

2408
01:54:37,140 --> 01:54:38,940
How is Leia?
I'm worried about how she's feeling.

2409
01:54:38,940 --> 01:54:40,780
- She's completely out of it.
- Oh, no.

2410
01:54:40,780 --> 01:54:42,210
- Seriously.
- Seriously.

2411
01:54:43,140 --> 01:54:45,550
- I'm going to go see Leia.
- Go ahead.

2412
01:54:45,550 --> 01:54:46,580
Okay.

2413
01:54:47,920 --> 01:54:49,920
A lot was said.

2414
01:54:50,480 --> 01:54:52,890
I said,
"I don't think a war is necessary."

2415
01:54:53,190 --> 01:54:54,990
"No, we need to make it clearer."

2416
01:54:54,990 --> 01:54:58,260
"And that's the polite thing to do."
Some people said that.

2417
01:55:00,230 --> 01:55:01,330
I don't know.

2418
01:55:02,430 --> 01:55:04,530
I'm sorry to say this,

2419
01:55:05,300 --> 01:55:06,930
but there was a lot
that could've been done.

2420
01:55:07,300 --> 01:55:09,540
For example, you could've tried
to appease them more...

2421
01:55:09,540 --> 01:55:11,340
before lunchtime.

2422
01:55:11,540 --> 01:55:12,910
"Give us a chance to buy weapons,
at least."

2423
01:55:12,910 --> 01:55:14,140
You could've done anything.

2424
01:55:14,340 --> 01:55:15,780
But this is what you did.

2425
01:55:15,780 --> 01:55:17,780
"Since we're obviously going to lose,
let's surrender."

2426
01:55:18,150 --> 01:55:20,210
"Let's ruin everything." Doing that...

2427
01:55:20,580 --> 01:55:21,850
I'm so sorry,

2428
01:55:22,120 --> 01:55:24,890
but I really think
that was rude to everyone.

2429
01:55:28,120 --> 01:55:31,430
You prevented us
from doing all of the things...

2430
01:55:31,630 --> 01:55:33,160
we tried to do in this game.

2431
01:55:33,160 --> 01:55:37,270
Isn't the reason you think
we didn't do our best...

2432
01:55:38,270 --> 01:55:41,970
that you didn't see
all of the things we tried to do?

2433
01:55:42,100 --> 01:55:43,270
- That could be the case.
- Yes.

2434
01:55:43,400 --> 01:55:44,810
- But...
- In the majority alliance,

2435
01:55:44,810 --> 01:55:46,170
you said some things happened.

2436
01:55:46,170 --> 01:55:47,740
There were some attempts at persuasion,

2437
01:55:47,740 --> 01:55:49,380
some failures, some reattempts.

2438
01:55:49,380 --> 01:55:51,550
- You said you tried many things.
- Yes.

2439
01:55:51,550 --> 01:55:53,050
But to us, it didn't seem like that.

2440
01:55:53,050 --> 01:55:55,550
To us, it was loosening up the game.

2441
01:55:55,650 --> 01:55:57,250
To us, that seemed rude.

2442
01:55:57,250 --> 01:55:58,250
That's a difference in perspective.

2443
01:55:58,250 --> 01:56:00,590
We each did our best...

2444
01:56:00,590 --> 01:56:02,690
- in the groups we were a part of.
- Fine.

2445
01:56:02,890 --> 01:56:04,430
So that's why we did that.

2446
01:56:04,430 --> 01:56:05,690
So if you say from a position of power,

2447
01:56:05,690 --> 01:56:08,030
"You could've begged more."

2448
01:56:08,030 --> 01:56:09,430
"You could've done this or that."

2449
01:56:09,430 --> 01:56:11,830
"You ran away without doing anything
like cowards."

2450
01:56:11,830 --> 01:56:13,400
If you say that...

2451
01:56:14,570 --> 01:56:15,740
That's too...

2452
01:56:16,700 --> 01:56:17,770
Too...

2453
01:56:18,640 --> 01:56:20,640
Don't you think that's too cruel?

2454
01:56:20,640 --> 01:56:22,580
- You're in such a superior position.
- You're right.

2455
01:56:24,850 --> 01:56:27,480
- But I really...
- You're part of such a majority.

2456
01:56:27,950 --> 01:56:29,750
You were never in the minority...

2457
01:56:29,750 --> 01:56:32,190
where you couldn't do anything.

2458
01:56:32,190 --> 01:56:33,550
That's not true.

2459
01:56:33,990 --> 01:56:35,260
I was White.

2460
01:56:35,990 --> 01:56:37,790
What did we try our best to do then?

2461
01:56:38,130 --> 01:56:39,390
Three of us died.

2462
01:56:39,630 --> 01:56:41,030
I even volunteered to die.

2463
01:56:43,900 --> 01:56:45,570
We accepted that result.

2464
01:56:46,230 --> 01:56:49,970
So are you saying, "We declared war,"

2465
01:56:50,070 --> 01:56:52,910
"and you didn't even try
to form an alliance..."

2466
01:56:53,010 --> 01:56:55,210
- You didn't even try to win.
- "or try to really fight?"

2467
01:56:55,210 --> 01:56:56,680
"You just left."

2468
01:56:56,680 --> 01:56:58,980
Are you blaming us for doing that?

2469
01:56:59,210 --> 01:57:00,680
I'm saying we're just disappointed.

2470
01:57:00,680 --> 01:57:02,250
- Disappointed?
- Yes.

2471
01:57:04,590 --> 01:57:06,720
Then I have nothing else to say.

2472
01:57:06,720 --> 01:57:08,360
- I think I said everything...
- Wait.

2473
01:57:08,360 --> 01:57:09,860
I needed to say to Leia.

2474
01:57:09,860 --> 01:57:11,630
This really isn't right, Leia.

2475
01:57:12,260 --> 01:57:13,830
- Listen.
- What am I supposed to say here?

2476
01:57:13,830 --> 01:57:14,900
- I understand.
- But...

2477
01:57:15,030 --> 01:57:16,100
- Wait. Everyone.
- No.

2478
01:57:16,100 --> 01:57:17,100
- I really...
- I understand.

2479
01:57:17,100 --> 01:57:18,930
I'm not trying to get you to make up.

2480
01:57:18,930 --> 01:57:20,370
I'm not trying to mediate.

2481
01:57:20,470 --> 01:57:23,570
- Everyone has their own perspective.
- Right.

2482
01:57:23,570 --> 01:57:25,970
- They had their own reasons...
- Right.

2483
01:57:25,970 --> 01:57:27,440
- for making that choice.
- Right.

2484
01:57:27,440 --> 01:57:28,740
- I'm sorry if I was too aggressive.
- Let's not...

2485
01:57:28,740 --> 01:57:30,680
- judge her right now.
- Okay.

2486
01:57:30,680 --> 01:57:33,310
We were just here...

2487
01:57:33,310 --> 01:57:34,780
- to share our own thoughts.
- Okay.

2488
01:57:34,780 --> 01:57:35,920
- Okay?
- Yes.

2489
01:57:35,920 --> 01:57:37,520
- So, right now...
- Yes.

2490
01:57:37,920 --> 01:57:40,820
But we don't have anything
to talk about anymore, right?

2491
01:57:41,260 --> 01:57:42,960
- We have nothing to talk about.
- Why not?

2492
01:57:42,960 --> 01:57:44,890
Can't we discuss the future?

2493
01:57:44,890 --> 01:57:46,230
That's over.

2494
01:57:46,230 --> 01:57:48,030
Please explain that to him, Leia.

2495
01:57:48,300 --> 01:57:51,070
I don't know what to say anymore.

2496
01:58:20,490 --> 01:58:22,200
Siseon said things to me...

2497
01:58:22,930 --> 01:58:24,770
that I felt like Team Red would say.

2498
01:58:25,170 --> 01:58:27,300
I thought it was Maillard talking.

2499
01:58:27,300 --> 01:58:29,600
(Luna, Influencer)

2500
01:58:29,600 --> 01:58:30,940
How could he berate me then...

2501
01:58:30,940 --> 01:58:32,610
I mean, how could he think that way?

2502
01:58:32,610 --> 01:58:36,310
"Oh, he really can't think
from someone else's perspective..."

2503
01:58:36,440 --> 01:58:40,310
"because he's so ingrained
in being part of that group."

2504
01:58:40,550 --> 01:58:43,220
When Siseon was on Team White
in the beginning,

2505
01:58:43,220 --> 01:58:45,590
he was so different from me...

2506
01:58:45,590 --> 01:58:48,320
in that he wanted peace for everyone.

2507
01:58:48,320 --> 01:58:50,660
I was the one saying,
"It's only important that we live."

2508
01:58:50,660 --> 01:58:53,190
The way Siseon is now.

2509
01:58:53,190 --> 01:58:55,060
Since I was the leader and all.

2510
01:58:55,130 --> 01:58:57,430
But seeing him like that now...

2511
01:58:57,800 --> 01:58:59,700
It's not that I felt that he had changed,

2512
01:58:59,800 --> 01:59:02,770
but I did think,
"People are weaker than situations."

2513
01:59:03,200 --> 01:59:05,840
I felt so resigned.

2514
01:59:06,110 --> 01:59:08,710
So I resent Siseon now.

2515
01:59:14,320 --> 01:59:15,380
I'm sorry.

2516
01:59:17,490 --> 01:59:19,890
But I honestly do feel that way.

2517
01:59:20,720 --> 01:59:22,660
- I think it was irresponsible.
- Okay.

2518
01:59:23,160 --> 01:59:25,060
But I don't think
it was the right time to say so.

2519
01:59:25,060 --> 01:59:26,860
Okay. I got it.

2520
01:59:26,860 --> 01:59:27,860
Okay.

2521
01:59:34,640 --> 01:59:36,100
They were so close.

2522
01:59:36,340 --> 01:59:41,210
Luna was the leader of Team White.

2523
01:59:41,640 --> 01:59:44,550
I was the bad cop.
Siseon was the good cop.

2524
01:59:44,550 --> 01:59:45,950
Luna balanced us.

2525
01:59:46,050 --> 01:59:48,880
The other team members
fought hard in their own ways too.

2526
01:59:48,880 --> 01:59:51,420
Hamlet would quietly share his thoughts.

2527
01:59:51,420 --> 01:59:53,220
Boss would be running around.

2528
01:59:53,420 --> 01:59:55,060
Paul would be running around.

2529
01:59:55,390 --> 01:59:57,420
We have those memories with Luna.

2530
01:59:58,060 --> 02:00:01,230
Seeing them like that
in a different situation...

2531
02:00:01,230 --> 02:00:03,300
The situation itself was sad.

2532
02:00:03,300 --> 02:00:09,970
(Leia, Journalist)

2533
02:00:10,470 --> 02:00:12,370
I didn't control my emotions well.

2534
02:00:12,370 --> 02:00:13,540
(Siseon, Gender equality activist)

2535
02:00:13,540 --> 02:00:16,340
There's a right time to say something,

2536
02:00:16,510 --> 02:00:17,980
but I chose the wrong time.

2537
02:00:18,350 --> 02:00:22,080
I feel really bad,
and I want to apologize.

2538
02:00:23,750 --> 02:00:25,820
- I said I'd respect her decision.
- Sounds good.

2539
02:00:26,690 --> 02:00:27,720
Good job.

2540
02:00:28,990 --> 02:00:30,460
That must've been hard on you, Leia.

2541
02:00:31,190 --> 02:00:32,890
I did choose this side.

2542
02:00:33,590 --> 02:00:35,860
Anyway, now that it's been decided...

2543
02:00:35,860 --> 02:00:37,430
- Yes.
- It's been decided.

2544
02:00:37,570 --> 02:00:40,730
But, now that I think about it,

2545
02:00:41,340 --> 02:00:42,800
- the diamonds won.
- Right.

2546
02:00:42,800 --> 02:00:44,770
- Right? We won, guys.
- Yes.

2547
02:00:47,140 --> 02:00:49,380
I'm sorry,
but you can't let your guard down.

2548
02:00:51,480 --> 02:00:52,550
Leia.

2549
02:00:59,720 --> 02:01:01,860
Leia, this is what's going to happen.

2550
02:01:02,420 --> 02:01:05,060
Thinking about that
makes me want to vomit.

2551
02:01:05,060 --> 02:01:06,730
- Why?
- Don't overthink it.

2552
02:01:06,730 --> 02:01:09,530
If you do so...

2553
02:01:33,150 --> 02:01:34,190
(Maillard, Cooking YouTuber)

2554
02:01:34,190 --> 02:01:35,560
Then, I wondered,

2555
02:01:36,290 --> 02:01:37,630
"Were my actions..."

2556
02:01:38,330 --> 02:01:43,930
"too focused on winning?"

2557
02:01:44,670 --> 02:01:45,700
"Was it..."

2558
02:01:46,430 --> 02:01:48,070
"too unfair?"

2559
02:01:49,100 --> 02:01:53,010
"Did I really deprive them..."

2560
02:01:53,010 --> 02:01:56,480
"of any ways to take action
the past few days?"

2561
02:01:56,740 --> 02:02:00,180
All of these thoughts
went through my head.

2562
02:02:01,380 --> 02:02:04,750
I did those things...

2563
02:02:05,050 --> 02:02:06,790
for the victory of our alliance,

2564
02:02:07,490 --> 02:02:08,690
but I thought...

2565
02:02:09,520 --> 02:02:11,890
I got too obsessed...

2566
02:02:12,830 --> 02:02:14,560
and greedy.

2567
02:02:15,660 --> 02:02:17,930
Processing those thoughts...

2568
02:02:18,070 --> 02:02:19,730
took some time.

2569
02:02:35,280 --> 02:02:37,850
Maillard's decisions were so aggressive.

2570
02:02:37,850 --> 02:02:38,990
He's coming.

2571
02:02:40,920 --> 02:02:42,790
I must've gotten way too obsessed.

2572
02:02:43,090 --> 02:02:45,030
- No, but that's the right thing to do.
- But if this were reality...

2573
02:02:45,030 --> 02:02:46,560
- You did your best.
- Yes.

2574
02:02:46,730 --> 02:02:48,730
I think I got too obsessed.

2575
02:02:48,730 --> 02:02:50,060
- But this is...
- I get that you're torn.

2576
02:02:50,060 --> 02:02:51,300
I think it taught us a lesson
that too much of a good thing...

2577
02:02:51,300 --> 02:02:52,700
is not always good.

2578
02:02:52,700 --> 02:02:55,140
I brought ruin upon myself
by being too greedy too.

2579
02:02:55,270 --> 02:02:56,940
But we weren't too greedy...

2580
02:02:56,940 --> 02:02:58,940
We were just preventing unknown risks.

2581
02:02:58,940 --> 02:03:00,070
- Right.
- No.

2582
02:03:00,070 --> 02:03:03,680
I feel like I should've at least
given them some breathing room.

2583
02:03:14,820 --> 02:03:17,360
They did have a way
to do some damage on us today.

2584
02:03:17,420 --> 02:03:18,760
- Right.
- During the trade,

2585
02:03:18,760 --> 02:03:19,760
they could've run over here.

2586
02:03:19,760 --> 02:03:20,760
- Run over and...
- But I...

2587
02:03:20,760 --> 02:03:22,200
I even thought about that.

2588
02:03:22,200 --> 02:03:23,760
- Because...
- That's why...

2589
02:03:23,760 --> 02:03:26,570
I was extra anxious then.

2590
02:03:26,570 --> 02:03:27,940
I even thought about that.

2591
02:03:27,940 --> 02:03:29,640
What if I had fallen on my way over here?

2592
02:03:29,640 --> 02:03:32,410
What if Mokgye went in first
and waged war?

2593
02:03:33,070 --> 02:03:34,840
- If that happened...
- I don't know. I really...

2594
02:03:35,410 --> 02:03:36,610
I have no idea, though.

2595
02:03:37,010 --> 02:03:38,080
Thank you for your work.

2596
02:03:38,350 --> 02:03:39,880
Gosh, this is really...

2597
02:03:40,550 --> 02:03:42,680
But Maillard, you did a good job.

2598
02:03:42,680 --> 02:03:44,950
Right. We were being smart.

2599
02:03:45,890 --> 02:03:48,190
Only Team Red has all members alive now.

2600
02:03:48,190 --> 02:03:49,190
I know.

2601
02:03:55,960 --> 02:03:57,730
It's time for dinner.

2602
02:03:58,270 --> 02:04:00,070
- Do you want to eat something?
- We need a meal.

2603
02:04:00,170 --> 02:04:01,840
This party celebrates war.

2604
02:04:01,970 --> 02:04:03,370
I've wanted to have this at least once.

2605
02:04:03,370 --> 02:04:04,570
Hi.

2606
02:04:04,570 --> 02:04:06,340
- Hi.
- Thank you for your work.

2607
02:04:06,570 --> 02:04:08,410
We really look so devious.

2608
02:04:09,010 --> 02:04:11,580
We're like psychopaths
who enjoy a meal after winning a war.

2609
02:04:11,580 --> 02:04:12,710
- We use swear words.
- Right.

2610
02:04:12,710 --> 02:04:14,250
- Cheers.
- Thank you for your work.

2611
02:04:14,250 --> 02:04:16,220
- You've been through a lot.
- Cheers.

2612
02:04:16,280 --> 02:04:17,920
- We did our best.
- Thank you for your work.

2613
02:04:17,920 --> 02:04:19,020
Good.

2614
02:04:19,720 --> 02:04:22,220
I just wanted to feed them,

2615
02:04:22,220 --> 02:04:24,360
so I was grilling some meat
standing next to them.

2616
02:04:24,730 --> 02:04:25,730
Still,

2617
02:04:25,960 --> 02:04:28,260
while eating and talking,

2618
02:04:28,500 --> 02:04:31,630
everyone looked relaxed,
and the mood lightened up.

2619
02:04:32,830 --> 02:04:34,400
So I was relieved.

2620
02:04:36,940 --> 02:04:37,940
I'm completely drained.

2621
02:04:38,270 --> 02:04:40,640
I'm so out of it,
I don't even know what I'm eating.

2622
02:04:40,640 --> 02:04:41,640
Still, you ate quite a lot.

2623
02:04:41,640 --> 02:04:42,840
I do know I'm eating something.

2624
02:04:43,110 --> 02:04:44,110
You do know?

2625
02:04:44,110 --> 02:04:46,150
I've been eating well here all the time.

2626
02:04:46,350 --> 02:04:48,150
Even after killing my team members,
I ate well the next day.

2627
02:04:48,150 --> 02:04:49,150
It's all right.

2628
02:04:49,150 --> 02:04:50,720
I hope I can leave here
with the prize money in my hands.

2629
02:04:50,980 --> 02:04:52,020
We never know.

2630
02:04:55,920 --> 02:04:58,560
This is an announcement
from the Community Center.

2631
02:04:58,730 --> 02:05:02,060
The leader negotiation will be held soon.

2632
02:05:02,160 --> 02:05:04,470
Since Team Gold's leader left,

2633
02:05:04,470 --> 02:05:06,530
Luna, the final survivor,

2634
02:05:06,530 --> 02:05:08,340
automatically has become the leader,

2635
02:05:08,870 --> 02:05:10,540
for your information.

2636
02:05:11,310 --> 02:05:12,440
(Sighing)

2637
02:05:12,440 --> 02:05:14,240
Gosh, I have to go
to the leader negotiation?

2638
02:05:15,640 --> 02:05:18,010
This is an absolute nightmare.

2639
02:05:21,080 --> 02:05:22,080
Goodness.

2640
02:05:23,950 --> 02:05:25,290
I shouldn't have said
that I wanted to stay.

2641
02:05:27,620 --> 02:05:28,690
Shall we drop by?

2642
02:05:30,320 --> 02:05:31,430
Is everyone really gone?

2643
02:05:38,830 --> 02:05:40,000
Luna.

2644
02:05:40,000 --> 02:05:41,470
- Have you eaten?
- Yes.

2645
02:05:41,670 --> 02:05:42,940
- Did you have the leftovers?
- Yes.

2646
02:05:42,940 --> 02:05:45,240
I thought it would be nice
if you had something warm.

2647
02:05:45,310 --> 02:05:46,770
I'm fine.

2648
02:05:46,770 --> 02:05:48,610
Still, take this, just in case.

2649
02:05:48,780 --> 02:05:50,440
- It's okay.
- What?

2650
02:05:51,910 --> 02:05:52,980
See you later.

2651
02:05:52,980 --> 02:05:54,410
- See you. Are you all right?
- Yes.

2652
02:05:54,410 --> 02:05:55,420
I'm okay.

2653
02:06:00,390 --> 02:06:01,920
She needs some time.

2654
02:06:02,860 --> 02:06:04,360
She needs to eat to carry on.

2655
02:06:05,190 --> 02:06:07,190
We just wanted to make a living,
but it ended up like this.

2656
02:06:09,600 --> 02:06:13,530
The last leader negotiation
will be held soon.

2657
02:06:14,100 --> 02:06:18,470
All team leaders, please gather
at the Community Center.

2658
02:06:19,510 --> 02:06:21,480
I'm so wasted on beer.
I've got nothing to lose.

2659
02:06:21,480 --> 02:06:22,480
That's nice.

2660
02:06:22,480 --> 02:06:23,910
If you mess with me, you're all dead meat.

2661
02:06:23,910 --> 02:06:26,050
Right. Darn it, stop it now.

2662
02:06:26,050 --> 02:06:28,580
- Stop it, please.
- Leave our Leia alone.

2663
02:06:29,580 --> 02:06:32,150
Don't start getting interesting
right when it's time to leave.

2664
02:06:45,430 --> 02:06:47,170
(Occupied: Please wait.)

2665
02:06:47,430 --> 02:06:50,370
The thought of seeing Luna
makes me scared.

2666
02:06:50,870 --> 02:06:52,910
Gosh, it's been a long day.

2667
02:06:52,910 --> 02:06:54,310
This is the last night here.

2668
02:06:54,310 --> 02:06:55,840
Right. It's the last leader negotiation.

2669
02:06:56,040 --> 02:06:57,610
But I feel...

2670
02:06:58,110 --> 02:06:59,780
like something is missing. Why?

2671
02:07:02,880 --> 02:07:04,320
- Hi.
- Hello.

2672
02:07:04,320 --> 02:07:05,590
Isn't Team Gold's leader coming?

2673
02:07:05,890 --> 02:07:07,520
- She should come.
- She's going to be here.

2674
02:07:23,540 --> 02:07:25,110
- Give me 1,250 dollars.
- Stop it.

2675
02:07:25,270 --> 02:07:26,410
I want to lose.

2676
02:07:26,670 --> 02:07:28,310
Take out the last digit for real.

2677
02:07:30,110 --> 02:07:31,350
Hello.

2678
02:07:32,980 --> 02:07:33,980
Hello.

2679
02:07:36,850 --> 02:07:38,720
All leaders,

2680
02:07:38,720 --> 02:07:41,290
stand at the designated spot, please.

2681
02:07:41,960 --> 02:07:44,790
The last leader negotiation...

2682
02:07:45,360 --> 02:07:47,660
will now begin.

2683
02:08:07,180 --> 02:08:10,320
After Luna entered,
there was silence for a while.

2684
02:08:10,780 --> 02:08:13,120
Due to various situations
that have happened so far,

2685
02:08:13,290 --> 02:08:14,620
we kept silence, I guess.

2686
02:08:22,030 --> 02:08:24,670
First, here's the pollution index...

2687
02:08:24,670 --> 02:08:26,700
for the entire Community Town.

2688
02:08:26,830 --> 02:08:29,140
The total pollution index
accumulated over the past eight days...

2689
02:08:29,240 --> 02:08:31,200
is 79.

2690
02:08:31,470 --> 02:08:35,180
Until Day Nine,
when every schedule is over,

2691
02:08:35,180 --> 02:08:39,110
the total amount of normal credit
hasn't reached 100.

2692
02:08:40,150 --> 02:08:43,550
You succeeded in maintaining
the stable pollution index.

2693
02:08:45,050 --> 02:08:49,020
Today, you'll have
the last leader negotiation.

2694
02:08:49,420 --> 02:08:53,490
The negotiation on aid and sanctions,
the last agenda, will be held.

2695
02:08:58,730 --> 02:09:03,140
Team Red requests a diamond aid
from Team Blue.

2696
02:09:07,210 --> 02:09:08,210
I agree.

2697
02:09:09,880 --> 02:09:11,850
- I agree.
- I agree.

2698
02:09:12,810 --> 02:09:14,820
The decision on the aid has been made.

2699
02:09:15,420 --> 02:09:17,750
The leader of the team to provide aid,

2700
02:09:18,090 --> 02:09:21,020
please insert the resources into the slot.

2701
02:09:22,020 --> 02:09:24,290
From Team Red to Team Blue,

2702
02:09:24,290 --> 02:09:27,130
a total of 12,500,096 diamonds
are provided as aid.

2703
02:09:29,600 --> 02:09:30,700
I was dumbfounded.

2704
02:09:30,700 --> 02:09:34,100
I realized everyone
shared it down to the penny.

2705
02:09:34,770 --> 02:09:38,570
The resources are showing
in both teams' resource screens.

2706
02:09:39,710 --> 02:09:41,710
All negotiations are complete.

2707
02:09:41,940 --> 02:09:45,450
We'll move on to today's life submission.

2708
02:10:04,730 --> 02:10:06,830
It really weighs on my mind.

2709
02:10:07,130 --> 02:10:08,900
She should submit the life left.

2710
02:10:09,970 --> 02:10:11,970
No, she doesn't have to.
I took it from her.

2711
02:10:12,370 --> 02:10:14,010
She only had one.

2712
02:10:14,140 --> 02:10:15,410
She only had one, and it was taken?

2713
02:10:15,410 --> 02:10:17,280
I threw the bomb.

2714
02:10:17,280 --> 02:10:18,280
Right.

2715
02:10:18,850 --> 02:10:21,450
It weighs on my mind even more
because Luna is the one left.

2716
02:10:21,450 --> 02:10:24,750
That's why Luna said she wanted to stay.

2717
02:10:25,350 --> 02:10:26,420
Why?

2718
02:10:27,320 --> 02:10:29,990
She wanted us to see
that she was left behind.

2719
02:10:30,360 --> 02:10:31,360
She did?

2720
02:10:31,730 --> 02:10:33,730
- Yes.
- She's mad at us, so she's doing that.

2721
02:10:37,030 --> 02:10:39,430
Please check the contents
of the central box...

2722
02:10:39,430 --> 02:10:43,270
and assign lives
to the residents of your choice.

2723
02:10:45,070 --> 02:10:48,280
(The last survivor of Team Blue: Pitou)

2724
02:10:53,880 --> 02:10:57,050
Still, all members of my team survived,
just like my original goal.

2725
02:10:57,150 --> 02:10:58,150
We succeeded.

2726
02:10:58,750 --> 02:11:00,290
I don't care about the prize money.

2727
02:11:00,720 --> 02:11:01,890
(Life Submission for Day 8)

2728
02:11:01,890 --> 02:11:03,490
(The last survivors of Team Red:
Donkey, Maillard, Izaha, Siseon)

2729
02:11:04,260 --> 02:11:06,330
Please check the contents
of the central box...

2730
02:11:06,660 --> 02:11:10,360
and assign lives
to the residents of your choice.

2731
02:11:14,000 --> 02:11:16,040
(Life Submission for Day 8)

2732
02:11:24,210 --> 02:11:26,550
When I submitted the last life,

2733
02:11:26,550 --> 02:11:29,520
(Leia, Journalist)

2734
02:11:29,520 --> 02:11:32,920
I had to pick Paul, and then me,

2735
02:11:34,590 --> 02:11:37,890
and the reality hit me hard.

2736
02:11:41,560 --> 02:11:43,700
Was it the only solution?

2737
02:11:44,000 --> 02:11:46,930
I don't think either side is to blame...

2738
02:11:46,930 --> 02:11:48,440
for things getting this far out of hand.

2739
02:11:49,270 --> 02:11:52,010
The idea crossed my mind...

2740
02:11:53,140 --> 02:11:56,640
that I wanted to stop.

2741
02:12:09,490 --> 02:12:11,420
Team White submits its lives.

2742
02:12:12,460 --> 02:12:14,560
Still, surviving to the end...

2743
02:12:14,560 --> 02:12:16,500
is building trust in myself.

2744
02:12:16,900 --> 02:12:19,200
So I submitted the lives as I planned
and left.

2745
02:12:21,300 --> 02:12:23,940
Your life submission is complete.

2746
02:12:23,940 --> 02:12:25,840
(The last survivors of Team White:
Leia and Paul)

2747
02:12:28,810 --> 02:12:29,880
You've been through a lot.

2748
02:12:31,280 --> 02:12:34,210
Without a problem
and according to my plan,

2749
02:12:34,210 --> 02:12:35,620
I submitted the lives.

2750
02:12:36,520 --> 02:12:38,350
Luna didn't say anything.

2751
02:12:38,550 --> 02:12:40,620
- During the sanction too?
- She said nothing.

2752
02:12:40,790 --> 02:12:42,290
- She...
- Did she just go back alone?

2753
02:12:42,720 --> 02:12:43,790
She entered,

2754
02:12:45,490 --> 02:12:46,560
stood there...

2755
02:12:46,890 --> 02:12:48,030
saying nothing,

2756
02:12:48,800 --> 02:12:50,560
and just left after everything ended.

2757
02:12:50,560 --> 02:12:52,000
She didn't have to submit life.

2758
02:12:53,830 --> 02:12:54,900
Goodness.

2759
02:12:59,710 --> 02:13:01,340
I felt so conflicted.

2760
02:13:01,740 --> 02:13:03,680
She was alone suffering,

2761
02:13:03,680 --> 02:13:06,780
and that image...

2762
02:13:07,150 --> 02:13:10,220
broke my heart so much.

2763
02:13:14,960 --> 02:13:15,960
That's how I felt.

2764
02:13:16,490 --> 02:13:17,560
It broke my heart.

2765
02:13:52,760 --> 02:13:54,660
The announcement on the last day...

2766
02:13:54,760 --> 02:13:56,830
was sent to the dormitory.

2767
02:13:57,400 --> 02:14:00,770
Please check the announcement
at the dormitory.

2768
02:14:03,800 --> 02:14:04,870
Here it is.

2769
02:14:05,410 --> 02:14:06,670
Here's the announcement.

2770
02:14:10,240 --> 02:14:11,380
Gosh, I...

2771
02:14:12,150 --> 02:14:13,550
can't lose this game.

2772
02:14:14,980 --> 02:14:18,650
Tomorrow is the final voting day
for the Community Town.

2773
02:14:18,950 --> 02:14:21,990
I will announce the schedule
for the last day.

2774
02:14:23,020 --> 02:14:24,060
First,

2775
02:14:24,320 --> 02:14:27,260
the last leader reappointment
will be conducted.

2776
02:14:29,000 --> 02:14:30,530
After the leader reappointment ends,

2777
02:14:30,530 --> 02:14:32,600
the resource distribution
per team will take place.

2778
02:14:32,600 --> 02:14:34,400
We have time for distribution.

2779
02:14:34,500 --> 02:14:35,670
Second,

2780
02:14:35,670 --> 02:14:37,470
the last leader selected...

2781
02:14:37,470 --> 02:14:39,510
should visit the Community Center...

2782
02:14:39,710 --> 02:14:41,710
distribute all diamonds, gold pieces,
lives, and credits...

2783
02:14:41,710 --> 02:14:46,080
that exist as resources for each team...

2784
02:14:46,150 --> 02:14:49,650
to individual residents,
leaving nothing behind.

2785
02:14:50,250 --> 02:14:53,420
The result of the distribution
will be revealed to each dormitory.

2786
02:14:54,190 --> 02:14:56,520
- So leaders distribute those.
- Yes.

2787
02:14:56,920 --> 02:14:58,460
Getting them out of the war...

2788
02:14:59,330 --> 02:15:00,430
was huge.

2789
02:15:00,430 --> 02:15:02,060
Otherwise, I would have been...

2790
02:15:02,330 --> 02:15:03,900
a little anxious.

2791
02:15:08,070 --> 02:15:09,100
Let me see.

2792
02:15:09,470 --> 02:15:10,800
This is the absolute highlight.

2793
02:15:11,340 --> 02:15:12,810
After resource distribution...

2794
02:15:12,870 --> 02:15:16,180
Third, residents who received
the resources distributed...

2795
02:15:16,340 --> 02:15:21,150
are given one last chance for relocation.

2796
02:15:21,310 --> 02:15:23,750
Then the personal resources distributed...

2797
02:15:23,750 --> 02:15:25,550
can be taken along for relocation.

2798
02:15:26,220 --> 02:15:29,660
Fourth, after that,
Team White and Team Gold...

2799
02:15:29,660 --> 02:15:32,130
will issue the last resources.

2800
02:15:32,960 --> 02:15:34,860
- "After that."
- They can mess with it...

2801
02:15:34,860 --> 02:15:36,900
- at the end.
- Team White can do that.

2802
02:15:37,130 --> 02:15:39,730
Team White and Team Gold
will issue currency...

2803
02:15:39,730 --> 02:15:41,940
for the last time before the last vote...

2804
02:15:41,940 --> 02:15:43,840
for one time.

2805
02:15:44,070 --> 02:15:46,670
Since it's after distribution
for individuals,

2806
02:15:46,770 --> 02:15:49,680
it will be distributed
as soon as it's issued.

2807
02:15:49,780 --> 02:15:51,440
The currency issued...

2808
02:15:51,440 --> 02:15:54,180
will be distributed only
to the residents of those teams.

2809
02:15:54,780 --> 02:15:56,550
The resources distributed
will be announced...

2810
02:15:56,550 --> 02:15:58,280
to the dormitory of those teams,

2811
02:15:58,380 --> 02:15:59,990
and the amount of gold pieces issued...

2812
02:15:59,990 --> 02:16:02,590
can be checked at every dormitory.

2813
02:16:02,590 --> 02:16:04,260
(The amount of gold pieces finally issued)

2814
02:16:04,320 --> 02:16:06,060
The amount of gold
is revealed, but not mine.

2815
02:16:06,060 --> 02:16:08,060
- Right.
- It's whether I'm trusted or not.

2816
02:16:08,160 --> 02:16:09,300
If they don't trust me,

2817
02:16:09,300 --> 02:16:10,530
- Yes.
- they could all issue gold.

2818
02:16:10,530 --> 02:16:12,530
So, if Team White's leader...

2819
02:16:12,630 --> 02:16:14,770
blows it out of proportion,

2820
02:16:14,770 --> 02:16:16,140
the only one who can betray
everyone else...

2821
02:16:16,140 --> 02:16:17,740
and move on...

2822
02:16:17,740 --> 02:16:19,070
- is Team White's leader.
- That's right.

2823
02:16:19,210 --> 02:16:21,670
They gave the leader
one last chance to backstab.

2824
02:16:21,670 --> 02:16:22,940
Team White's leader...

2825
02:16:23,110 --> 02:16:24,240
What's happening?

2826
02:16:24,580 --> 02:16:25,910
I'm the one pulling the strings.

2827
02:16:29,150 --> 02:16:30,280
Fifth,

2828
02:16:30,320 --> 02:16:32,490
a vote will be conducted
so that diamonds or gold pieces...

2829
02:16:32,490 --> 02:16:35,660
will be received as the final prize.

2830
02:16:36,060 --> 02:16:39,160
The resource selected by the majority
in the last vote...

2831
02:16:39,160 --> 02:16:40,990
will be chosen as the prize.

2832
02:16:41,860 --> 02:16:44,560
The resource decided
will be converted into Korean won...

2833
02:16:44,930 --> 02:16:47,900
and will be paid out based on
each individual's holdings,

2834
02:16:48,800 --> 02:16:51,870
and the resource not chosen will vanish.

2835
02:16:53,240 --> 02:16:56,410
I will explain the final voting format.

2836
02:16:56,640 --> 02:16:59,510
In the Community Town, one life equals...

2837
02:16:59,510 --> 02:17:01,850
the life of a single resident.

2838
02:17:01,920 --> 02:17:05,920
Every resident is given one base vote.

2839
02:17:06,450 --> 02:17:08,620
Per life that each resident possesses,

2840
02:17:08,620 --> 02:17:11,890
one extra vote is given.

2841
02:17:12,990 --> 02:17:14,830
- Yes.
- You got it right.

2842
02:17:14,830 --> 02:17:17,000
So, doing it this way
was correct after all.

2843
02:17:17,000 --> 02:17:18,230
Goodness, Maillard.

2844
02:17:18,230 --> 02:17:20,370
- Maillard, your prophecy is insane.
- I know.

2845
02:17:20,430 --> 02:17:21,570
It's one life.

2846
02:17:22,540 --> 02:17:25,340
During the final vote, residents...

2847
02:17:25,510 --> 02:17:27,510
can purchase
the offensive and defensive rights...

2848
02:17:27,510 --> 02:17:29,210
for your values code...

2849
02:17:29,210 --> 02:17:31,280
and use them immediately.

2850
02:17:31,340 --> 02:17:33,910
I knew it. There's no way
we wouldn't use the values card.

2851
02:17:34,380 --> 02:17:36,750
Per one credit, you can purchase...

2852
02:17:36,920 --> 02:17:40,120
one offensive or defensive right.

2853
02:17:40,390 --> 02:17:42,090
After your credits are used up,

2854
02:17:42,190 --> 02:17:45,890
you can make an additional purchase
using diamonds or gold pieces.

2855
02:17:46,190 --> 02:17:50,230
However, the cost for additional purchases
will be deducted from the total prize.

2856
02:17:50,730 --> 02:17:52,570
If the values codes of the resident...

2857
02:17:52,570 --> 02:17:55,130
targeted by the offensive right
are guessed correctly,

2858
02:17:55,670 --> 02:17:58,870
that resident will be stripped...

2859
02:17:58,870 --> 02:18:00,640
of both the base
and the additional voting rights.

2860
02:18:00,640 --> 02:18:02,180
(The offensive right)

2861
02:18:02,280 --> 02:18:05,080
Each defensive right negates
one successful offensive right...

2862
02:18:05,080 --> 02:18:07,850
executed against the holder.

2863
02:18:09,020 --> 02:18:12,420
Multiple offensive
and defensive rights can be used...

2864
02:18:12,720 --> 02:18:14,750
and regardless of when they're used,

2865
02:18:14,750 --> 02:18:18,060
they will be applied in a lump sum
after all voting is over.

2866
02:18:18,990 --> 02:18:20,760
Who has many credits left?

2867
02:18:20,960 --> 02:18:21,960
It's Pitou.

2868
02:18:21,960 --> 02:18:24,830
Pitou originally had 2, and won 3
as the spoils of war, so 5 in total.

2869
02:18:24,960 --> 02:18:27,170
- She can attack five times.
- I see.

2870
02:18:27,430 --> 02:18:28,700
How many credits do I have?

2871
02:18:29,370 --> 02:18:30,870
How many for each?

2872
02:18:31,700 --> 02:18:33,410
Now, Team Blue...

2873
02:18:33,410 --> 02:18:34,840
- has a lot of resources.
- Resources.

2874
02:18:35,170 --> 02:18:38,010
Is it possible to have
many defensive rights?

2875
02:18:38,010 --> 02:18:40,210
Yes, you can have them
as many as your credits.

2876
02:18:40,480 --> 02:18:42,220
Honestly, between us,

2877
02:18:42,220 --> 02:18:44,480
there's no reason to attack and defend.

2878
02:18:44,580 --> 02:18:45,990
There's no reason to do it, really.

2879
02:18:45,990 --> 02:18:47,720
We're not doing it for money.

2880
02:18:52,260 --> 02:18:53,990
When the final voting time comes,

2881
02:18:54,330 --> 02:18:57,760
residents will visit
the Community Center one by one...

2882
02:18:58,060 --> 02:18:59,970
and exercise their voting rights.

2883
02:19:01,100 --> 02:19:02,770
After the voting is over,

2884
02:19:02,900 --> 02:19:05,740
all residents won't go back
to the dormitory.

2885
02:19:05,740 --> 02:19:08,570
Each of them will wait in a separate area.

2886
02:19:09,640 --> 02:19:12,010
After all residents
are done with the voting,

2887
02:19:12,250 --> 02:19:14,450
in the separate areas they're waiting,

2888
02:19:14,450 --> 02:19:16,320
they will check the result
of the final voting...

2889
02:19:16,720 --> 02:19:19,050
and the individual prize money.

2890
02:19:20,320 --> 02:19:21,920
Then,

2891
02:19:22,760 --> 02:19:23,890
practically,

2892
02:19:24,720 --> 02:19:26,090
I've won!

2893
02:19:27,330 --> 02:19:29,160
I just don't know how to lose.

2894
02:19:30,730 --> 02:19:32,770
If they don't mess with the issuance,

2895
02:19:32,770 --> 02:19:34,130
- it's already over.
- I know.

2896
02:19:34,130 --> 02:19:35,900
It's not fun at all. What shall we do?

2897
02:19:38,670 --> 02:19:40,110
No, don't change.

2898
02:19:40,110 --> 02:19:41,570
Don't change into someone else.

2899
02:19:42,240 --> 02:19:43,940
Just hold on for a moment.

2900
02:19:43,940 --> 02:19:45,810
But your calculation was correct.

2901
02:19:45,810 --> 02:19:49,320
If we had sat on the bomb and dawdled...

2902
02:19:49,450 --> 02:19:50,850
and let our guards off,

2903
02:19:50,850 --> 02:19:52,190
- they could have won...
- Right.

2904
02:19:52,190 --> 02:19:54,490
If they went
for production activities today,

2905
02:19:54,490 --> 02:19:55,620
mined lives,

2906
02:19:55,620 --> 02:19:57,390
won the war and all,

2907
02:19:57,390 --> 02:19:59,330
- they could have made things different.
- Right.

2908
02:19:59,330 --> 02:20:00,860
And since they knew personal codes,

2909
02:20:00,860 --> 02:20:02,730
- if they attacked...
- Right.

2910
02:20:02,730 --> 02:20:05,470
And if we had not waged war yesterday,

2911
02:20:05,470 --> 02:20:07,730
- we couldn't have taken eight lives.
- I know.

2912
02:20:07,770 --> 02:20:09,270
Those eight votes...

2913
02:20:09,270 --> 02:20:10,770
- could have gone to Team Gold.
- Yes.

2914
02:20:10,770 --> 02:20:12,770
- We could have lost.
- That's right.

2915
02:20:12,870 --> 02:20:15,040
- Then Team Gold could have won.
- They actually stood a chance.

2916
02:20:15,040 --> 02:20:17,880
If they had won the war,

2917
02:20:18,180 --> 02:20:19,280
they actually could have won this game.

2918
02:20:19,280 --> 02:20:20,310
That's how the picture is painted.

2919
02:20:24,850 --> 02:20:26,820
This is irritating.

2920
02:20:29,660 --> 02:20:32,990
I thought, "Siseon was right."

2921
02:20:33,130 --> 02:20:36,030
We just gave it up.

2922
02:20:36,660 --> 02:20:39,530
If we had just made our move
earlier today,

2923
02:20:39,570 --> 02:20:41,130
if, as soon as we had mined lives,

2924
02:20:41,170 --> 02:20:45,410
we declared war on the team...

2925
02:20:45,410 --> 02:20:49,680
that seemingly had
the most resources and won the war,

2926
02:20:50,340 --> 02:20:52,280
we could have had a shot at winning.

2927
02:20:52,680 --> 02:20:55,650
This is crazy.
The last resource issuance is a killer.

2928
02:20:55,850 --> 02:20:58,150
They might feel anxious about it
and choose gold.

2929
02:20:58,680 --> 02:21:01,550
The sheer power
of the selected currency, so to speak.

2930
02:21:03,860 --> 02:21:05,220
Did you see the rule card?

2931
02:21:05,220 --> 02:21:07,260
- Is it you, Siseon?
- Yes, we did.

2932
02:21:07,260 --> 02:21:09,260
This is our last night together...

2933
02:21:10,360 --> 02:21:11,460
The weather got so nice.

2934
02:21:11,460 --> 02:21:12,670
The air feels so fresh too.

2935
02:21:12,670 --> 02:21:13,870
- Yes, it's so nice.
- This is the perfect temperature.

2936
02:21:13,870 --> 02:21:15,840
The only variable we have now...

2937
02:21:15,840 --> 02:21:18,570
- is Leia. If Leia...
- Right.

2938
02:21:18,570 --> 02:21:20,070
If you don't issue additional currency...

2939
02:21:20,070 --> 02:21:21,440
Just as much as you've been doubted,

2940
02:21:21,440 --> 02:21:22,640
you'd issue
additional currency tomorrow, right?

2941
02:21:22,640 --> 02:21:23,740
- Hey..
- Answer me.

2942
02:21:23,740 --> 02:21:24,880
Donkey.

2943
02:21:24,880 --> 02:21:26,010
Donkey, you shouldn't stay here.

2944
02:21:26,010 --> 02:21:28,210
You need to look at Black's rule book.

2945
02:21:28,750 --> 02:21:30,980
You need to bring your supervisor now.

2946
02:21:30,980 --> 02:21:33,290
- Shall I bring him now?
- Okay.

2947
02:21:34,990 --> 02:21:36,190
Vector.

2948
02:21:38,060 --> 02:21:39,130
Coming.

2949
02:21:41,360 --> 02:21:43,960
- Did you receive the rule card?
- Yes.

2950
02:21:44,300 --> 02:21:46,570
- Can I see it?
- Okay.

2951
02:21:47,200 --> 02:21:50,770
- Do they have the weapon dealer's rule?
- No.

2952
02:21:50,770 --> 02:21:52,970
Is it okay to show this?

2953
02:21:53,840 --> 02:21:57,310
The prices of offensive
and defensive rights for value code...

2954
02:21:57,310 --> 02:21:59,310
are set by the weapon dealer,

2955
02:21:59,480 --> 02:22:03,280
and the amount will be paid
to the weapon dealer.

2956
02:22:04,880 --> 02:22:07,320
The prices of offensive
and defensive rights...

2957
02:22:07,320 --> 02:22:11,220
can be set within the total supply
of existing diamonds and gold pieces.

2958
02:22:11,320 --> 02:22:14,130
And zero price cannot be set...

2959
02:22:14,130 --> 02:22:16,000
since it fundamentally breaks the game.

2960
02:22:16,130 --> 02:22:19,470
After all the schedule ends,
the weapon dealer's prize money...

2961
02:22:19,470 --> 02:22:23,240
will be split through the agreement
by the weapon dealer and the ally.

2962
02:22:23,300 --> 02:22:25,810
So if they purchase defensive rights,
the cost comes to us.

2963
02:22:26,370 --> 02:22:27,740
I see.

2964
02:22:28,040 --> 02:22:29,340
Maybe we don't need to show this.

2965
02:22:29,880 --> 02:22:33,050
How about only earning
the cost of the additional gold pieces?

2966
02:22:34,210 --> 02:22:37,380
- I don't think we need to show this.
- Let's not overdo it.

2967
02:22:37,380 --> 02:22:39,750
(They don't share
the weapon dealer's rule.)

2968
02:22:41,290 --> 02:22:42,860
But there was nothing special.

2969
02:22:42,860 --> 02:22:44,220
Why are you avoiding my gaze?

2970
02:22:44,590 --> 02:22:45,830
I'm afraid you might betray me tomorrow.

2971
02:22:48,690 --> 02:22:50,930
I'll only buy defensive rights tomorrow,
just in case.

2972
02:22:51,030 --> 02:22:53,370
Black knows my code, so I'll buy it.

2973
02:22:53,500 --> 02:22:54,670
Right.

2974
02:22:54,670 --> 02:22:56,370
- Black knows my code.
- He's coming.

2975
02:22:56,600 --> 02:22:58,000
Right. I forgot about Black.

2976
02:22:58,000 --> 02:22:59,910
- Hello.
- Hello.

2977
02:22:59,910 --> 02:23:01,440
- Is your rule book the same?
- It's the same, isn't it?

2978
02:23:01,770 --> 02:23:03,540
- It's the same.
- Is it?

2979
02:23:03,540 --> 02:23:06,080
But while reading this, I felt...

2980
02:23:06,080 --> 02:23:08,180
that if Team Gold...

2981
02:23:08,310 --> 02:23:10,450
did their best and kept their resources,

2982
02:23:10,450 --> 02:23:12,080
they could have betrayed us.

2983
02:23:12,080 --> 02:23:13,120
Pitou.

2984
02:23:13,120 --> 02:23:15,450
If we had lost the war yesterday,
we would have lost the whole game.

2985
02:23:15,450 --> 02:23:16,560
- Right.
- I heard that too.

2986
02:23:16,560 --> 02:23:17,920
It's only the 16 votes' difference.

2987
02:23:17,920 --> 02:23:18,930
- That's right.
- Really.

2988
02:23:18,930 --> 02:23:20,860
Therefore, all wars were necessary...

2989
02:23:20,860 --> 02:23:22,330
- from our perspective.
- I know.

2990
02:23:22,330 --> 02:23:24,200
- We had no choice but to wage war.
- Team Gold...

2991
02:23:24,200 --> 02:23:25,770
might not understand this.

2992
02:23:25,770 --> 02:23:27,970
However, now that
we have the final rule book here,

2993
02:23:27,970 --> 02:23:31,540
- every single war was a must for us.
- Exactly.

2994
02:23:31,540 --> 02:23:33,170
It has always been that way,
without exception.

2995
02:23:34,140 --> 02:23:35,240
That's true.

2996
02:23:36,010 --> 02:23:37,340
But people won't go crazy...

2997
02:23:37,340 --> 02:23:39,380
and make huge additional purchases, right?

2998
02:23:39,580 --> 02:23:41,050
Still,

2999
02:23:41,050 --> 02:23:43,880
defensive and offensive rights
won't make much difference.

3000
02:23:44,020 --> 02:23:46,290
How much is each one
when buying with resources?

3001
02:23:46,290 --> 02:23:48,150
This isn't a vote...

3002
02:23:48,150 --> 02:23:49,720
but an offensive right,
so it doesn't mean anything.

3003
02:23:50,190 --> 02:23:52,330
Unless all of us
miraculously guessed right,

3004
02:23:52,560 --> 02:23:54,430
even if a single person is missed,
it makes a tie.

3005
02:23:54,430 --> 02:23:56,200
- You can only buy the offensive right?
- Yes.

3006
02:23:56,300 --> 02:23:58,460
- Therefore, she's the only wildcard left.
- Right.

3007
02:23:58,700 --> 02:24:00,070
- We cannot check the diamonds.
- Yes.

3008
02:24:00,070 --> 02:24:01,370
Leia is the heroine for tomorrow.

3009
02:24:01,370 --> 02:24:04,370
Would Leia, who cried today
because of war...

3010
02:24:05,300 --> 02:24:07,170
This was exactly why...

3011
02:24:07,170 --> 02:24:09,840
we couldn't trust Team White.

3012
02:24:09,840 --> 02:24:11,610
- You're right.
- Because they could execute at the end.

3013
02:24:11,610 --> 02:24:13,880
- Yes.
- That's why we were with Team Red.

3014
02:24:13,880 --> 02:24:15,080
Of course.

3015
02:24:15,080 --> 02:24:16,880
It turned out pretty much like
as we expected.

3016
02:24:16,880 --> 02:24:20,690
Just how Maillard expected.

3017
02:24:21,650 --> 02:24:24,320
I'm relieved that it's Leia.

3018
02:24:24,320 --> 02:24:25,790
- Definitely.
- Yes.

3019
02:24:25,790 --> 02:24:27,830
She's the one who would suffer
the most if she betrayed.

3020
02:24:27,830 --> 02:24:29,100
- You're right
- Yes.

3021
02:24:29,100 --> 02:24:31,300
- I'd love to chase the fun,
- Yes.

3022
02:24:31,300 --> 02:24:34,730
but so many principles have been
compromised on this show.

3023
02:24:34,730 --> 02:24:36,500
I'm going to stick to the principles
at least at the end.

3024
02:24:36,500 --> 02:24:37,940
- That's good.
- Don't worry.

3025
02:24:37,940 --> 02:24:39,710
It's over now.

3026
02:24:39,710 --> 02:24:40,710
I'm so happy.

3027
02:24:40,710 --> 02:24:42,680
Everyone, salute to Leia.

3028
02:24:42,680 --> 02:24:44,080
No, don't.

3029
02:24:44,080 --> 02:24:45,780
- I'm counting on you.
- Princess Leia.

3030
02:24:45,780 --> 02:24:46,880
Thank you in advance.

3031
02:24:58,760 --> 02:25:02,860
I'm going to get up to speed
on these final rules as fast as I can,

3032
02:25:03,000 --> 02:25:07,230
so I can boost my chances of
taking my share in Team Gold.

3033
02:25:07,400 --> 02:25:11,000
I considered it as zero percent.

3034
02:25:11,000 --> 02:25:15,570
I just wanted to leave a message.

3035
02:25:16,080 --> 02:25:19,280
I'm going to keep fighting
to the very end,

3036
02:25:19,280 --> 02:25:22,080
even if I have to do it alone.
Just like they said.

3037
02:25:42,400 --> 02:25:44,940
Day Nine has begun.

3038
02:25:46,870 --> 02:25:49,480
You can change your leader from now.

3039
02:25:49,810 --> 02:25:51,580
Teams with a change in leadership...

3040
02:25:51,580 --> 02:25:53,710
are requested to have both
the current and new leaders...

3041
02:25:53,950 --> 02:25:56,450
visit the Community Center together...

3042
02:25:56,450 --> 02:25:59,090
to complete the handover procedure.

3043
02:26:00,020 --> 02:26:01,020
In addition,

3044
02:26:01,350 --> 02:26:03,160
Aside from leader change,

3045
02:26:03,390 --> 02:26:05,320
final relocation,

3046
02:26:05,790 --> 02:26:06,990
resource issuance,

3047
02:26:07,760 --> 02:26:09,460
and the final vote,

3048
02:26:09,630 --> 02:26:13,030
no other Community Center functions
will be in operation.

3049
02:26:13,030 --> 02:26:14,730
Please take note of this.

3050
02:26:15,840 --> 02:26:18,040
Since there's no trading session today,

3051
02:26:18,040 --> 02:26:20,470
the Platform won't be accessible.

3052
02:26:20,870 --> 02:26:24,640
That's all
from the Community Center for now.

3053
02:26:28,250 --> 02:26:29,320
Lesson learned.

3054
02:26:30,120 --> 02:26:31,850
Try to have it all,

3055
02:26:32,180 --> 02:26:33,550
and you lose it all.

3056
02:26:34,120 --> 02:26:36,420
If you never give up,
even to the bitter end,

3057
02:26:36,690 --> 02:26:38,590
your chance at victory will come.

3058
02:26:40,830 --> 02:26:42,560
I've learned many lessons.

3059
02:26:43,200 --> 02:26:45,930
All good. My goal was to survive
until the end.

3060
02:26:45,930 --> 02:26:47,600
Seeing how
all of my team members survived...

3061
02:26:47,600 --> 02:26:48,870
makes me feel relieved.

3062
02:26:49,070 --> 02:26:50,470
Once reappointment is done,

3063
02:26:50,470 --> 02:26:52,510
we shall go to vote immediately, right?

3064
02:26:53,040 --> 02:26:55,310
I guess we'll move on to the next step.

3065
02:26:55,310 --> 02:26:57,940
Now for the leader redistribution.

3066
02:26:58,210 --> 02:26:59,210
Yes.

3067
02:26:59,550 --> 02:27:02,450
The discussion time
for leader reappointment has ended.

3068
02:27:02,450 --> 02:27:05,180
We'll now start
the final resource distribution.

3069
02:27:05,180 --> 02:27:08,920
The leader of the Team White
should now go to the Community Center...

3070
02:27:08,920 --> 02:27:10,520
and distribute...

3071
02:27:10,520 --> 02:27:13,960
all of the group's diamonds,
gold, lives, and credits...

3072
02:27:13,960 --> 02:27:17,330
to each individual member,
leaving nothing behind.

3073
02:27:17,660 --> 02:27:20,370
Team White's members
get half the prize money.

3074
02:27:20,570 --> 02:27:22,740
It's only me and Paul.

3075
02:27:22,740 --> 02:27:26,010
We had 25,000,098 diamonds.

3076
02:27:26,010 --> 02:27:28,670
So we'll get 12,500,000 each.

3077
02:27:28,670 --> 02:27:30,910
For 98, I'll give Paul a hundred more.

3078
02:27:31,210 --> 02:27:32,980
We'll get one life and credit each,

3079
02:27:33,550 --> 02:27:35,510
and for the 75 gold,

3080
02:27:35,510 --> 02:27:39,080
we'll divide them into 37 and 38.

3081
02:27:39,490 --> 02:27:42,120
Paul, I gave you 98 diamonds more.

3082
02:27:42,420 --> 02:27:44,420
Since Team Blue is a one-person group,

3083
02:27:44,420 --> 02:27:46,830
the distribution
has been completed automatically.

3084
02:27:47,330 --> 02:27:50,500
Team Gold and Black is a one-person group.

3085
02:27:50,730 --> 02:27:53,130
So the distribution
has been completed automatically.

3086
02:27:54,900 --> 02:27:56,270
The safest thing is for me...

3087
02:27:56,570 --> 02:27:58,240
is to be the only one left in Team Red.

3088
02:27:58,540 --> 02:28:00,240
- For the final relocation?
- Yes.

3089
02:28:00,240 --> 02:28:02,480
Why? What's the risk then?

3090
02:28:02,480 --> 02:28:04,340
Siseon might relocate to Team White.

3091
02:28:04,340 --> 02:28:07,210
If they issue one billion...

3092
02:28:07,780 --> 02:28:09,580
- when Paul, Leia, and Siseon are there...
- One billion?

3093
02:28:09,580 --> 02:28:12,180
But they're relocating
after the resource distribution.

3094
02:28:12,180 --> 02:28:13,350
- But...
- If they issue again,

3095
02:28:13,350 --> 02:28:14,950
they can distribute again.

3096
02:28:14,950 --> 02:28:16,360
The final currency issuance...

3097
02:28:16,360 --> 02:28:18,720
gets distributed
within the team immediately.

3098
02:28:18,720 --> 02:28:19,730
I see.

3099
02:28:19,730 --> 02:28:21,490
Team White is lucky.

3100
02:28:21,490 --> 02:28:24,660
If they'd been playing
super exclusively up to now,

3101
02:28:25,060 --> 02:28:26,500
they might have pulled something.

3102
02:28:26,500 --> 02:28:27,500
That's right.

3103
02:28:27,700 --> 02:28:30,070
It seems like they're keeping variables
in play until the very end.

3104
02:28:30,070 --> 02:28:32,300
Yes. Can we trust Team White?

3105
02:28:32,740 --> 02:28:34,170
Can we trust Team Gold?

3106
02:28:34,170 --> 02:28:35,880
We should've sent Izaha too.

3107
02:28:36,040 --> 02:28:37,110
- To Team White?
- Yes.

3108
02:28:37,110 --> 02:28:38,180
If we doubt them.

3109
02:28:38,180 --> 02:28:39,180
I see.

3110
02:28:39,280 --> 02:28:40,280
I'm going to put in...

3111
02:28:40,950 --> 02:28:42,720
one last safeguard.

3112
02:28:43,080 --> 02:28:44,320
- For me...
- Pitou!

3113
02:28:44,320 --> 02:28:45,580
- Yes?
- Yes?

3114
02:28:45,580 --> 02:28:48,190
- I'm going to put in one last safeguard.
- What's that?

3115
02:28:48,190 --> 02:28:51,290
If Izaha fails to relocate to Team White,

3116
02:28:51,860 --> 02:28:53,190
we should all vote Team Gold.

3117
02:28:55,390 --> 02:28:56,400
Why is that?

3118
02:28:56,400 --> 02:28:58,830
If Team White gathers...

3119
02:28:58,830 --> 02:29:00,300
and issues extra currency,

3120
02:29:00,630 --> 02:29:02,670
all the previous team members
of Team White will get the dividends.

3121
02:29:02,670 --> 02:29:03,670
Yes.

3122
02:29:04,300 --> 02:29:06,270
So we're going to ask them
to accept Izaha.

3123
02:29:06,270 --> 02:29:07,910
I'm a hostage too, aren't I?

3124
02:29:08,140 --> 02:29:09,140
Go together.

3125
02:29:09,140 --> 02:29:10,780
- I'll be here.
- Isn't it better to divide?

3126
02:29:10,780 --> 02:29:12,480
- Send...
- Izaha will go to Team White.

3127
02:29:12,480 --> 02:29:13,580
- Yes, leave him here.
- Siseon will stay in Team Red.

3128
02:29:13,580 --> 02:29:16,320
Yes, but him being here is his choice.

3129
02:29:16,320 --> 02:29:18,720
So if he requests to relocate,

3130
02:29:18,720 --> 02:29:20,320
you'll be going
even if we don't want to send him.

3131
02:29:20,750 --> 02:29:21,890
- Okay.
- Okay.

3132
02:29:21,890 --> 02:29:23,160
If they accept Izaha...

3133
02:29:23,460 --> 02:29:25,820
Decide after talking about it.

3134
02:29:25,820 --> 02:29:27,290
She might not accept it
if she doesn't understand.

3135
02:29:27,290 --> 02:29:28,290
Okay.

3136
02:29:28,290 --> 02:29:31,030
For me, Team Gold isn't bad too.

3137
02:29:31,030 --> 02:29:32,770
- Do as you wish.
- That's what I'm saying.

3138
02:29:32,770 --> 02:29:34,700
- I have nothing to lose.
- So I'll send Izaha.

3139
02:29:34,700 --> 02:29:36,000
If they don't accept,

3140
02:29:36,000 --> 02:29:37,270
I'll put all my votes to Team Gold.

3141
02:29:37,270 --> 02:29:38,270
Okay.

3142
02:29:39,200 --> 02:29:40,870
He's removing even the last bit of risk.

3143
02:29:40,870 --> 02:29:43,410
He's going all in until the end.

3144
02:29:43,410 --> 02:29:44,410
I know.

3145
02:29:44,640 --> 02:29:46,010
He's very smart.

3146
02:29:47,080 --> 02:29:48,310
- Leia.
- Yes?

3147
02:29:49,420 --> 02:29:51,980
I'll put one last lock.

3148
02:29:52,150 --> 02:29:54,150
I'm relocating Izaha to Team White.

3149
02:29:54,150 --> 02:29:55,620
- Izaha? Sure.
- Yes.

3150
02:29:55,620 --> 02:29:56,620
- Okay.
- It doesn't matter.

3151
02:29:56,620 --> 02:29:58,120
Am I not trustworthy?

3152
02:29:58,690 --> 02:29:59,690
Well,

3153
02:30:00,290 --> 02:30:03,000
we made it this far because
we kept each other in check.

3154
02:30:03,000 --> 02:30:06,070
- Yes, this is the last check.
- The last check.

3155
02:30:06,070 --> 02:30:07,400
- He says it's not.
- Cool.

3156
02:30:07,400 --> 02:30:08,930
We didn't come this far
by trusting each other?

3157
02:30:08,930 --> 02:30:10,140
- No, not with trust.
- It was trust for me.

3158
02:30:10,140 --> 02:30:12,140
We came here by risking each other.

3159
02:30:12,140 --> 02:30:13,170
You're right.

3160
02:30:13,170 --> 02:30:15,470
We had hostages in our teams.

3161
02:30:15,470 --> 02:30:17,640
- Holding each other's lives.
- It's good to do this until the end.

3162
02:30:17,640 --> 02:30:18,980
You're doing your best.

3163
02:30:19,380 --> 02:30:21,580
From the start,

3164
02:30:21,580 --> 02:30:25,250
no strategy in Community Town
has ever been built on trust.

3165
02:30:25,250 --> 02:30:27,190
Trust is all broken.

3166
02:30:27,190 --> 02:30:29,390
We've made it this far...

3167
02:30:29,390 --> 02:30:31,860
by calculating the minimum risk...

3168
02:30:31,860 --> 02:30:34,360
and agreeing on how to split it among us.

3169
02:30:36,330 --> 02:30:38,500
Would Team Red and Black consider this?

3170
02:30:39,930 --> 02:30:40,930
They would.

3171
02:30:45,300 --> 02:30:46,310
There.

3172
02:30:53,350 --> 02:30:56,220
Even when I asked a girl out,
I never went this far.

3173
02:30:57,880 --> 02:31:00,590
I distributed zero diamonds to Donkey...

3174
02:31:00,590 --> 02:31:02,490
and 12,500,000 diamonds to Izaha.

3175
02:31:02,490 --> 02:31:06,160
Siseon also received 12,500,000 diamonds.

3176
02:31:06,160 --> 02:31:08,930
I have the remainder.

3177
02:31:09,330 --> 02:31:13,730
If Team White declines to accept Izaha,

3178
02:31:13,730 --> 02:31:16,540
I'll vote for Team Gold.

3179
02:31:16,540 --> 02:31:18,740
It's to distribute the risk.

3180
02:31:18,740 --> 02:31:21,540
If Izaha stays in Team Red,

3181
02:31:21,540 --> 02:31:25,440
I told Leia
that we will support Team Gold.

3182
02:31:25,810 --> 02:31:28,750
In the end, it finishes with blood mixed.

3183
02:31:28,750 --> 02:31:29,820
You're right.

3184
02:31:31,020 --> 02:31:32,280
Prepare to relocate.

3185
02:31:32,920 --> 02:31:35,390
(Final resource distribution is complete
and last relocation starts.)

3186
02:31:35,850 --> 02:31:37,860
I'm requesting to relocate to Team White.

3187
02:31:37,860 --> 02:31:39,560
I accept. Welcome!

3188
02:31:39,560 --> 02:31:41,430
You've accepted the relocation.

3189
02:31:42,390 --> 02:31:46,070
Izaha from Team Red relocated
to Team White.

3190
02:31:46,070 --> 02:31:47,070
Final relocation.

3191
02:31:47,870 --> 02:31:52,440
Izaha, please relocate within one hour.

3192
02:32:05,380 --> 02:32:06,990
- You're here.
- I'm here.

3193
02:32:06,990 --> 02:32:09,050
- Our room is...
- Fancy living room.

3194
02:32:09,050 --> 02:32:11,120
- the largest.
- Nice!

3195
02:32:11,120 --> 02:32:12,590
It's larger in size.

3196
02:32:12,590 --> 02:32:13,690
- We have a nice view.
- Welcome.

3197
02:32:13,690 --> 02:32:14,690
My goodness.

3198
02:32:14,690 --> 02:32:15,790
The view is spectacular.

3199
02:32:15,790 --> 02:32:18,360
Now, hold on to Siseon.

3200
02:32:18,360 --> 02:32:19,770
Block him from getting out.

3201
02:32:19,770 --> 02:32:21,370
I'm not going out!

3202
02:32:21,370 --> 02:32:22,430
He might relocate.

3203
02:32:22,730 --> 02:32:24,370
Lock him in the bathroom.

3204
02:32:25,640 --> 02:32:28,010
Izaha is the only one who relocated.

3205
02:32:28,210 --> 02:32:29,210
For the final?

3206
02:32:29,210 --> 02:32:31,780
The final relocation is over.

3207
02:32:32,110 --> 02:32:35,710
Now residents can't ask for relocation.

3208
02:32:35,710 --> 02:32:38,920
The final resource issuance will begin.

3209
02:32:39,220 --> 02:32:41,450
Please wait.

3210
02:32:41,950 --> 02:32:45,360
Will Team White understand my intention?

3211
02:32:47,260 --> 02:32:49,290
I'm just fighting until the end.

3212
02:32:50,700 --> 02:32:54,800
(Dormitory for Black)

3213
02:32:59,170 --> 02:33:01,070
I didn't want to bring this up,

3214
02:33:01,410 --> 02:33:03,010
but let me tell you something.

3215
02:33:03,910 --> 02:33:06,780
There's one variant.

3216
02:33:07,750 --> 02:33:08,750
Vector...

3217
02:33:09,520 --> 02:33:11,720
can set the price for the offensive right.

3218
02:33:12,250 --> 02:33:13,790
The offensive right...

3219
02:33:13,790 --> 02:33:16,990
can deduct the prize money
the same as gold.

3220
02:33:16,990 --> 02:33:20,030
But the prize money will come to us again.

3221
02:33:20,030 --> 02:33:21,260
To Vector and me.

3222
02:33:23,900 --> 02:33:26,400
The weapon dealer should decide...

3223
02:33:26,400 --> 02:33:30,000
the price for values code
and the offensive right...

3224
02:33:30,000 --> 02:33:33,710
in terms of gold and diamonds.

3225
02:33:36,710 --> 02:33:37,710
Yes.

3226
02:33:37,840 --> 02:33:39,980
(1 hour ago)

3227
02:33:39,980 --> 02:33:40,980
Did you...

3228
02:33:41,450 --> 02:33:43,180
set your resources?

3229
02:33:43,180 --> 02:33:44,280
Not yet.

3230
02:33:44,280 --> 02:33:47,750
Luna might burn everything.

3231
02:33:48,820 --> 02:33:50,460
It's good for us.

3232
02:33:51,320 --> 02:33:52,460
Shall we leave it as is?

3233
02:33:52,990 --> 02:33:55,930
I want to give Luna a choice.

3234
02:33:55,930 --> 02:33:58,260
- Okay.
- If that's what she wants.

3235
02:33:58,800 --> 02:34:00,770
I thought of making it expensive.

3236
02:34:00,770 --> 02:34:02,570
But then it'll mean we're giving...

3237
02:34:02,570 --> 02:34:04,470
- no choice for Luna until the end.
- You're right.

3238
02:34:04,470 --> 02:34:06,340
If we set 1 for 10,

3239
02:34:06,340 --> 02:34:07,940
- it's reasonable.
- Yes.

3240
02:34:08,670 --> 02:34:10,280
Let's set as 1 for 10...

3241
02:34:11,310 --> 02:34:13,350
I'll set the price of...

3242
02:34:13,350 --> 02:34:16,680
values code offensive right
and defensive right.

3243
02:34:17,680 --> 02:34:18,980
For diamonds,

3244
02:34:19,380 --> 02:34:20,490
it'll be five million diamonds.

3245
02:34:22,390 --> 02:34:25,920
Ten gold pieces.

3246
02:34:26,360 --> 02:34:29,290
Luna has 37 gold pieces,

3247
02:34:29,290 --> 02:34:32,430
so I figured 15,000 dollars
would be a huge win...

3248
02:34:32,530 --> 02:34:34,300
and set the price at ten gold pieces.

3249
02:34:34,400 --> 02:34:36,740
For diamonds, I used the same value.

3250
02:34:36,740 --> 02:34:38,100
That's 5,000 dollars' worth of diamonds,

3251
02:34:38,100 --> 02:34:40,570
which comes to five million diamonds.

3252
02:34:41,440 --> 02:34:43,380
The prices have been set.

3253
02:34:44,110 --> 02:34:46,180
You may now leave.

3254
02:34:46,180 --> 02:34:47,980
Good work. Thank you.

3255
02:34:48,950 --> 02:34:53,820
(Offensive and defensive right prices:
5 million diamonds, 10 gold pieces)

3256
02:34:54,220 --> 02:34:56,560
Here are the prices of the offensive...

3257
02:34:56,560 --> 02:34:59,960
and defensive rights available
during today's final vote.

3258
02:35:00,530 --> 02:35:04,260
If you purchase
an offensive or defensive right,

3259
02:35:05,130 --> 02:35:09,370
the value of that resource will be
deducted from the total prize money.

3260
02:35:09,570 --> 02:35:11,040
Please keep that in mind.

3261
02:35:13,210 --> 02:35:16,170
At least we'll be able to do something
at the very end if we want to.

3262
02:35:16,170 --> 02:35:17,580
- Right.
- Yes.

3263
02:35:17,740 --> 02:35:19,850
- If we were to issue it now...
- Right.

3264
02:35:19,850 --> 02:35:21,480
- We're going to issue gold now, right?
- We're doing it now.

3265
02:35:23,480 --> 02:35:25,420
So it's based on the current amount.

3266
02:35:25,420 --> 02:35:27,120
The baseline is 200 gold pieces...

3267
02:35:28,420 --> 02:35:30,020
because I haven't issued any.

3268
02:35:31,020 --> 02:35:32,690
Good thing I didn't issue any yesterday.

3269
02:35:36,430 --> 02:35:37,600
What, 500? Seriously?

3270
02:35:37,600 --> 02:35:40,270
The final resource issuance...

3271
02:35:40,270 --> 02:35:42,130
for Team White and Team Gold begins now.

3272
02:35:42,130 --> 02:35:43,140
That's really expensive.

3273
02:35:43,340 --> 02:35:44,770
The leader of Team White must...

3274
02:35:44,770 --> 02:35:47,670
bring the resource issuance voucher
and the stamp...

3275
02:35:47,710 --> 02:35:49,170
to the Community Center...

3276
02:35:49,170 --> 02:35:51,180
- and decide how many diamonds...
- Let's just...

3277
02:35:51,180 --> 02:35:52,740
- to issue one last time.
- not go.

3278
02:35:53,180 --> 02:35:54,350
- I'll be back.
- Okay.

3279
02:35:54,350 --> 02:35:55,450
Good luck.

3280
02:35:58,150 --> 02:35:59,550
The leader of Team Gold must...

3281
02:35:59,550 --> 02:36:02,420
bring the resource issuance voucher
and the stamp...

3282
02:36:02,590 --> 02:36:04,260
to the Community Center...

3283
02:36:04,260 --> 02:36:07,790
and decide the final amount of gold
to issue.

3284
02:36:49,000 --> 02:36:52,270
(Final resource issuance)

3285
02:37:10,620 --> 02:37:13,730
If you wish to issue diamonds,
enter the quantity on the voucher...

3286
02:37:14,090 --> 02:37:16,760
and submit it to the central box.

3287
02:37:26,040 --> 02:37:31,080
(Diamond issuance)

3288
02:37:31,080 --> 02:37:34,750
I've never betrayed the trust...

3289
02:37:34,750 --> 02:37:36,350
of anyone I've worked with.

3290
02:37:36,980 --> 02:37:38,350
I stayed loyal...

3291
02:37:39,950 --> 02:37:41,450
to every alliance...

3292
02:37:44,890 --> 02:37:45,990
because only then,

3293
02:37:47,030 --> 02:37:48,930
could I land one decisive blow...

3294
02:37:50,200 --> 02:37:53,030
at the critical moment.

3295
02:37:55,230 --> 02:37:59,240
When Team Blue declared war on us,

3296
02:38:00,170 --> 02:38:03,070
Team White lost...

3297
02:38:04,040 --> 02:38:05,710
three of our valued teammates.

3298
02:38:06,650 --> 02:38:07,780
As for Team Red,

3299
02:38:08,380 --> 02:38:10,920
they never actually declared war.

3300
02:38:11,020 --> 02:38:13,750
They always killed by proxy.

3301
02:38:15,220 --> 02:38:18,760
So I believe they are guilty...

3302
02:38:19,190 --> 02:38:21,230
of turning Team White and Team Blue
into war criminals.

3303
02:38:21,730 --> 02:38:24,060
Izaha did join our team,

3304
02:38:24,700 --> 02:38:26,500
but he worked hard,

3305
02:38:27,000 --> 02:38:29,500
so I wanted to reward him more.

3306
02:38:34,140 --> 02:38:37,710
I also wanted to respect Luna's choice...

3307
02:38:37,710 --> 02:38:40,010
to remain with Team Gold until the end...

3308
02:38:41,680 --> 02:38:43,780
and send a message to those...

3309
02:38:44,450 --> 02:38:47,950
who declared war and launched bombs...

3310
02:38:49,150 --> 02:38:52,820
against a threat that wasn't even real.

3311
02:39:42,310 --> 02:39:44,210
Team White's leader, Leia.

3312
02:39:44,210 --> 02:39:47,610
I will issue diamonds one last time.

3313
02:39:55,520 --> 02:39:58,660
(Diamond issuance)

3314
02:40:06,870 --> 02:40:08,970
No diamonds were issued.

3315
02:40:09,970 --> 02:40:11,900
You may now leave.

3316
02:40:13,570 --> 02:40:15,710
(No alliance lasts forever,)

3317
02:40:15,710 --> 02:40:18,510
(but neither does any cycle.)

3318
02:40:18,510 --> 02:40:20,010
(Still dreaming of peace...)

3319
02:40:20,010 --> 02:40:21,350
(0 diamonds)

3320
02:41:57,540 --> 02:41:58,680
With this,

3321
02:41:58,680 --> 02:42:01,880
Luna could take all the prize money
and win for sure.

3322
02:42:02,310 --> 02:42:04,780
Team White can't issue any more...

3323
02:42:04,880 --> 02:42:06,450
because too many people
have a stake in it.

3324
02:42:06,890 --> 02:42:09,920
If you wish to issue gold,
enter the quantity on the voucher...

3325
02:42:09,920 --> 02:42:12,520
and submit it to the central box.

3326
02:42:12,760 --> 02:42:14,890
We're done for now.

3327
02:42:14,890 --> 02:42:18,130
We could now lose by a single vote
because we got complacent!

3328
02:42:18,560 --> 02:42:20,370
- But now...
- This last bit of complacency!

3329
02:42:21,500 --> 02:42:24,440
I'll issue one trillion gold pieces.

3330
02:42:39,220 --> 02:42:41,690
The final resource issuance is complete.

3331
02:42:41,990 --> 02:42:44,960
The final vote will begin shortly.

3332
02:42:45,160 --> 02:42:48,390
Until then, all residents must wait
in their dormitories.

3333
02:42:48,390 --> 02:42:50,060
We're done for. She issued one trillion?

3334
02:42:50,760 --> 02:42:53,360
As soon as I heard the announcement,
I knew something was wrong.

3335
02:42:53,470 --> 02:42:56,230
I knew Team White was too entangled...

3336
02:42:56,230 --> 02:42:58,340
in conflicting interests to issue more,

3337
02:42:58,770 --> 02:43:01,240
but Team Gold only has one member.

3338
02:43:01,440 --> 02:43:03,070
If she issued a huge amount of gold,

3339
02:43:03,440 --> 02:43:06,040
she could use it to buy...

3340
02:43:06,140 --> 02:43:07,480
more offensive rights
and attack endlessly.

3341
02:43:07,480 --> 02:43:09,780
I should have seen this coming.

3342
02:43:09,910 --> 02:43:12,980
During the war, we set the war cost...

3343
02:43:13,150 --> 02:43:15,350
before we could issue more currency.

3344
02:43:15,350 --> 02:43:17,490
I think this follows the same logic.

3345
02:43:18,520 --> 02:43:22,290
They held the currency issuance...

3346
02:43:22,560 --> 02:43:24,700
after individual allocations
and relocation were complete.

3347
02:43:24,830 --> 02:43:27,670
Then Team White can't issue more.
Everything is already distributed.

3348
02:43:28,030 --> 02:43:31,140
But if I issue gold like crazy now,

3349
02:43:31,140 --> 02:43:32,970
its value becomes worthless, right?

3350
02:43:32,970 --> 02:43:36,940
That was the strategy I kept planning
when I wanted to start a war.

3351
02:43:37,180 --> 02:43:39,480
Then I can attack endlessly, right?

3352
02:43:39,780 --> 02:43:41,380
The moment I saw it, I knew we'd lost.

3353
02:43:41,380 --> 02:43:43,980
I was certain. Luna had made up her mind.

3354
02:43:43,980 --> 02:43:47,890
Team Gold would gain
nearly unlimited offensive rights.

3355
02:43:47,990 --> 02:43:50,820
It probably won't greatly affect
the actual prize payout.

3356
02:43:50,820 --> 02:43:53,320
Even if she attacks 10 million times
or 100 million times,

3357
02:43:53,320 --> 02:43:56,460
the actual prize might drop
by only 50 dollars.

3358
02:43:56,460 --> 02:43:58,600
Issuing that much currency means...

3359
02:43:58,600 --> 02:44:01,630
she plans to attack every value code
and win.

3360
02:44:01,630 --> 02:44:03,570
Team Gold will win with just one vote.

3361
02:44:03,670 --> 02:44:05,200
Team White now...

3362
02:44:05,200 --> 02:44:07,740
has a psychological barrier
to issuing any more,

3363
02:44:07,740 --> 02:44:09,210
so I concluded we couldn't win.

3364
02:44:10,010 --> 02:44:12,940
With no conflicting interests,
Team Gold is guaranteed to win.

3365
02:44:14,480 --> 02:44:16,880
Does Team Diamond know they've lost?

3366
02:44:17,250 --> 02:44:18,350
They must all know, right?

3367
02:44:20,490 --> 02:44:21,920
So we shouldn't vote for Team Gold.

3368
02:44:23,090 --> 02:44:24,820
- She issued one trillion gold pieces.
- Right.

3369
02:44:24,860 --> 02:44:26,090
But what are those 200 gold pieces?

3370
02:44:26,090 --> 02:44:27,490
- Those 200 were the initial issuance.
- The original issuance.

3371
02:44:27,490 --> 02:44:29,630
- Because of the initial issuance?
- Yes.

3372
02:44:30,060 --> 02:44:32,600
Exactly. Congratulations
on one trillion gold pieces.

3373
02:44:32,600 --> 02:44:33,670
That's cute.

3374
02:44:34,030 --> 02:44:37,900
- She's trying to send a message.
- Definitely.

3375
02:44:38,240 --> 02:44:39,600
"Don't even think about coming over!"

3376
02:44:41,070 --> 02:44:42,870
It's a message. A message.

3377
02:44:42,910 --> 02:44:44,440
"I don't want anything from you."

3378
02:44:44,440 --> 02:44:45,780
"We lost."

3379
02:44:45,780 --> 02:44:48,010
"It's not that you didn't choose me."

3380
02:44:48,080 --> 02:44:51,250
"I made sure you couldn't choose me."

3381
02:44:51,620 --> 02:44:54,390
I think that was the message
she wanted to send.

3382
02:44:55,790 --> 02:44:57,490
Issuing all that gold...

3383
02:44:57,490 --> 02:44:59,720
felt like firing a warning shot.

3384
02:44:59,720 --> 02:45:02,860
Everyone in the other dorms could see it.

3385
02:45:03,090 --> 02:45:05,560
So I was really nervous on the way there.

3386
02:45:10,700 --> 02:45:13,440
Then I came back and found a flower
waiting for me.

3387
02:45:13,810 --> 02:45:16,370
If they fully understood my position...

3388
02:45:16,370 --> 02:45:19,040
and the strategy behind it,

3389
02:45:19,040 --> 02:45:20,450
I think they might accept it.

3390
02:45:20,650 --> 02:45:23,010
But I don't think they realized...

3391
02:45:23,010 --> 02:45:25,420
the rules gave me one last option.

3392
02:45:25,420 --> 02:45:27,950
They'll probably see it as a betrayal.

3393
02:45:28,590 --> 02:45:30,620
So I felt a little bad about that.

3394
02:45:32,760 --> 02:45:34,830
Let me run through one scenario.

3395
02:45:34,830 --> 02:45:35,890
There's no winning scenario.

3396
02:45:35,890 --> 02:45:38,430
With this setup, we have no way to win.

3397
02:45:38,600 --> 02:45:41,000
Isn't this basically tying our hands...

3398
02:45:41,000 --> 02:45:42,530
and killing us?

3399
02:45:42,800 --> 02:45:44,000
Gosh.

3400
02:45:44,000 --> 02:45:45,940
What? I'm the only one who came out ahead.

3401
02:45:46,640 --> 02:45:48,110
I got complacent too.

3402
02:45:48,110 --> 02:45:50,480
I should've told Vector
to issue zero diamonds.

3403
02:45:51,010 --> 02:45:54,080
The vote to determine the final prize...

3404
02:45:54,650 --> 02:45:57,880
and individual value code targeting
will now begin.

3405
02:45:59,080 --> 02:46:02,650
Residents must visit the Community Center
one at a time...

3406
02:46:03,760 --> 02:46:07,060
to vote and target a value code.

3407
02:46:08,260 --> 02:46:09,290
Let's do this!

3408
02:46:24,480 --> 02:46:26,610
To stop Team Gold from running wild,

3409
02:46:26,610 --> 02:46:29,350
whoever held the casting vote
also had to hold the gold...

3410
02:46:29,350 --> 02:46:30,950
and both sides had to promise...

3411
02:46:30,950 --> 02:46:33,420
not to devalue it. That might've worked.

3412
02:46:33,920 --> 02:46:35,290
If that person said,
"I'll trust you on this."

3413
02:46:35,750 --> 02:46:37,760
"Don't issue any gold."

3414
02:46:37,760 --> 02:46:39,390
As a show of trust?

3415
02:46:39,390 --> 02:46:41,660
Then she might not have issued any.

3416
02:46:45,100 --> 02:46:47,470
Leia, check your personal resources,

3417
02:46:47,670 --> 02:46:49,530
mark your final ballot,

3418
02:46:49,670 --> 02:46:51,740
and submit it to the central box.

3419
02:46:52,240 --> 02:46:55,770
If you wish to purchase an offensive...

3420
02:46:55,770 --> 02:46:57,580
or defensive right, state the quantity.

3421
02:46:57,980 --> 02:46:59,840
With your current credits, Leia,

3422
02:46:59,840 --> 02:47:02,280
you can purchase one right.

3423
02:47:02,280 --> 02:47:05,720
The cost of additional purchases
will come out of the total prize money.

3424
02:47:06,250 --> 02:47:10,120
I'll use a credit to buy
one offensive right.

3425
02:47:11,360 --> 02:47:13,690
Please collect one offensive right.

3426
02:47:18,400 --> 02:47:19,500
"Target name"?

3427
02:47:20,570 --> 02:47:22,030
This really feels like
I'm killing someone.

3428
02:47:22,870 --> 02:47:24,970
I'll try attacking...

3429
02:47:24,970 --> 02:47:26,140
(Leia's choice: Vector)

3430
02:47:26,140 --> 02:47:27,870
Vector.

3431
02:47:28,970 --> 02:47:30,070
But will it work?

3432
02:47:30,580 --> 02:47:31,940
To prepare for the worst,

3433
02:47:31,940 --> 02:47:34,180
I should've used it on Team Gold,
my direct competitor,

3434
02:47:34,180 --> 02:47:35,380
but I didn't want to do that.

3435
02:47:35,480 --> 02:47:36,850
I had one either way,

3436
02:47:37,220 --> 02:47:39,820
so I thought about who was the worst
out of everyone here.

3437
02:47:39,820 --> 02:47:41,090
(Leia, Journalist)

3438
02:47:41,090 --> 02:47:42,790
I thought, "Let's try targeting Black."

3439
02:47:42,790 --> 02:47:45,260
"Ability" is maxed out.

3440
02:47:45,460 --> 02:47:47,530
"Practicality" is maxed out too.

3441
02:47:47,660 --> 02:47:48,730
"Result."

3442
02:47:49,330 --> 02:47:51,860
Has he ever made a utilitarian choice...

3443
02:47:51,860 --> 02:47:53,000
(Values Code Offensive Right)

3444
02:47:53,770 --> 02:47:57,000
Please submit the offensive right
to the central box.

3445
02:47:57,570 --> 02:47:58,870
Sorry, Vector.

3446
02:48:01,410 --> 02:48:02,510
I went for it.

3447
02:48:03,410 --> 02:48:04,640
A total failure.

3448
02:48:05,340 --> 02:48:07,180
Your attack has failed.

3449
02:48:07,180 --> 02:48:10,720
If you wish to buy more,
please state the quantity.

3450
02:48:11,550 --> 02:48:13,120
I won't purchase any more.

3451
02:48:13,680 --> 02:48:16,750
Please proceed with
the final resource vote.

3452
02:48:17,560 --> 02:48:20,060
I had 1 base vote and 1 life,
so that was 2 votes for diamonds.

3453
02:48:20,390 --> 02:48:21,490
I had two votes.

3454
02:48:21,930 --> 02:48:25,030
I think it'll turn out as expected.

3455
02:48:25,360 --> 02:48:27,400
I don't think there'll be any surprises.

3456
02:48:28,200 --> 02:48:29,730
(Paul's personal resources)

3457
02:48:29,730 --> 02:48:31,840
I'll use one credit on defense.

3458
02:48:32,970 --> 02:48:34,140
That's two.

3459
02:48:34,140 --> 02:48:36,670
(1 base vote and 1 life: 2 diamond votes)

3460
02:48:38,080 --> 02:48:40,850
(Izaha's 1 base vote:)

3461
02:48:40,850 --> 02:48:42,610
(1 diamond vote)

3462
02:48:43,450 --> 02:48:45,450
I'll buy five defensive rights.

3463
02:48:46,320 --> 02:48:48,550
(Pitou's 1 base vote and 4 lives:)

3464
02:48:48,550 --> 02:48:50,490
(5 diamond votes)

3465
02:48:51,220 --> 02:48:53,560
I'll use 6 credits
to buy 6 defensive rights.

3466
02:48:53,690 --> 02:48:57,560
I'll use 50 gold pieces
to buy 5 defensive rights.

3467
02:48:58,030 --> 02:48:59,460
The 50 gold pieces have been...

3468
02:48:59,460 --> 02:49:01,270
- deducted from the prize money.
- Okay.

3469
02:49:01,930 --> 02:49:03,570
(Maillard's 1 base vote and 9 lives)

3470
02:49:03,570 --> 02:49:04,640
Plus...

3471
02:49:04,640 --> 02:49:06,670
(10 diamond votes in total)

3472
02:49:06,670 --> 02:49:07,710
Ten.

3473
02:49:08,070 --> 02:49:09,470
Why don't I have anything?

3474
02:49:10,240 --> 02:49:12,180
(Donkey's 1 base vote:)

3475
02:49:12,180 --> 02:49:14,710
(1 diamond vote)

3476
02:49:17,920 --> 02:49:21,290
(Siseon's 1 base vote: 1 diamond vote)

3477
02:49:21,490 --> 02:49:22,590
I'm counting on you.

3478
02:49:23,720 --> 02:49:26,760
I'll spend 1 life to buy 1 extra vote.

3479
02:49:26,760 --> 02:49:28,090
I'll use a credit...

3480
02:49:28,090 --> 02:49:30,700
to defend myself, even if it's pointless.

3481
02:49:31,160 --> 02:49:33,800
It may be pointless,
but I'll do it for Team Diamond.

3482
02:49:34,330 --> 02:49:36,770
Honestly, if Leia had acted faster,

3483
02:49:36,870 --> 02:49:40,070
I'd feel bad for the others,
but I would've issued a massive amount...

3484
02:49:40,070 --> 02:49:42,840
and bought an absurd number
of defensive rights.

3485
02:49:43,240 --> 02:49:45,980
I wondered whether Luna would win
once those two fought it out...

3486
02:49:45,980 --> 02:49:47,850
or if they used five million diamonds...

3487
02:49:47,850 --> 02:49:50,480
to buy around two offensive rights,

3488
02:49:50,620 --> 02:49:52,980
we might make another 20,000 dollars.

3489
02:49:53,150 --> 02:49:56,420
I waited for the result,
hoping that might happen.

3490
02:50:01,590 --> 02:50:03,360
(Offensive and defensive right prices)

3491
02:50:03,360 --> 02:50:05,160
(Final personal resources)

3492
02:50:05,560 --> 02:50:08,900
I will use 98 gold pieces
plus 2 more with credits...

3493
02:50:08,900 --> 02:50:11,740
to buy a total of 100 defensive rights.

3494
02:50:12,140 --> 02:50:15,570
I know 100 sounds completely absurd,

3495
02:50:15,640 --> 02:50:18,210
but I calculated how many I'd need
if one person held all those resources...

3496
02:50:18,210 --> 02:50:20,510
and used them to attack me.

3497
02:50:20,510 --> 02:50:22,350
I'll use gold...

3498
02:50:22,650 --> 02:50:26,480
to buy 8,898 offensive rights.

3499
02:50:26,880 --> 02:50:28,890
The requested quantity is too large.

3500
02:50:29,290 --> 02:50:31,420
We don't have
enough printed offensive rights.

3501
02:50:31,760 --> 02:50:34,690
They'll be issued to you in stages.

3502
02:50:34,790 --> 02:50:37,800
If you repeat the same attack,

3503
02:50:37,800 --> 02:50:40,100
write down the number of repetitions
and submit it.

3504
02:50:40,100 --> 02:50:42,530
The number you enter will be applied
to the attack,

3505
02:50:42,670 --> 02:50:46,000
and that amount will be deducted
from the prize money.

3506
02:50:49,570 --> 02:50:50,640
The prize money...

3507
02:50:53,310 --> 02:50:54,710
This is going to take forever.

3508
02:50:56,650 --> 02:50:58,120
Again. Slowly.

3509
02:50:58,120 --> 02:51:00,620
So it's 1-1-1, 1-1-1.

3510
02:51:00,750 --> 02:51:03,650
I accidentally wrote 1-2-1.

3511
02:51:08,790 --> 02:51:10,230
(Values Code Offensive Right)

3512
02:51:14,330 --> 02:51:16,470
It's 2-1... It's 2-2-2.

3513
02:51:16,800 --> 02:51:18,470
This is just about combinations.

3514
02:51:18,470 --> 02:51:21,140
Multiply them out,
and there are 64 per person.

3515
02:51:21,310 --> 02:51:23,470
I even had a rough idea
of their Majority Rules Game choices,

3516
02:51:23,710 --> 02:51:25,240
so I used that as my baseline.

3517
02:51:25,280 --> 02:51:28,080
But Team Red had always feared...

3518
02:51:28,080 --> 02:51:29,780
having their values codes targeted,

3519
02:51:29,780 --> 02:51:31,950
so I considered that they might've...

3520
02:51:32,220 --> 02:51:35,150
deliberately chosen answers
different from their own beliefs.

3521
02:51:35,420 --> 02:51:37,620
I entered 100 repetitions per attack.

3522
02:51:39,620 --> 02:51:41,430
(People backed into a corner will bite.)

3523
02:51:41,960 --> 02:51:43,460
(At least one person survives.)

3524
02:51:43,460 --> 02:51:46,400
(That person can reduce your prize
to 1 cent.)

3525
02:51:46,400 --> 02:51:48,030
(The moment our numbers dwindle,)

3526
02:51:48,030 --> 02:51:49,800
(we're much more likely
to act aggressively.)

3527
02:51:56,470 --> 02:51:57,880
When will I ever finish this?

3528
02:51:58,580 --> 02:52:00,040
This is driving me insane.

3529
02:52:05,320 --> 02:52:06,780
It was just a reality check.

3530
02:52:06,780 --> 02:52:07,890
(Luna, Influencer)

3531
02:52:07,890 --> 02:52:12,920
Until yesterday, I'd felt this way
about the majority alliance.

3532
02:52:13,760 --> 02:52:15,790
"Why are they taking it this far?"

3533
02:52:15,890 --> 02:52:18,660
But I kept asking myself
the same question.

3534
02:52:18,760 --> 02:52:20,360
I was checking every possible outcome...

3535
02:52:20,360 --> 02:52:21,800
and writing each one down.

3536
02:52:21,800 --> 02:52:24,070
My hands were shaking,
so I couldn't even calculate.

3537
02:52:24,070 --> 02:52:26,570
I kept making mistakes.

3538
02:52:27,240 --> 02:52:28,570
Why am I taking it this far?

3539
02:52:28,870 --> 02:52:31,510
I don't even want all the prize money.

3540
02:52:31,640 --> 02:52:34,810
I just want everyone to split it evenly.

3541
02:52:35,650 --> 02:52:37,480
What started this fight?

3542
02:52:37,780 --> 02:52:39,920
What made us shut each other out?

3543
02:52:39,920 --> 02:52:41,990
It was a sobering reality check,

3544
02:52:42,550 --> 02:52:44,090
but I still wouldn't change my decision...

3545
02:52:44,090 --> 02:52:47,360
and kept trying so hard.
I felt this strange disconnect.

3546
02:52:49,630 --> 02:52:52,860
They were all B choices.
All about Meaning.

3547
02:52:53,230 --> 02:52:56,330
It made me wonder whether...

3548
02:52:56,330 --> 02:52:59,040
they'd truly been making choices
to seek Meaning...

3549
02:52:59,670 --> 02:53:02,670
and how much people judge things...

3550
02:53:02,910 --> 02:53:06,580
based on their circumstances
and the lives they've lived.

3551
02:53:06,780 --> 02:53:09,310
I chose Ability because I lived...

3552
02:53:09,310 --> 02:53:12,720
in a world where having it
meant I could use it.

3553
02:53:13,020 --> 02:53:15,250
If I'd lived in a world
with limits like this...

3554
02:53:15,250 --> 02:53:17,390
of course I would've chosen Structure.

3555
02:53:17,860 --> 02:53:21,160
Seeing so many B choices
made me think about that.

3556
02:53:21,460 --> 02:53:24,030
It seemed like they'd made choices...

3557
02:53:24,030 --> 02:53:25,730
that leaned too heavily
toward Practicality.

3558
02:53:26,130 --> 02:53:27,400
So what did any of it mean?

3559
02:53:29,370 --> 02:53:31,140
Your attack was successful.

3560
02:53:31,500 --> 02:53:34,610
Please proceed with
the final resource vote.

3561
02:53:34,970 --> 02:53:36,740
For the final resource vote,

3562
02:53:36,970 --> 02:53:39,880
each resident receives one base vote...

3563
02:53:41,050 --> 02:53:45,120
plus one additional vote
for every life they hold.

3564
02:53:45,580 --> 02:53:48,350
Luna, you have...

3565
02:53:48,990 --> 02:53:50,290
one vote in the final resource vote.

3566
02:53:51,620 --> 02:53:54,430
(Final resource selection)

3567
02:54:10,940 --> 02:54:13,910
This is an announcement
from the Community Center.

3568
02:54:14,810 --> 02:54:17,250
The final currency vote results are in.

3569
02:54:18,220 --> 02:54:20,350
- Gold has been selected.
- Gold?

3570
02:54:21,020 --> 02:54:22,450
(Final selected resource: Gold)

3571
02:54:26,320 --> 02:54:27,360
What?

3572
02:54:28,360 --> 02:54:29,390
What?

3573
02:54:34,570 --> 02:54:35,670
What is this?

3574
02:54:35,670 --> 02:54:37,000
(Final selected resource: Gold)

3575
02:54:37,000 --> 02:54:38,100
What?

3576
02:54:40,740 --> 02:54:42,210
Luna worked hard for this.

3577
02:54:43,040 --> 02:54:46,080
Leia, your final prize is as follows.

3578
02:54:46,380 --> 02:54:47,910
(Current value per gold piece:
0.000000075 dollars)

3579
02:54:47,910 --> 02:54:49,580
(Gold held: 37, final prize: 0 dollars)

3580
02:54:51,120 --> 02:54:52,920
It didn't feel real. I just went, "What?"

3581
02:54:52,920 --> 02:54:54,190
(Leia, Journalist)

3582
02:54:54,190 --> 02:54:55,220
Gold?

3583
02:54:55,720 --> 02:54:56,750
Gold?

3584
02:54:57,190 --> 02:55:00,360
So she tried until she got it right.

3585
02:55:00,360 --> 02:55:03,890
Was it one trillion?
She issued that much until she got it.

3586
02:55:04,060 --> 02:55:07,470
This is why you should never upset anyone.

3587
02:55:08,500 --> 02:55:11,270
This is why
you should never corner anyone...

3588
02:55:11,270 --> 02:55:13,270
or upset them.

3589
02:55:13,500 --> 02:55:14,870
(The current value of 1 gold:
0.00000075 dollars)

3590
02:55:14,870 --> 02:55:16,070
Oh, my gosh.

3591
02:55:21,750 --> 02:55:24,150
Luna, talk to you never!

3592
02:55:24,150 --> 02:55:27,720
I shed so many tears for you.

3593
02:55:28,690 --> 02:55:31,220
Because you disgraced my tears,

3594
02:55:31,220 --> 02:55:34,860
you're unforgivable.

3595
02:55:36,860 --> 02:55:39,400
After one trillion gold pieces
were issued,

3596
02:55:39,400 --> 02:55:42,570
I gave up.

3597
02:55:42,630 --> 02:55:44,270
Luna isn't trying...

3598
02:55:44,270 --> 02:55:46,970
to end game like this. It's a relief.

3599
02:55:46,970 --> 02:55:49,840
Honestly, I'm very offended.

3600
02:55:49,840 --> 02:55:52,640
It's a reasonable choice for Luna.

3601
02:55:52,640 --> 02:55:54,710
But I blame the system.

3602
02:55:55,310 --> 02:55:57,720
I'm kind of stunned.

3603
02:55:57,780 --> 02:56:00,550
I never expected that from Luna.

3604
02:56:00,550 --> 02:56:03,590
Honestly, I didn't think she'd do that.

3605
02:56:03,590 --> 02:56:04,820
So,

3606
02:56:04,960 --> 02:56:07,560
I'm kind of sick of people right now.

3607
02:56:07,690 --> 02:56:09,930
Just people in general, not just her.

3608
02:56:09,930 --> 02:56:12,930
I'm sick of people as a whole.

3609
02:56:14,470 --> 02:56:17,200
(Leia, Journalist)

3610
02:56:17,200 --> 02:56:18,340
That was expected of Luna.

3611
02:56:20,240 --> 02:56:21,910
That was very typical of her. And I am...

3612
02:56:24,170 --> 02:56:25,780
actually pretty happy.

3613
02:56:28,510 --> 02:56:30,410
There is something regrettable.

3614
02:56:30,410 --> 02:56:33,580
In the current system,
Team White's leader...

3615
02:56:33,880 --> 02:56:35,590
may feel pressured...

3616
02:56:35,750 --> 02:56:39,560
to issue additional resources.

3617
02:56:39,560 --> 02:56:42,090
Now that Donkey's bound
to receive a prize,

3618
02:56:42,090 --> 02:56:44,160
he'll remain alone in Team Red.

3619
02:56:44,700 --> 02:56:46,860
We need at least one person on the team.

3620
02:56:46,860 --> 02:56:48,470
So I'm moving to Team Blue.

3621
02:56:48,670 --> 02:56:50,400
Then aside from Donkey in Team Red...

3622
02:56:50,400 --> 02:56:52,300
and me in Team Blue,

3623
02:56:52,570 --> 02:56:55,110
everyone has moved to Team White.

3624
02:56:55,610 --> 02:56:57,580
In that situation,

3625
02:56:57,580 --> 02:56:59,280
no matter how much
Team White's leader issues resources,

3626
02:56:59,710 --> 02:57:01,450
its members will receive...

3627
02:57:01,450 --> 02:57:04,010
the equal amount of the prize.

3628
02:57:04,550 --> 02:57:06,920
As long as I give up on taking the prize,

3629
02:57:07,150 --> 02:57:10,290
it'll be a good idea.

3630
02:57:10,290 --> 02:57:13,160
The plan where eight people
divide the prize equally...

3631
02:57:13,160 --> 02:57:14,360
didn't include me.

3632
02:57:14,460 --> 02:57:17,830
Because when I first submitted
the proposal,

3633
02:57:17,830 --> 02:57:20,100
it was distributed to seven people
without me.

3634
02:57:20,460 --> 02:57:22,430
Then when Leia saw that,

3635
02:57:23,100 --> 02:57:25,670
she said it'd be best
to distribute it to eight.

3636
02:57:25,970 --> 02:57:27,640
So it was fixed.

3637
02:57:28,170 --> 02:57:30,010
It'd be nice for me
to take the prize, but...

3638
02:57:30,010 --> 02:57:32,480
(Maillard, Cooking YouTuber)

3639
02:57:59,540 --> 02:58:01,440
I want to bring a definite result...

3640
02:58:01,910 --> 02:58:04,270
for my teammates...

3641
02:58:04,540 --> 02:58:07,080
who trusted me
and participated in my plan.

3642
02:58:10,380 --> 02:58:13,680
I feel bad for them
that I didn't see that coming.

3643
02:58:26,000 --> 02:58:29,170
This is an announcement
from the Community Center.

3644
02:58:29,870 --> 02:58:32,400
According to the final currency vote,

3645
02:58:33,270 --> 02:58:35,170
gold has been selected.

3646
02:58:39,240 --> 02:58:42,380
Here is Luna's final prize.

3647
02:58:42,510 --> 02:58:45,780
(Final prize: 75,000.18 dollars)

3648
02:58:49,890 --> 02:58:53,560
I found the whole situation ridiculous.

3649
02:58:54,060 --> 02:58:57,960
Even though I never planned to
take the prize to myself,

3650
02:58:57,960 --> 02:58:59,200
that's what happened.

3651
02:58:59,330 --> 02:59:01,770
The value of each gold is ridiculous.

3652
02:59:02,170 --> 02:59:06,570
Those ridiculous numbers were
utter nonsense.

3653
02:59:07,470 --> 02:59:09,970
This could've been avoided.

3654
02:59:09,970 --> 02:59:12,610
At first, we were like,
"Let's all survive together."

3655
02:59:12,610 --> 02:59:15,780
"Let's all take the prize home together."

3656
02:59:15,780 --> 02:59:17,650
Then we suddenly declared
unnecessary wars...

3657
02:59:17,650 --> 02:59:21,050
and killed people unnecessarily.

3658
02:59:21,790 --> 02:59:25,320
I felt deflated.

3659
02:59:25,960 --> 02:59:28,230
Despite that,

3660
02:59:29,760 --> 02:59:31,030
I made it.

3661
02:59:33,630 --> 02:59:37,300
All schedule in the Community Town
has come to an end.

3662
02:59:38,500 --> 02:59:39,970
Goodbye.

3663
02:59:52,380 --> 02:59:55,050
The weapon dealer's
final accumulated prize...

3664
02:59:55,050 --> 02:59:59,790
is 24,999.82 dollars.

3665
03:00:00,360 --> 03:00:04,130
The weapon dealer and the ally...

3666
03:00:04,130 --> 03:00:06,030
will split the prize
through the Ultimatum Negotiation.

3667
03:00:07,800 --> 03:00:10,000
The weapon dealer...

3668
03:00:10,000 --> 03:00:12,540
will suggest the ratio of the prize...

3669
03:00:12,540 --> 03:00:13,770
he'll split with the ally.

3670
03:00:15,410 --> 03:00:17,470
If the ally accepts it,

3671
03:00:17,880 --> 03:00:19,940
the prize will be given...

3672
03:00:19,940 --> 03:00:21,880
according to the ratio
the weapon dealer suggested.

3673
03:00:22,250 --> 03:00:24,580
However, if the ally doesn't accept it,

3674
03:00:24,580 --> 03:00:28,990
neither the weapon dealer
or the ally can have the prize.

3675
03:00:29,420 --> 03:00:31,720
Please check the prize...

3676
03:00:31,990 --> 03:00:34,090
and suggest the ratio.

3677
03:00:37,290 --> 03:00:38,660
I'm ready to set the ratio.

3678
03:00:40,360 --> 03:00:43,500
Here is the prize...

3679
03:00:43,500 --> 03:00:45,100
the weapon dealer suggested.

3680
03:00:48,470 --> 03:00:51,140
(He suggested exactly half.)

3681
03:00:54,580 --> 03:00:56,810
If you accept
the weapon dealer's suggestion,

3682
03:00:56,810 --> 03:00:59,350
you will both receive the prize.

3683
03:01:06,460 --> 03:01:10,160
- Twelve thousand...
- The ally agreed to your suggestion.

3684
03:01:10,160 --> 03:01:11,230
Yes!

3685
03:01:14,800 --> 03:01:18,370
You will both receive the prize.

3686
03:01:21,470 --> 03:01:24,910
- I get to take something home.
- All schedule in the Community Town...

3687
03:01:24,910 --> 03:01:26,280
has come to an end.

3688
03:01:27,410 --> 03:01:28,510
Goodbye.

3689
03:01:39,290 --> 03:01:41,230
For example, here's what's possible.

3690
03:01:41,230 --> 03:01:45,460
If you're a leader
and the group split into two,

3691
03:01:45,460 --> 03:01:47,760
there will be a moment...

3692
03:01:47,760 --> 03:01:50,130
when you need to sacrifice
one of your members.

3693
03:01:50,730 --> 03:01:53,570
I'm never going to sacrifice anyone.

3694
03:01:53,570 --> 03:01:56,570
I'll stay with you to the end.

3695
03:01:56,570 --> 03:01:58,480
That is something I can't promise, though.

3696
03:01:58,980 --> 03:02:02,650
Because only then,
this system can keep going.

3697
03:02:02,780 --> 03:02:06,720
I hope I can be seen as...

3698
03:02:06,720 --> 03:02:08,250
one of the believable representations
of humanity.

3699
03:02:08,250 --> 03:02:12,090
It reminded me of dilemma questions
I'd forgotten about.

3700
03:02:12,090 --> 03:02:15,530
In the past,
if I believed I had to be moral...

3701
03:02:15,530 --> 03:02:19,130
and uphold the values one should have
as a decent human being,

3702
03:02:19,130 --> 03:02:21,530
now, I've adapted to reality.

3703
03:02:21,530 --> 03:02:23,200
Because I've experienced it.

3704
03:02:23,500 --> 03:02:25,940
Some of the memorable questions were...

3705
03:02:25,940 --> 03:02:28,170
whether to force an innocent person
to sacrifice...

3706
03:02:28,170 --> 03:02:32,380
in order to avoid multiple sacrifices.

3707
03:02:32,540 --> 03:02:33,540
Something like that.

3708
03:02:33,680 --> 03:02:35,980
The answer I had in my mind was...

3709
03:02:35,980 --> 03:02:39,680
different from the actual choice I'd make
in that situation.

3710
03:02:39,680 --> 03:02:41,920
I was asked to answer questions...

3711
03:02:41,920 --> 03:02:43,390
that I never could have
imagined how I'd answer.

3712
03:02:43,390 --> 03:02:44,620
That was the most memorable part.

3713
03:02:44,890 --> 03:02:47,960
I think political influence is about
persuading people of the value behind it.

3714
03:02:47,960 --> 03:02:49,690
Rather than going, "You need to
recognize me because we were close."

3715
03:02:49,690 --> 03:02:51,160
"It's a matter of loyalty."

3716
03:02:51,160 --> 03:02:53,200
Should I call it important values?

3717
03:02:53,200 --> 03:02:54,400
Or goals?

3718
03:02:54,400 --> 03:02:56,070
There must be a baseline.

3719
03:02:56,570 --> 03:02:59,340
It's up to me to persuade them...

3720
03:02:59,340 --> 03:03:01,440
and agree with me.

3721
03:03:02,440 --> 03:03:05,480
I think people suppress the evil
inside them.

3722
03:03:05,710 --> 03:03:07,280
I do have evil inside.

3723
03:03:07,280 --> 03:03:11,150
Because I have the desire to find out
how evil I can be,

3724
03:03:11,150 --> 03:03:14,050
I'm looking forward to participating
in this show.

3725
03:03:14,580 --> 03:03:15,990
I wonder how evil I can be.

3726
03:03:16,350 --> 03:03:19,020
I hope I'm not someone
that make people go,

3727
03:03:19,020 --> 03:03:22,830
"What is wrong with her?"

3728
03:03:23,090 --> 03:03:26,160
I hope I don't have to torture myself.

3729
03:03:26,700 --> 03:03:27,800
You know what they say.

3730
03:03:28,070 --> 03:03:31,170
If you chase money, you can't make money.

3731
03:03:31,230 --> 03:03:33,640
If you follow your heart,
money will follow you.

3732
03:03:33,640 --> 03:03:36,970
Like the saying goes,
if I win people's hearts,

3733
03:03:36,970 --> 03:03:39,180
I'll survive to the end.

3734
03:03:39,280 --> 03:03:41,380
Being transparent is the best.

3735
03:03:41,380 --> 03:03:44,250
It keeps the organization stable.

3736
03:03:44,250 --> 03:03:47,880
However, domestic companies
don't like to be transparent...

3737
03:03:47,880 --> 03:03:51,890
about their internal situation
to external shareholders.

3738
03:03:51,890 --> 03:03:56,060
That is one of the reasons
the stock prices were low until now.

3739
03:03:56,060 --> 03:03:59,260
Society in general
should be transparent...

3740
03:03:59,260 --> 03:04:01,030
for people to trust one another.

3741
03:04:01,030 --> 03:04:02,770
I believe trust is the force...

3742
03:04:02,770 --> 03:04:06,470
that drives nations
and organizations forward in the end.

3743
03:04:06,800 --> 03:04:08,910
I think transparency is
a very important value.

3744
03:04:08,910 --> 03:04:11,380
This kind of problem occurㄴ...

3745
03:04:11,380 --> 03:04:12,780
because you can't predict
the other person in the game.

3746
03:04:12,780 --> 03:04:15,410
What influences that the most?

3747
03:04:15,410 --> 03:04:17,550
And I think that is reputation.

3748
03:04:17,550 --> 03:04:20,820
If the other person's strength is one,

3749
03:04:20,820 --> 03:04:25,090
ordinary people criticize others
four times more.

3750
03:04:25,090 --> 03:04:26,190
People don't like to
compliment each other.

3751
03:04:26,190 --> 03:04:27,560
It's hard to build up your reputation,

3752
03:04:27,560 --> 03:04:29,930
but it only takes a moment
to bring it down.

3753
03:04:29,930 --> 03:04:33,000
Because everyone likes to gossip.

3754
03:04:33,000 --> 03:04:35,130
If you want to be good at politics
in the end,

3755
03:04:35,130 --> 03:04:36,700
you need to know
what the other person wants...

3756
03:04:36,700 --> 03:04:39,270
and how you can help them.

3757
03:04:39,270 --> 03:04:43,770
You can't help
but understand the other person...

3758
03:04:43,770 --> 03:04:47,240
and think about the situation they're in.

3759
03:04:47,580 --> 03:04:50,850
Rather than surviving,

3760
03:04:52,220 --> 03:04:54,250
I'm here to understand people.

3761
03:04:54,350 --> 03:04:56,220
Games? I normally play...

3762
03:04:56,450 --> 03:04:58,220
games that require cooperation.

3763
03:04:58,220 --> 03:05:00,620
If I lose an individual match,
it's entirely my fault.

3764
03:05:01,220 --> 03:05:03,130
Whereas for a team match,
I can blame others.

3765
03:05:03,130 --> 03:05:04,390
It makes me feel better.

3766
03:05:04,390 --> 03:05:06,160
That helps me stay mentally strong.

3767
03:05:06,460 --> 03:05:08,570
In the end, you play games for fun.

3768
03:05:09,670 --> 03:05:10,700
(The Community 2: Invisible Hand)
